msgid "API reference"
msgstr "API 参考"

msgid ""
"Import each function from its module, as in ``from kivi.woe import woe_table``. "
":doc:`api/conventions` describes the rules that every function follows for its arguments, results"
" and errors, and :doc:`api/glossary` defines the terms of the guides. Each of the other pages "
"documents one module, in the order of the user guide."
msgstr ""
"请从各自所在的模块导入函数，例如 ``from kivi.woe import woe_table`` 。 :doc:`api/conventions` "
"说明所有函数在参数、结果和错误方面共同遵守的规则， :doc:`api/glossary` 给出各篇指南所用术语的定义。其余每一页对应一个模块，按用户指南的顺序排列。"

msgid "Binning"
msgstr "分箱"

msgid ""
"Fit bin edges on a reference sample and group every sample with the same edges. "
":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` fits quantile or uniform edges from the values alone; "
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges`, :func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` and "
":func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` also use a binary target. :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` groups "
"a sample and gives each special code a group of its own."
msgstr ""
"在基准样本上拟合分箱边界，并用同一组边界对每个样本分组。 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 只根据取值拟合等频或等距边界； "
":func:`~kivi.binning.chimerge_edges` 、 :func:`~kivi.binning.tree_edges` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` 还会用到二元目标变量。 :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` 对样本分组，并让每个特殊值单独成组。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/binning` for examples and how to choose the edges."
msgstr "示例以及如何选择边界，见 :doc:`/user_guide/binning` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`bin_edges <kivi.binning.bin_edges>`\\ \\(values\\[\\, bins\\, method\\, special\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`bin_edges <kivi.binning.bin_edges>`\\ \\(values\\[\\, bins\\, method\\, special\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit numeric bin edges on a reference sample."
msgstr "在基准样本上拟合数值变量的分箱边界。"

msgid ":py:obj:`cut <kivi.binning.cut>`\\ \\(values\\, edges\\, \\*\\[\\, special\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`cut <kivi.binning.cut>`\\ \\(values\\, edges\\, \\*\\[\\, special\\]\\)"

msgid "Assign values to bins, with a separate group for each special value."
msgstr "将取值分配到各箱，每个特殊值单独成组。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`chimerge_edges <kivi.binning.chimerge_edges>`\\ \\(values\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`chimerge_edges <kivi.binning.chimerge_edges>`\\ \\(values\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit edges by merging adjacent quantile bins with ChiMerge."
msgstr "用 ChiMerge（卡方分箱）合并相邻的等频箱，拟合分箱边界。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`tree_edges <kivi.binning.tree_edges>`\\ \\(values\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, max\\_bins\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`tree_edges <kivi.binning.tree_edges>`\\ \\(values\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, max\\_bins\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit edges with the splits of a decision tree on one variable."
msgstr "用单变量决策树的切分点拟合分箱边界。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`monotonic_edges <kivi.binning.monotonic_edges>`\\ \\(values\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`monotonic_edges <kivi.binning.monotonic_edges>`\\ \\(values\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit edges by merging adjacent quantile bins until the WOE is monotonic."
msgstr "合并相邻的等频箱，直到 WOE 单调，以此拟合分箱边界。"

msgid ""
"The edges are fitted once and then applied with ``pandas.cut`` to the reference and to every "
"sample compared with it."
msgstr "边界只拟合一次，然后用 ``pandas.cut`` 应用到基准样本以及每个与之比较的样本上。"

msgid "Parameters"
msgstr "参数"

msgid "**values**"
msgstr "**values**"

msgid "array_like"
msgstr "array_like"

msgid ""
"One-dimensional numeric reference values, such as a list, a NumPy array or a pandas Series. "
"Missing values are omitted."
msgstr "一维数值型基准取值，可以是列表、NumPy 数组或 pandas Series。拟合时忽略缺失值。"

msgid "**bins**"
msgstr "**bins**"

msgid "int, default 5"
msgstr "int，默认 5"

msgid "Requested number of bins. Tied quantiles can reduce this number."
msgstr "期望箱数。分位点重合时实际箱数可能减少。"

msgid "**method**"
msgstr "**method**"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{\"quantile\", \"uniform\"}, default \"quantile\""
msgstr "{\"quantile\", \"uniform\"}，默认 \"quantile\""

msgid "Use sample quantiles or equally spaced edges."
msgstr "使用样本分位数或等距边界。"

msgid "**special**"
msgstr "**special**"

msgid "array_like, optional"
msgstr "array_like，可选"

msgid ""
"Special values, such as codes for \"not applicable\", that are omitted when the edges are fitted."
" Pass the same values to `cut` so that each one forms its own group."
msgstr "特殊值，例如表示“不适用”的编码，拟合边界时会被排除。请把同样的值传给 `cut` ，使每个特殊值单独成组。"

msgid "**weights**"
msgstr "**weights**"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each value, for example the inverse of its sampling rate. Values with zero"
" weight are left out. With weights, quantile edges are weighted quantiles by the inverted CDF, so"
" every interior edge is an observed value."
msgstr "每个取值的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数。权重为零的取值会被排除。使用权重时，等频边界取逆累积分布（inverted CDF）意义下的加权分位数，因此每个内部边界都是实际观测到的取值。"

msgid "Returns"
msgstr "返回值"

msgid "numpy.ndarray"
msgstr "numpy.ndarray"

msgid "Increasing edges with infinite endpoints, suitable for pandas.cut."
msgstr "严格递增的边界数组，两端为负无穷和正无穷，可直接传给 pandas.cut。"

msgid "Raises"
msgstr "异常"

msgid "ValueError"
msgstr "ValueError"

msgid ""
"If `bins` is not a positive integer, `method` is not recognized, `values` is not one-dimensional "
"or not numeric, `special` is not one-dimensional or contains a missing value or a boolean, or the"
" reference has no observations or contains an infinite value apart from special values. Also if "
"`weights` is not numeric, does not give each value one finite, non-negative weight with a "
"positive total, or has an index other than that of `values`."
msgstr ""
"如果 `bins` 不是正整数、 `method` 无法识别、 `values` 不是一维或不是数值、 `special` "
"不是一维或含有缺失值或布尔值，或者除特殊值外基准样本没有观测值或含有无穷值。此外，如果 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个取值给出一个有限非负的权重、权重总和不为正，或其索引与 "
"`values` 不同。"

msgid "Warns"
msgstr "警告"

msgid "UserWarning"
msgstr "UserWarning"

msgid ""
"If tied edges leave fewer bins than requested, for example when a single value accounts for a "
"large share of the reference."
msgstr "如果边界重合导致实际箱数少于期望箱数，例如某个取值在基准样本中占比很大。"

msgid ":obj:`cut`"
msgstr ":obj:`cut`"

msgid ":obj:`pandas.cut`"
msgstr ":obj:`pandas.cut`"

msgid "Assign values to the bins defined by the edges."
msgstr "按边界把取值分配到各箱。"

msgid ":obj:`numpy.quantile`"
msgstr ":obj:`numpy.quantile`"

msgid "Compute the quantile edges."
msgstr "计算分位数边界。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.woe.woe_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.woe.woe_table`"

msgid "Weight of evidence of the resulting groups."
msgstr "计算所得分组的证据权重。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.stability.psi_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.stability.psi_table`"

msgid "Stability of the resulting groups."
msgstr "计算所得分组的稳定性。"

msgid "Notes"
msgstr "说明"

msgid ""
"Quantile edges are the sample quantiles at equally spaced probabilities, computed with the "
"default linear interpolation of ``numpy.quantile``. Uniform edges divide the range from the "
"smallest to the largest value into equal widths."
msgstr "分位数边界是在等间距概率处取的样本分位数，使用 ``numpy.quantile`` 默认的线性插值计算。等距边界把从最小值到最大值的区间等分。"

msgid ""
"Repeated edges are merged, and the outer edges are replaced with infinities, so every finite "
"value falls into exactly one interval. The intervals of ``pandas.cut`` are closed on the right."
msgstr "重复的边界会被合并，最外侧的两个边界替换为无穷，因此每个有限值都恰好落入一个区间。 ``pandas.cut`` 的区间为左开右闭。"

msgid "Examples"
msgstr "示例"

msgid "A special value is left out of the fit:"
msgstr "特殊值不参与拟合："

msgid "Without `special` the result is the same as ``pandas.cut(values, edges)``."
msgstr "不传 `special` 时，结果与 ``pandas.cut(values, edges)`` 相同。"

msgid "One-dimensional numeric values to assign. Missing values stay missing."
msgstr "待分箱的一维数值。缺失值保持缺失。"

msgid "**edges**"
msgstr "**edges**"

msgid "Increasing bin edges, usually from `bin_edges`."
msgstr "递增的分箱边界，通常来自 `bin_edges` 。"

msgid ""
"Special values that each form their own group instead of falling into an interval. Use the values"
" passed to `bin_edges`."
msgstr "每个特殊值单独成组，不落入任何区间。请使用传给 `bin_edges` 的同一组值。"

msgid "pandas.Series or pandas.Categorical"
msgstr "pandas.Series 或 pandas.Categorical"

msgid ""
"Categorical groups whose categories are the special values, in the order given, followed by the "
"intervals. A Series input gives a Series with the same index and name."
msgstr "分类型的分组结果，类别依次为按给定顺序排列的特殊值和各区间。输入为 Series 时返回 Series，索引和名称保持不变。"

msgid ""
"If `values` is not one-dimensional or is not numeric apart from special values, `edges` does not "
"increase, or `special` is not one-dimensional or contains a missing value or a boolean."
msgstr "如果 `values` 不是一维或除特殊值外不是数值、 `edges` 不是递增的，或者 `special` 不是一维或含有缺失值或布尔值。"

msgid ":obj:`bin_edges`"
msgstr ":obj:`bin_edges`"

msgid "Fit the edges on a reference sample."
msgstr "在基准样本上拟合边界。"

msgid "Assign values to intervals only."
msgstr "只把取值分配到区间。"

msgid ""
"A special value is matched by equality, so ``-1`` and ``-1.0`` are the same code. Values that are"
" not numbers, such as strings read from a file, are also matched after conversion with "
"``pandas.to_numeric``, so the string ``\"-1\"`` falls into the group of the code ``-1``. Values "
"outside the edges become missing, as with ``pandas.cut``; the infinite outer edges of `bin_edges`"
" avoid this."
msgstr ""
"特殊值按相等关系匹配，因此 ``-1`` 和 ``-1.0`` 视为同一个编码。不是数字的值（例如从文件读入的字符串）还会在经 ``pandas.to_numeric`` "
"转换后再匹配一次，因此字符串 ``\"-1\"`` 会落入编码 ``-1`` 的分组。与 ``pandas.cut`` 一样，超出边界的值会变为缺失； `bin_edges` "
"两端的无穷边界可以避免这种情况。"

msgid ""
"The values are first cut into ``initial_bins`` quantile bins, or into one bin per distinct value "
"if there are no more distinct values than that. The adjacent pair with the smallest chi-square "
"statistic, the pair whose event rates are most alike, is then merged, and merging is repeated "
"while more than ``max_bins`` bins remain or while some adjacent pair is not significantly "
"different at level ``alpha``."
msgstr ""
"先将数值切成 ``initial_bins`` 个等频箱；若不同取值的个数不超过该数，则每个取值单独成一箱。随后合并卡方统计量最小、即事件率最接近的一对相邻箱。只要箱数仍多于 "
"``max_bins``，或仍有相邻两箱在显著性水平 ``alpha`` 下差异不显著，就继续合并。"

msgid ""
"One-dimensional numeric values, such as a list, a NumPy array or a pandas Series. Missing values "
"and their labels are omitted."
msgstr "一维数值，可以是列表、NumPy 数组或 pandas Series。缺失值及其标签会被忽略。"

msgid "**target**"
msgstr "**target**"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event. If `values` and `target` are both pandas Series, they"
" must have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by position."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件。如果 `values` 和 `target` 都是 pandas Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid "**max_bins**"
msgstr "**max_bins**"

msgid "Maximum number of bins."
msgstr "最大箱数。"

msgid "**alpha**"
msgstr "**alpha**"

msgid "float or None, default 0.05"
msgstr "float 或 None，默认 0.05"

msgid ""
"Significance level of the chi-square test with one degree of freedom. Adjacent bins are merged "
"until every pair differs at this level. Pass None to merge down to ``max_bins`` only."
msgstr "自由度为 1 的卡方检验的显著性水平。相邻箱会一直合并，直到每一对在该水平下都差异显著。传入 None 时只合并到 ``max_bins`` 个箱。"

msgid "**initial_bins**"
msgstr "**initial_bins**"

msgid "int, default 20"
msgstr "int，默认 20"

msgid "Number of quantile bins to start from. Tied quantiles can reduce it."
msgstr "起始的等频箱数。分位点重合时实际箱数可能减少。"

msgid ""
"Special values, such as codes for \"not applicable\", that are omitted with their labels when the"
" edges are fitted. Pass the same values to `cut` so that each one forms its own group."
msgstr "特殊值，例如表示“不适用”的编码；拟合边界时，这些值连同其标签一起被排除。请把同样的值传给 `cut` ，使每个特殊值单独成组。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, for example the inverse of its sampling rate, matched "
"like `target`. Observations with zero weight are left out, and the counts in each bin are sums of"
" weights. The initial quantile bins then use weighted quantiles by the inverted CDF, so unit "
"weights can give other edges than no weights when there are more distinct values than "
"`initial_bins`. The chi-square test treats the weighted counts as counts, so scale the weights to"
" sum to the sample size when the p-values matter."
msgstr ""
"每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` "
"相同。权重为零的观测会被排除，每箱的计数为权重之和。此时初始的等频细分箱也使用逆累积分布意义下的加权分位数，因此当不同取值的个数多于 `initial_bins` 时，权重全为 1 "
"与不传权重得到的边界可能不同。卡方检验把加权计数当作计数处理，因此在需要参考 p 值时，请把权重缩放到总和等于样本量。"

msgid ""
"If `max_bins` or `initial_bins` is not a positive integer, `alpha` is neither None nor between 0 "
"and 1, `values` and `target` are not one-dimensional or their indices or lengths do not match, "
"`special` is not one-dimensional or contains a missing value or a boolean, `values` is not "
"numeric or has no finite observations apart from missing and special values, or `target` has "
"labels other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of them in the rows that are fitted. Also if `weights` is "
"not numeric, does not give each value one finite, non-negative weight with a positive total, or "
"has an index other than that of `values`."
msgstr ""
"`max_bins` 或 `initial_bins` 不是正整数，`alpha` 既不是 None 也不在 0 与 1 之间，`values` 与 `target` "
"不是一维、索引或长度不一致，`special` 不是一维或含有缺失值或布尔值，`values` 不是数值或除缺失值和特殊值外没有有限观测值，或者 `target` 含有 0 和 1 "
"以外的标签、在参与拟合的行中缺少其中一类，都会引发此异常。此外，如果 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个取值给出一个有限非负的权重、权重总和不为正，或其索引与 `values` 不同。"

msgid ":obj:`tree_edges`"
msgstr ":obj:`tree_edges`"

msgid "Split the values recursively instead of merging."
msgstr "递归切分数值，而不是合并。"

msgid ":obj:`monotonic_edges`"
msgstr ":obj:`monotonic_edges`"

msgid "Merge until the WOE is monotonic."
msgstr "合并到 WOE 单调为止。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For an adjacent pair of bins with observed counts :math:`O_{ij}` (bin :math:`i`, class :math:`j`)"
" and expected counts :math:`E_{ij} = R_i C_j / N` under equal event rates,"
msgstr ""
"对相邻的两个箱，记观测计数为 :math:`O_{ij}` （箱 :math:`i`，类别 :math:`j`），事件率相同假设下的期望计数为 :math:`E_{ij} = R_i C_j /"
" N`，则"

msgid "\\chi^2 = \\sum_{i=1}^{2} \\sum_{j=0}^{1} \\frac{(O_{ij} - E_{ij})^2}{E_{ij}}"
msgstr "\\chi^2 = \\sum_{i=1}^{2} \\sum_{j=0}^{1} \\frac{(O_{ij} - E_{ij})^2}{E_{ij}}"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where cells with :math:`E_{ij} = 0` contribute nothing. A pair stays separate when the p-value of"
" :math:`\\chi^2` is below ``alpha``."
msgstr "其中 :math:`E_{ij} = 0` 的单元格不计入。当 :math:`\\chi^2` 的 p 值小于 ``alpha`` 时，这两个箱保持分开。"

msgid ""
"The tree grows best first: of all current bins, the one whose best split most reduces the total "
"impurity is split next, until there are ``max_bins`` bins or no split reduces the impurity while "
"leaving at least ``min_bin_share`` of the observations on each side."
msgstr ""
"决策树按最优优先的顺序生长：在当前所有箱中，最优切分能让总不纯度下降最多的箱先被切分，直到箱数达到 ``max_bins``，或者在两侧都保留至少 ``min_bin_share`` "
"观测的前提下，已没有能降低不纯度的切分。"

msgid "Maximum number of bins, the leaves of the tree."
msgstr "最大箱数，即决策树的叶节点数。"

msgid "**min_bin_share**"
msgstr "**min_bin_share**"

msgid "float, default 0.05"
msgstr "float，默认 0.05"

msgid ""
"Minimum share of the fitted values in every bin, from 0 to 0.5, or of their total weight when "
"`weights` is given. Missing and special values do not count towards it."
msgstr "每个箱至少包含的拟合取值占比，取值范围为 0 到 0.5；传入 `weights` 时按权重总和计算。缺失值和特殊值不计入。"

msgid "**criterion**"
msgstr "**criterion**"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{\"entropy\", \"gini\"}, default \"entropy\""
msgstr "{\"entropy\", \"gini\"}，默认 \"entropy\""

msgid "Impurity measure: entropy for information gain, or the Gini index."
msgstr "不纯度指标：熵（即信息增益）或基尼指数。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, for example the inverse of its sampling rate, matched "
"like `target`. Observations with zero weight are left out, and the counts in each bin are sums of"
" weights."
msgstr "每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` 相同。权重为零的观测会被排除，每箱的计数为权重之和。"

msgid ""
"Increasing edges with infinite endpoints, suitable for pandas.cut. Every interior edge is an "
"observed value, the largest one in the bin to its left."
msgstr "严格递增的边界数组，两端为负无穷和正无穷，可直接传给 pandas.cut。每个内部边界都是一个观测值，即其左侧箱中的最大值。"

msgid ""
"If `max_bins` is not a positive integer, `min_bin_share` is not between 0 and 0.5, `criterion` is"
" not recognized, `values` and `target` are not one-dimensional or their indices or lengths do not"
" match, `special` is not one-dimensional or contains a missing value or a boolean, `values` is "
"not numeric or has no finite observations apart from missing and special values, or `target` has "
"labels other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of them in the rows that are fitted. Also if `weights` is "
"not numeric, does not give each value one finite, non-negative weight with a positive total, or "
"has an index other than that of `values`."
msgstr ""
"`max_bins` 不是正整数，`min_bin_share` 不在 0 与 0.5 之间，`criterion` 无法识别，`values` 与 `target` "
"不是一维、索引或长度不一致，`special` 不是一维或含有缺失值或布尔值，`values` 不是数值或除缺失值和特殊值外没有有限观测值，或者 `target` 含有 0 和 1 "
"以外的标签、在参与拟合的行中缺少其中一类，都会引发此异常。此外，如果 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个取值给出一个有限非负的权重、权重总和不为正，或其索引与 `values` 不同。"

msgid ":obj:`chimerge_edges`"
msgstr ":obj:`chimerge_edges`"

msgid "Merge fine bins instead of splitting."
msgstr "合并细分箱，而不是切分。"

msgid ""
"For a bin with :math:`n` observations (their total weight, with `weights`) and event rate "
":math:`p`, the impurity is :math:`H(p) = -p \\ln p - (1 - p) \\ln(1 - p)` (entropy) or "
":math:`G(p) = 2p(1 - p)` (Gini). A split into :math:`n_L` and :math:`n_R` observations reduces "
"the total impurity by :math:`n H(p) - n_L H(p_L) - n_R H(p_R)`, and the largest reduction over "
"all bins and cut points is chosen."
msgstr ""
"对含 :math:`n` 个观测（传入 `weights` 时为其权重总和）、事件率为 :math:`p` 的箱，不纯度为 :math:`H(p) = -p \\ln p - (1 - p) "
"\\ln(1 - p)` （熵）或 :math:`G(p) = 2p(1 - p)` （基尼指数）。把它切成 :math:`n_L` 和 :math:`n_R` 个观测的两部分，总不纯度下降 "
":math:`n H(p) - n_L H(p_L) - n_R H(p_R)`；在所有箱和切分点中选择下降最多的一个。"

msgid ""
"The values are first cut into ``initial_bins`` quantile bins, or into one bin per distinct value "
"if there are no more distinct values than that. While two adjacent bins break the trend, the "
"first such pair is merged and the WOE is recomputed (pool adjacent violators), so the WOE of the "
"final bins is strictly increasing or strictly decreasing. While more than ``max_bins`` bins "
"remain, the adjacent pair with the smallest chi-square statistic is merged as in "
":func:`chimerge_edges`, and the trend is checked again."
msgstr ""
"先将数值切成 ``initial_bins`` 个等频箱；若不同取值的个数不超过该数，则每个取值单独成一箱。只要有相邻两箱违背趋势，就合并第一对这样的箱并重新计算 "
"WOE（合并相邻违序者，pool adjacent violators），因此最终各箱的 WOE 严格递增或严格递减。若箱数仍多于 ``max_bins``，则像 "
":func:`chimerge_edges` 一样合并卡方统计量最小的相邻两箱，再重新检查趋势。"

msgid "int or None, default 5"
msgstr "int 或 None，默认 5"

msgid "Maximum number of bins. Pass None to stop as soon as the WOE is monotonic."
msgstr "最大箱数。传入 None 时，WOE 一旦单调即停止合并。"

msgid "**direction**"
msgstr "**direction**"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{\"auto\", \"increasing\", \"decreasing\"}, default \"auto\""
msgstr "{\"auto\", \"increasing\", \"decreasing\"}，默认 \"auto\""

msgid ""
"Trend of the WOE as the values grow. ``\"auto\"`` fits both directions and keeps the one with the"
" larger information value, preferring ``\"increasing\"`` on a tie."
msgstr "随数值增大时 WOE 的趋势。``\"auto\"`` 会两个方向都拟合，保留信息值较大的一个；两者相等时取 ``\"increasing\"``。"

msgid "**smoothing**"
msgstr "**smoothing**"

msgid "float, default 0.5"
msgstr "float，默认 0.5"

msgid ""
"Positive replacement for a zero count when calculating the WOE, as in :func:`kivi.woe.woe_table`."
" Use the same value there to see the same trend."
msgstr "计算 WOE 时用这个正数替代零计数，含义与 :func:`kivi.woe.woe_table` 相同。在那里使用同一取值，才能看到同样的趋势。"

msgid ""
"Special values, such as codes for \"not applicable\", that are omitted with their labels when the"
" edges are fitted. Pass the same values to `cut` so that each one forms its own group. The trend "
"applies to the intervals only; a special group can have any WOE."
msgstr "特殊值，例如表示“不适用”的编码；拟合边界时，这些值连同其标签一起被排除。请把同样的值传给 `cut` ，使每个特殊值单独成组。单调趋势只约束各区间，特殊值组的 WOE 不受限制。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, for example the inverse of its sampling rate, matched "
"like `target`. Observations with zero weight are left out, and the counts in each bin are sums of"
" weights. The initial quantile bins then use weighted quantiles by the inverted CDF, so unit "
"weights can give other edges than no weights when there are more distinct values than "
"`initial_bins`. `smoothing` is then in units of weight."
msgstr ""
"每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` "
"相同。权重为零的观测会被排除，每箱的计数为权重之和。此时初始的等频细分箱也使用逆累积分布意义下的加权分位数，因此当不同取值的个数多于 `initial_bins` 时，权重全为 1 "
"与不传权重得到的边界可能不同。此时 `smoothing` 以权重为单位。"

msgid ""
"If `max_bins` is neither None nor a positive integer, `initial_bins` is not a positive integer, "
"`direction` is not recognized, `smoothing` is not finite and positive, `values` and `target` are "
"not one-dimensional or their indices or lengths do not match, `special` is not one-dimensional or"
" contains a missing value or a boolean, `values` is not numeric or has no finite observations "
"apart from missing and special values, or `target` has labels other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of "
"them in the rows that are fitted. Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each value one "
"finite, non-negative weight with a positive total, or has an index other than that of `values`."
msgstr ""
"`max_bins` 既不是 None 也不是正整数，`initial_bins` 不是正整数，`direction` 无法识别，`smoothing` 不是有限正数，`values` 与 "
"`target` 不是一维、索引或长度不一致，`special` 不是一维或含有缺失值或布尔值，`values` 不是数值或除缺失值和特殊值外没有有限观测值，或者 `target` 含有 0 和"
" 1 以外的标签、在参与拟合的行中缺少其中一类，都会引发此异常。此外，如果 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个取值给出一个有限非负的权重、权重总和不为正，或其索引与 `values` "
"不同。"

msgid "Merge fine bins by a chi-square test."
msgstr "按卡方检验合并细分箱。"

msgid "Split the values recursively."
msgstr "递归切分数值。"

msgid "Calibration"
msgstr "校准"

msgid ""
"Check and correct predicted probabilities. :func:`~kivi.calibration.prior_correction` and "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.corrected_intercept` correct them for the sampling of the development "
"data, :func:`~kivi.calibration.master_scale`, :func:`~kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd` and "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` build a master scale and assign its grades, "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` and the tests count and test the grades, and "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` and :func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` recalibrate a "
"score."
msgstr ""
"检查并校正预测概率。 :func:`~kivi.calibration.prior_correction` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.corrected_intercept` 按开发数据的抽样方式校正概率， "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.master_scale` 、 :func:`~kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` 构建主标尺并分配等级， :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` "
"和各项检验统计并检验各等级， :func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` 和 :func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` "
"重新校准评分。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/calibration` for examples on the bundled data."
msgstr "基于内置数据的示例见 :doc:`/user_guide/calibration` 。"

msgid ":py:obj:`prior_correction <kivi.calibration.prior_correction>`\\ \\(probability\\, \\*\\, ...\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`prior_correction <kivi.calibration.prior_correction>`\\ \\(probability\\, \\*\\, ...\\)"

msgid "Correct event probabilities for a development sample with another event rate."
msgstr "当开发样本的事件率与总体不同时，校正事件概率。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`corrected_intercept <kivi.calibration.corrected_intercept>`\\ \\(intercept\\, \\*\\, "
"...\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`corrected_intercept <kivi.calibration.corrected_intercept>`\\ \\(intercept\\, \\*\\, "
"...\\)"

msgid "Correct a logistic intercept for a development sample with another event rate."
msgstr "当开发样本的事件率与总体不同时，校正逻辑回归的截距。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`calibration_table <kivi.calibration.calibration_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, target\\, "
"probability\\, \\*\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`calibration_table <kivi.calibration.calibration_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, target\\, "
"probability\\, \\*\\)"

msgid "Compare the predicted and observed event rates of each group."
msgstr "比较每组的预测事件率与实际观测事件率。"

msgid ":py:obj:`binomial_test <kivi.calibration.binomial_test>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, probability\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`binomial_test <kivi.calibration.binomial_test>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, probability\\)"

msgid "Test whether each grade has more events than its probability predicts."
msgstr "检验每个等级的事件数是否多于其概率所预测的数量。"

msgid ":py:obj:`jeffreys_test <kivi.calibration.jeffreys_test>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, probability\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`jeffreys_test <kivi.calibration.jeffreys_test>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, probability\\)"

msgid "Test each grade's probability against its event rate with the Jeffreys prior."
msgstr "基于 Jeffreys 先验，检验每个等级的概率是否与其事件率相符。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`hosmer_lemeshow <kivi.calibration.hosmer_lemeshow>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, "
"probability\\, \\*\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`hosmer_lemeshow <kivi.calibration.hosmer_lemeshow>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, "
"probability\\, \\*\\)"

msgid "Test the calibration of all groups at once with the Hosmer-Lemeshow statistic."
msgstr "用 Hosmer-Lemeshow 统计量一次检验所有分组的校准情况。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`herfindahl_index <kivi.calibration.herfindahl_index>`\\ \\(counts\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"normalize\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`herfindahl_index <kivi.calibration.herfindahl_index>`\\ \\(counts\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"normalize\\]\\)"

msgid "Measure how concentrated a portfolio is across grades."
msgstr "衡量资产组合在各等级间的集中程度。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`master_scale <kivi.calibration.master_scale>`\\ \\(probability\\, \\*\\[\\, boundary\\, "
"labels\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`master_scale <kivi.calibration.master_scale>`\\ \\(probability\\, \\*\\[\\, boundary\\, "
"labels\\]\\)"

msgid "Build a master scale from the PD of each grade."
msgstr "根据每个等级的 PD 构建主标尺。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`fit_grade_pd <kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"smoothing\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`fit_grade_pd <kivi.calibration.fit_grade_pd>`\\ \\(event\\, total\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"smoothing\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit the PD of each grade to observed default rates, log-linear in the grade."
msgstr "按观测违约率拟合每个等级的 PD，其对数与等级呈线性关系。"

msgid ":py:obj:`assign_grades <kivi.calibration.assign_grades>`\\ \\(probability\\, scale\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`assign_grades <kivi.calibration.assign_grades>`\\ \\(probability\\, scale\\)"

msgid "Give each predicted PD the grade of a master scale."
msgstr "为每个预测 PD 指定主标尺上的等级。"

msgid ":py:obj:`platt_fit <kivi.calibration.platt_fit>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`platt_fit <kivi.calibration.platt_fit>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit Platt scaling, a logistic curve from a score to event probabilities."
msgstr "拟合 Platt 缩放，即从评分到事件概率的逻辑曲线。"

msgid ":py:obj:`platt_predict <kivi.calibration.platt_predict>`\\ \\(score\\, slope\\, intercept\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`platt_predict <kivi.calibration.platt_predict>`\\ \\(score\\, slope\\, intercept\\)"

msgid "Turn scores into event probabilities with a fitted Platt scaling."
msgstr "用拟合好的 Platt 缩放把评分转换为事件概率。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`isotonic_fit <kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"weights\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`isotonic_fit <kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"weights\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit an isotonic calibration, a step function from a score to event probabilities."
msgstr "拟合保序校准，即从评分到事件概率的阶梯函数。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`isotonic_predict <kivi.calibration.isotonic_predict>`\\ \\(score\\, edges\\, "
"probabilities\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`isotonic_predict <kivi.calibration.isotonic_predict>`\\ \\(score\\, edges\\, "
"probabilities\\)"

msgid "Give each score the probability of its band from an isotonic calibration."
msgstr "按保序校准，给每个评分赋予其所在分段的概率。"

msgid ""
"A model developed on a sample that over- or undersamples events predicts probabilities for that "
"sample. The correction rescales the odds so the probabilities refer to the population."
msgstr "如果开发样本对事件做了过采样或欠采样，模型预测的是该样本上的概率。本函数按比例调整几率，使概率对应总体。"

msgid "**probability**"
msgstr "**probability**"

msgid "Event probabilities from the model, between 0 and 1. Missing values stay missing."
msgstr "模型给出的事件概率，取值在 0 与 1 之间。缺失值保持缺失。"

msgid "**sample_rate**"
msgstr "**sample_rate**"

msgid "float"
msgstr "float"

msgid "Event rate of the development sample, strictly between 0 and 1."
msgstr "开发样本的事件率，严格介于 0 与 1 之间。"

msgid "**population_rate**"
msgstr "**population_rate**"

msgid "Event rate of the population, strictly between 0 and 1."
msgstr "总体的事件率，严格介于 0 与 1 之间。"

msgid "float, pandas.Series or numpy.ndarray"
msgstr "float、pandas.Series 或 numpy.ndarray"

msgid ""
"Corrected probabilities with the shape of `probability`. A Series input gives a Series with the "
"same index and name, and a scalar gives a float."
msgstr "校正后的概率，形状与 `probability` 相同。输入为 Series 时返回 Series，索引和名称保持不变；输入为标量时返回 float。"

msgid "If `probability` has values outside [0, 1], or a rate is not strictly between 0 and 1."
msgstr "如果 `probability` 含有 [0, 1] 以外的值，或者某个事件率不严格介于 0 与 1 之间。"

msgid ":obj:`corrected_intercept`"
msgstr ":obj:`corrected_intercept`"

msgid "Apply the same correction to a logistic intercept."
msgstr "对逻辑回归截距做同样的校正。"

msgid ":obj:`calibration_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`calibration_table`"

msgid "Compare predicted and observed event rates."
msgstr "比较预测事件率与观测事件率。"

msgid ""
"With sample event rate :math:`\\bar y` and population event rate :math:`\\tau`, the odds of every"
" probability are multiplied by"
msgstr "设样本事件率为 :math:`\\bar y` ，总体事件率为 :math:`\\tau` ，则每个概率的几率都乘以"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\omega = \\frac{\\tau / (1 - \\tau)}{\\bar y / (1 - \\bar y)}, \\qquad\n"
"\\tilde p = \\frac{\\omega p}{\\omega p + 1 - p}."
msgstr ""
"\\omega = \\frac{\\tau / (1 - \\tau)}{\\bar y / (1 - \\bar y)}, \\qquad\n"
"\\tilde p = \\frac{\\omega p}{\\omega p + 1 - p}."

msgid ""
"This is the prior correction of King and Zeng [R4b74edbba56e-1]_. It changes the level of the "
"probabilities but not their order. For a logistic regression it equals adding :math:`\\ln "
"\\omega` to the intercept."
msgstr ""
"这是 King 和 Zeng [R4b74edbba56e-1]_ 提出的先验校正（prior correction）。它改变概率的水平，但不改变其排序。对逻辑回归而言，这等价于在截距上加上 "
":math:`\\ln \\omega` 。"

msgid "References"
msgstr "参考文献"

msgid ""
"G. King and L. Zeng, \"Logistic Regression in Rare Events Data\", Political Analysis, vol. 9, no."
" 2, pp. 137-163, 2001."
msgstr ""
"G. King and L. Zeng, \"Logistic Regression in Rare Events Data\", Political Analysis, vol. 9, no."
" 2, pp. 137-163, 2001."

msgid "[R4b74edbba56e-1]_"
msgstr "[R4b74edbba56e-1]_"

msgid ""
"The corrected model gives the probabilities of `prior_correction`: only the intercept changes, so"
" the coefficients and the order of applicants stay as they are."
msgstr "校正后的模型给出与 `prior_correction` 相同的概率：只有截距改变，系数和申请人的排序都保持不变。"

msgid "**intercept**"
msgstr "**intercept**"

msgid "Intercept of a logistic regression of the event."
msgstr "以事件为因变量的逻辑回归的截距。"

msgid "The intercept for the population, ``intercept + ln(omega)``."
msgstr "适用于总体的截距，即 ``intercept + ln(omega)`` 。"

msgid "If `intercept` is not a finite number, or a rate is not strictly between 0 and 1."
msgstr "如果 `intercept` 不是有限数值，或者某个事件率不严格介于 0 与 1 之间。"

msgid ":obj:`prior_correction`"
msgstr ":obj:`prior_correction`"

msgid "Apply the correction to probabilities."
msgstr "对概率做同样的校正。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"King and Zeng [Rc67660983562-1]_ subtract :math:`\\ln\\left[\\frac{1 - \\tau}{\\tau} \\cdot "
"\\frac{\\bar y}{1 - \\bar y}\\right] = -\\ln \\omega` from the intercept; see `prior_correction`."
msgstr ""
"King 和 Zeng [Rc67660983562-1]_ 从截距中减去 :math:`\\ln\\left[\\frac{1 - \\tau}{\\tau} \\cdot "
"\\frac{\\bar y}{1 - \\bar y}\\right] = -\\ln \\omega` ；参见 `prior_correction` 。"

msgid "[Rc67660983562-1]_"
msgstr "[Rc67660983562-1]_"

msgid ""
"The groups are typically the grades of a master scale, formed by cutting the probabilities at "
"fixed edges, or score bands. Each row has the inputs of the calibration tests."
msgstr "分组通常是主标尺的等级（按固定边界切分概率得到），或者分数段。每一行都包含校准检验所需的输入。"

msgid "**groups**"
msgstr "**groups**"

msgid "Grade or group labels. Missing values form a group."
msgstr "等级或分组标签。缺失值独立成组。"

msgid "Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event. A group, or the whole sample, may have no events."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件。某个分组乃至整个样本都可以没有事件。"

msgid ""
"Predicted event probabilities between 0 and 1. Series inputs must have identical indices; "
"otherwise the inputs are matched by position."
msgstr "预测的事件概率，取值在 0 与 1 之间。作为 Series 传入的输入，索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, such as the inverse of its sampling rate, matched like "
"`target`. ``total`` and ``event`` are then sums of weights, the rate and the mean probability are"
" weighted, and groups whose weights sum to zero are left out."
msgstr "每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` 相同。此时 ``total`` 和 ``event`` 为权重之和，事件率和平均概率都按权重计算，权重之和为零的组会被排除。"

msgid "pandas.DataFrame"
msgstr "pandas.DataFrame"

msgid ""
"One row per group with the number of observations ``total``, the number of events ``event``, the "
"observed ``event_rate`` and the mean predicted probability ``mean_probability``."
msgstr "每组一行，包括观测数 ``total`` 、事件数 ``event`` 、观测事件率 ``event_rate`` 以及平均预测概率 ``mean_probability`` 。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are not one-dimensional, are empty, or their indices or lengths do not match, "
"`target` has labels other than 0 and 1, or `probability` has missing values or values outside [0,"
" 1]. Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one finite, non-negative "
"weight with a positive total, or has an index other than that of `groups`."
msgstr ""
"如果输入不是一维、为空，或者索引或长度不一致， `target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签，或者 `probability` 含有缺失值或 [0, 1] 以外的值。此外，如果 "
"`weights` 不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负且总和为正的权重，或者索引与 `groups` 不同。"

msgid ":obj:`binomial_test`"
msgstr ":obj:`binomial_test`"

msgid "Test whether a grade has more events than predicted."
msgstr "检验某个等级的事件数是否多于预测。"

msgid ":obj:`jeffreys_test`"
msgstr ":obj:`jeffreys_test`"

msgid "The Bayesian counterpart of the binomial test."
msgstr "二项检验的贝叶斯版本。"

msgid ":obj:`hosmer_lemeshow`"
msgstr ":obj:`hosmer_lemeshow`"

msgid "Test the calibration of all groups at once."
msgstr "一次检验所有分组的校准情况。"

msgid ":obj:`herfindahl_index`"
msgstr ":obj:`herfindahl_index`"

msgid "Measure how concentrated the grades are."
msgstr "衡量各等级的集中程度。"

msgid ""
"Groups are counted as in `kivi.woe.woe_table`. Rows follow the order of the categories when "
"`groups` is categorical, such as the result of ``pandas.cut``, with missing values last. "
"Otherwise they follow the order in which the groups first appear. Categories that are never "
"observed are omitted."
msgstr ""
"分组的计数方式与 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 相同。当 `groups` 为分类型（例如 ``pandas.cut`` "
"的结果）时，各行按类别顺序排列，缺失值排在最后。否则按分组首次出现的次序排列。从未出现的类别不会列出。"

msgid ""
"The binomial, Jeffreys and Hosmer-Lemeshow tests need whole numbers of observations and events, "
"so run them on an unweighted table."
msgstr "二项检验、Jeffreys 检验和 Hosmer-Lemeshow 检验需要整数的观测数和事件数，因此请在不加权的表上进行这些检验。"

msgid ""
"The one-sided exact binomial test assumes independent events. A small p-value means that the "
"probability underestimates the event rate of the grade."
msgstr "单侧精确二项检验假定各事件相互独立。p 值较小，说明该概率低估了这个等级的事件率。"

msgid "**event**"
msgstr "**event**"

msgid "Number of events in each grade."
msgstr "每个等级的事件数。"

msgid "**total**"
msgstr "**total**"

msgid "Number of observations in each grade, a positive whole number."
msgstr "每个等级的观测数，为正整数。"

msgid ""
"Predicted event probability of each grade, between 0 and 1, such as the ``mean_probability`` "
"column of `calibration_table`. The three inputs are broadcast together; Series inputs must have "
"identical indices."
msgstr ""
"每个等级的预测事件概率，取值在 0 与 1 之间，例如 `calibration_table` 的 ``mean_probability`` 列。三个输入会一起广播；作为 Series "
"传入的输入，索引必须完全相同。"

msgid ""
"One-sided p-values: a Series with the index of the Series inputs, a float for scalar inputs and "
"an array otherwise."
msgstr "单侧 p 值：有 Series 输入时返回 Series，索引与 Series 输入相同；输入为标量时返回 float；其他情况返回数组。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs cannot be broadcast or their Series indices differ, `total` is not a positive whole"
" number, `event` is not a whole number between 0 and `total`, or `probability` is outside [0, 1]."
msgstr "如果输入无法广播或 Series 的索引不一致、 `total` 不是正整数、 `event` 不是介于 0 与 `total` 之间的整数，或者 `probability` 超出 [0, 1]。"

msgid "The Bayesian counterpart of this test."
msgstr "本检验的贝叶斯版本。"

msgid "The counts and predicted probabilities of each grade."
msgstr "每个等级的计数和预测概率。"

msgid ""
"Under the null hypothesis the number of events :math:`D` among :math:`N` observations follows a "
"binomial distribution with probability :math:`p`. The p-value is"
msgstr "在原假设下， :math:`N` 个观测中的事件数 :math:`D` 服从概率为 :math:`p` 的二项分布。p 值为"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"P(D \\ge d) = \\sum_{k=d}^{N} \\binom{N}{k} p^k (1 - p)^{N - k}\n"
"= I_p(d, N - d + 1),"
msgstr ""
"P(D \\ge d) = \\sum_{k=d}^{N} \\binom{N}{k} p^k (1 - p)^{N - k}\n"
"= I_p(d, N - d + 1),"

msgid ""
"with the regularized incomplete beta function :math:`I`, and 1 when :math:`d = 0`. Correlated "
"defaults, as in an economic downturn, make the test reject more often than its nominal level "
"[Rb734fd528b30-1]_."
msgstr ""
"其中 :math:`I` 为正则化不完全贝塔函数；当 :math:`d = 0` 时 p 值为 1。违约之间存在相关性时（例如经济下行期），该检验的拒绝频率会高于名义水平 "
"[Rb734fd528b30-1]_ 。"

msgid ""
"Basel Committee on Banking Supervision, \"Studies on the Validation of Internal Rating Systems\","
" Working Paper No. 14, 2005."
msgstr ""
"Basel Committee on Banking Supervision, \"Studies on the Validation of Internal Rating Systems\","
" Working Paper No. 14, 2005."

msgid "[Rb734fd528b30-1]_"
msgstr "[Rb734fd528b30-1]_"

msgid ""
"The p-value is the posterior probability that the true event rate is at most the predicted "
"probability. A small p-value means that the probability underestimates the event rate of the "
"grade."
msgstr "p 值是真实事件率不超过预测概率的后验概率。p 值较小，说明该概率低估了这个等级的事件率。"

msgid "The frequentist counterpart of this test."
msgstr "本检验的频率学派版本。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"With the Jeffreys prior Beta(1/2, 1/2), the posterior of the event rate after :math:`d` events "
"among :math:`N` observations is :math:`\\mathrm{Beta}(d + 1/2, N - d + 1/2)`, and the p-value is "
"its distribution function at the predicted probability :math:`p`:"
msgstr ""
"取 Jeffreys 先验 Beta(1/2, 1/2)，在 :math:`N` 个观测中出现 :math:`d` 个事件后，事件率的后验分布为 :math:`\\mathrm{Beta}(d "
"+ 1/2, N - d + 1/2)` ，p 值就是该分布在预测概率 :math:`p` 处的分布函数值："

msgid "I_p\\left(d + \\tfrac12, N - d + \\tfrac12\\right)."
msgstr "I_p\\left(d + \\tfrac12, N - d + \\tfrac12\\right)."

msgid ""
"This is the test that the European Central Bank asks for in the validation of PD models "
"[R73613bff641b-1]_. Unlike the binomial test, a grade without events still has a p-value below 1."
msgstr "这是欧洲央行在 PD 模型验证中要求使用的检验 [R73613bff641b-1]_ 。与二项检验不同，没有事件的等级其 p 值仍小于 1。"

msgid ""
"European Central Bank, \"Instructions for reporting the validation results of internal models: "
"IRB Pillar I models for credit risk\", 2019."
msgstr ""
"European Central Bank, \"Instructions for reporting the validation results of internal models: "
"IRB Pillar I models for credit risk\", 2019."

msgid "[R73613bff641b-1]_"
msgstr "[R73613bff641b-1]_"

msgid ""
"The statistic adds up the squared differences between observed and predicted events of each "
"group. A small p-value means that the probabilities do not match the observed event rates."
msgstr "该统计量把各组观测事件数与预测事件数之差的平方累加起来。p 值较小，说明概率与观测到的事件率不符。"

msgid "Number of events in each group."
msgstr "每组的事件数。"

msgid "Number of observations in each group, a positive whole number."
msgstr "每组的观测数，为正整数。"

msgid ""
"Mean predicted event probability of each group, strictly between 0 and 1, such as the "
"``mean_probability`` column of `calibration_table`. Series inputs must have identical indices."
msgstr ""
"每组的平均预测事件概率，严格介于 0 与 1 之间，例如 `calibration_table` 的 ``mean_probability`` 列。作为 Series "
"传入的输入，索引必须完全相同。"

msgid "**ddof**"
msgstr "**ddof**"

msgid "int, default 2"
msgstr "int，默认 2"

msgid "The chi-square distribution has as many degrees of freedom as there are groups, minus `ddof`."
msgstr "卡方分布的自由度等于分组数减去 `ddof` 。"

msgid "**statistic**"
msgstr "**statistic**"

msgid "The Hosmer-Lemeshow statistic."
msgstr "Hosmer-Lemeshow 统计量。"

msgid "**pvalue**"
msgstr "**pvalue**"

msgid "Its upper tail probability under the chi-square distribution."
msgstr "该统计量在卡方分布下的上尾概率。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are not one-dimensional, have different lengths or Series indices, `total` is not a"
" positive whole number, `event` is not a whole number between 0 and `total`, `probability` is not"
" strictly between 0 and 1, or `ddof` is negative or leaves no degree of freedom."
msgstr ""
"如果输入不是一维、长度或 Series 索引不一致、 `total` 不是正整数、 `event` 不是介于 0 与 `total` 之间的整数、 `probability` 不严格介于 0 与"
" 1 之间，或者 `ddof` 为负数或使自由度不足 1。"

msgid "The counts and predicted probabilities of each group."
msgstr "每组的计数和预测概率。"

msgid "Test each grade on its own."
msgstr "逐个检验每个等级。"

msgid ""
"For :math:`g` groups with :math:`d_k` events among :math:`n_k` observations and mean predicted "
"probability :math:`\\bar p_k`,"
msgstr "对 :math:`g` 个分组，设第 :math:`k` 组有 :math:`n_k` 个观测、 :math:`d_k` 个事件，平均预测概率为 :math:`\\bar p_k` ，则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "H = \\sum_{k=1}^{g} \\frac{(d_k - n_k \\bar p_k)^2}{n_k \\bar p_k (1 - \\bar p_k)},"
msgstr "H = \\sum_{k=1}^{g} \\frac{(d_k - n_k \\bar p_k)^2}{n_k \\bar p_k (1 - \\bar p_k)},"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"compared with a chi-square distribution with :math:`g - \\mathrm{ddof}` degrees of freedom. "
"Hosmer and Lemeshow [Rde8a0df3097b-1]_ form about ten groups of similar size from the sorted "
"probabilities of the sample the model was fitted on, which gives :math:`g - 2`. For probabilities"
" that were not fitted on the tested sample, such as a validation sample, use ``ddof=0`` "
"[Rde8a0df3097b-2]_."
msgstr ""
"并与自由度为 :math:`g - \\mathrm{ddof}` 的卡方分布比较。Hosmer 和 Lemeshow [Rde8a0df3097b-1]_ "
"将拟合模型所用样本的概率排序后分成约十个大小相近的组，此时自由度为 :math:`g - 2` 。如果概率不是在被检验的样本上拟合的（例如验证样本），请使用 ``ddof=0`` "
"[Rde8a0df3097b-2]_ 。"

msgid ""
"D. W. Hosmer and S. Lemeshow, \"Goodness of fit tests for the multiple logistic regression "
"model\", Communications in Statistics - Theory and Methods, vol. 9, no. 10, pp. 1043-1069, 1980."
msgstr ""
"D. W. Hosmer and S. Lemeshow, \"Goodness of fit tests for the multiple logistic regression "
"model\", Communications in Statistics - Theory and Methods, vol. 9, no. 10, pp. 1043-1069, 1980."

msgid ""
"D. W. Hosmer, S. Lemeshow and R. X. Sturdivant, \"Applied Logistic Regression\", 3rd ed., Wiley, "
"2013."
msgstr ""
"D. W. Hosmer, S. Lemeshow and R. X. Sturdivant, \"Applied Logistic Regression\", 3rd ed., Wiley, "
"2013."

msgid "[Rde8a0df3097b-1]_, [Rde8a0df3097b-2]_"
msgstr "[Rde8a0df3097b-1]_, [Rde8a0df3097b-2]_"

msgid ""
"The Herfindahl-Hirschman index is the sum of the squared shares of the grades. It is 1 when every"
" observation is in one grade and :math:`1/k` when :math:`k` grades are equally full."
msgstr "赫芬达尔-赫希曼指数（HHI）是各等级占比的平方和。所有观测都在同一等级时为 1； :math:`k` 个等级人数相同时为 :math:`1/k` 。"

msgid "**counts**"
msgstr "**counts**"

msgid ""
"Number of observations, or exposure, in each grade, such as the ``total`` column of "
"`calibration_table`."
msgstr "每个等级的观测数或敞口，例如 `calibration_table` 的 ``total`` 列。"

msgid "**normalize**"
msgstr "**normalize**"

msgid "bool, default False"
msgstr "bool，默认 False"

msgid "Rescale the index to run from 0 for equally full grades to 1 for a single full grade."
msgstr "重新缩放指数，使各等级人数相同时为 0，全部集中在一个等级时为 1。"

msgid "The index."
msgstr "指数值。"

msgid ""
"If `counts` is not one-dimensional, has negative or non-finite values or sums to zero, or "
"`normalize` is not a boolean or is set with fewer than two grades."
msgstr "如果 `counts` 不是一维、含有负值或非有限值、总和为零，或者 `normalize` 不是布尔值，或在少于两个等级时设置了 `normalize` 。"

msgid "The number of observations in each grade."
msgstr "每个等级的观测数。"

msgid "For grade shares :math:`s_i = c_i / \\sum_j c_j` of :math:`k` grades,"
msgstr "对 :math:`k` 个等级，设各等级占比为 :math:`s_i = c_i / \\sum_j c_j` ，则"

msgid ""
"\\mathrm{HHI} = \\sum_{i=1}^{k} s_i^2, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{HHI}^* = \\frac{\\mathrm{HHI} - 1/k}{1 - 1/k}."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{HHI} = \\sum_{i=1}^{k} s_i^2, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{HHI}^* = \\frac{\\mathrm{HHI} - 1/k}{1 - 1/k}."

msgid ""
"A rating scale whose observations crowd into a few grades differentiates risk poorly. Empty "
"grades count towards :math:`k`."
msgstr "如果观测集中在少数几个等级，评级标尺对风险的区分能力就较差。空等级也计入 :math:`k` 。"

msgid ""
"A master scale divides the PD range from 0 to 1 into grades, each with one PD. The bounds between"
" adjacent grades lie between their PDs, so that `assign_grades` can give every predicted PD its "
"grade."
msgstr "主标尺把从 0 到 1 的 PD 范围划分为若干等级，每个等级有一个 PD。相邻等级之间的界限位于两者的 PD 之间，因此 `assign_grades` 能为每个预测 PD 指定其等级。"

msgid ""
"PD of each grade, strictly increasing from the grade with the lowest risk and strictly between 0 "
"and 1. ``numpy.geomspace(first, last, grades)`` gives a geometric grid, and `fit_grade_pd` fits "
"the PDs to observed default rates."
msgstr ""
"每个等级的 PD，从风险最低的等级起严格递增，且严格介于 0 和 1 之间。 ``numpy.geomspace(first, last, grades)`` 给出几何网格， "
"`fit_grade_pd` 则按观测违约率拟合这些 PD。"

msgid "**boundary**"
msgstr "**boundary**"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{\"geometric\", \"arithmetic\"}, default \"geometric\""
msgstr "{\"geometric\", \"arithmetic\"}，默认 \"geometric\""

msgid ""
"Bound between two adjacent grades: the geometric mean of their PDs, the midpoint on a logarithmic"
" scale, or their arithmetic mean."
msgstr "相邻两个等级之间的界限：取两者 PD 的几何平均数，即对数尺度上的中点，或取其算术平均数。"

msgid "**labels**"
msgstr "**labels**"

msgid ""
"Unique label of each grade, such as ``list(\"ABCDEFG\")``. By default the grades are numbered "
"from 1."
msgstr "每个等级唯一的标签，例如 ``list(\"ABCDEFG\")`` 。默认从 1 开始为等级编号。"

msgid ""
"One row per grade, indexed by its label in an index named ``grade``, with the columns ``lower``, "
"``probability`` and ``upper``. The first grade starts at 0, the last one ends at 1, and each "
"grade ends where the next one starts."
msgstr ""
"每个等级一行，以其标签为索引（索引名为 ``grade`` ），包含 ``lower`` 、 ``probability`` 和 ``upper`` 三列。第一个等级从 0 开始，最后一个等级在"
" 1 结束，每个等级在下一个等级开始处结束。"

msgid ""
"If `probability` is empty, not one-dimensional or not real and numeric, has a missing value, is "
"not strictly increasing or is not strictly between 0 and 1, `boundary` is not recognized, or "
"`labels` does not give one unique, non-missing label per grade."
msgstr ""
"如果 `probability` 为空、不是一维、不是实数数值、含有缺失值、不严格递增或不严格介于 0 和 1 之间， `boundary` 无法识别，或 `labels` "
"没有为每个等级给出一个唯一且非缺失的标签。"

msgid ":obj:`fit_grade_pd`"
msgstr ":obj:`fit_grade_pd`"

msgid "Fit the PD of each grade to observed default rates."
msgstr "按观测违约率拟合每个等级的 PD。"

msgid ":obj:`assign_grades`"
msgstr ":obj:`assign_grades`"

msgid "Give each predicted PD the grade of the scale."
msgstr "为每个预测 PD 指定标尺上的等级。"

msgid "Compare the grades with their observed default rates."
msgstr "比较各等级与其观测违约率。"

msgid ""
"For the PDs :math:`p_1 < \\dots < p_K` of the grades, the bound between grades :math:`k` and "
":math:`k + 1` is"
msgstr "设各等级的 PD 为 :math:`p_1 < \\dots < p_K` ，等级 :math:`k` 与 :math:`k + 1` 之间的界限为"

msgid ""
"b_k = \\sqrt{p_k \\, p_{k+1}} \\quad \\text{(geometric)}, \\qquad\n"
"b_k = \\frac{p_k + p_{k+1}}{2} \\quad \\text{(arithmetic)},"
msgstr ""
"b_k = \\sqrt{p_k \\, p_{k+1}} \\quad \\text{(geometric)}, \\qquad\n"
"b_k = \\frac{p_k + p_{k+1}}{2} \\quad \\text{(arithmetic)},"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"and grade :math:`k` holds the PDs in :math:`(b_{k-1}, b_k]`, with :math:`b_0 = 0` and :math:`b_K "
"= 1`. PDs of a master scale usually grow by a constant factor from grade to grade, so they are "
"evenly spaced on a logarithmic scale. The geometric bound is the midpoint on that scale: a PD "
"goes to the grade whose PD is nearer by ratio. The arithmetic mean, which the 0.2 versions of "
"kivi used, always lies above the geometric one, so each grade reaches further towards the grade "
"above it than towards the grade below. With PDs that double from grade to grade, a grade with PD "
":math:`p` then holds the PDs up to :math:`1.5 p` instead of :math:`\\sqrt 2 p \\approx 1.41 p`, "
"and its observed default rate tends to exceed its PD."
msgstr ""
"等级 :math:`k` 包含 :math:`(b_{k-1}, b_k]` 中的 PD，其中 :math:`b_0 = 0` ， :math:`b_K = 1` 。主标尺的 PD "
"通常逐级按固定倍数增长，因此在对数尺度上等距分布。几何界限正是该尺度上的中点：PD 归入按比值更接近的那个等级。kivi 0.2 "
"版本使用的算术平均数总是高于几何平均数，因此每个等级向上一个等级延伸得比向下一个等级更远。若 PD 逐级翻倍，PD 为 :math:`p` 的等级将包含直到 :math:`1.5 p` 的 "
"PD，而不是 :math:`\\sqrt 2 p \\approx 1.41 p` ，其观测违约率往往高于其 PD。"

msgid "The arithmetic mean of adjacent PDs gives higher bounds:"
msgstr "相邻 PD 的算术平均数给出更高的界限："

msgid ""
"The logarithm of the default rate is fitted as a straight line in the grade number, so the fitted"
" PDs grow by a constant factor from grade to grade. Pass the result to `master_scale` for the "
"bounds of the grades."
msgstr "把违约率的对数拟合为等级编号的直线，因此拟合的 PD 逐级按固定倍数增长。把结果传给 `master_scale` 即可得到各等级的界限。"

msgid ""
"Number of defaults in each grade, ordered from the grade with the lowest risk to the grade with "
"the highest. Weighted counts, such as those of a weighted `calibration_table`, are accepted."
msgstr "每个等级的违约数，从风险最低的等级排到风险最高的等级。也接受加权计数，例如加权 `calibration_table` 中的计数。"

msgid ""
"Number of observations in each grade. A grade without observations is left out of the fit but "
"still gets a fitted PD, so pass a 0 for every grade of the scale that the data do not cover. "
"Series inputs must have identical indices."
msgstr "每个等级的观测数。没有观测的等级不参与拟合，但仍会得到拟合的 PD，因此对数据未覆盖的每个标尺等级都传入 0。Series 输入必须具有相同的索引。"

msgid ""
"Number of defaults that replaces a count of zero, whose logarithm is undefined, as "
"`kivi.woe.woe_table` replaces an empty cell."
msgstr "替换零计数（其对数无定义）的违约数，与 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 替换空单元格的方式相同。"

msgid "pandas.Series or numpy.ndarray"
msgstr "pandas.Series 或 numpy.ndarray"

msgid ""
"Fitted PD of each grade, strictly increasing and below 1: a Series with the index of the Series "
"inputs, an array otherwise."
msgstr "每个等级拟合的 PD，严格递增且小于 1：有 Series 输入时返回 Series，索引与 Series 输入相同；否则返回数组。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are not one-dimensional, have different lengths or Series indices, are not finite "
"and non-negative, or `event` exceeds `total`; if fewer than two grades have observations or "
"`smoothing` is not finite and positive. Also if the fitted PDs do not rise with the grade or "
"reach 1."
msgstr ""
"如果输入不是一维、长度或 Series 索引不同、不是有限的非负数，或 `event` 超过 `total` ；如果有观测的等级少于两个，或 `smoothing` "
"不是有限的正数。此外，如果拟合的 PD 不随等级上升或达到 1，也会抛出。"

msgid ":obj:`master_scale`"
msgstr ":obj:`master_scale`"

msgid "Build the scale from the fitted PDs."
msgstr "用拟合的 PD 构建标尺。"

msgid "Count the observations and defaults of each grade."
msgstr "统计每个等级的观测数和违约数。"

msgid ""
"With :math:`d_k` defaults among :math:`n_k` observations in grade :math:`k = 1, \\dots, K`, the "
"intercept :math:`a` and the slope :math:`b` minimize the weighted sum of squares"
msgstr ""
"设等级 :math:`k = 1, \\dots, K` 的 :math:`n_k` 个观测中有 :math:`d_k` 次违约，截距 :math:`a` 和斜率 :math:`b` "
"使如下加权平方和最小"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\sum_{k : n_k > 0} n_k \\left(\\ln \\frac{d_k}{n_k} - a - b k\\right)^2,"
msgstr "\\sum_{k : n_k > 0} n_k \\left(\\ln \\frac{d_k}{n_k} - a - b k\\right)^2,"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"where :math:`d_k` is replaced by `smoothing` when it is 0. The fitted PD of grade :math:`k` is "
":math:`e^{a + b k}`, and consecutive PDs have the constant ratio :math:`e^b`. The weights give "
"each observation the same influence, so integer counts weigh like repeated observations; the 0.2 "
"versions of kivi fitted the line by ordinary least squares, giving each grade the same influence "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"其中 :math:`d_k` 为 0 时用 `smoothing` 代替。等级 :math:`k` 的拟合 PD 为 :math:`e^{a + b k}` ，相邻 PD 之比恒为 "
":math:`e^b` 。这种权重让每个观测具有相同的影响，因此整数计数的权重与重复的观测相同；kivi 0.2 版本用普通最小二乘拟合这条直线，让每个等级具有相同的影响。"

msgid ""
"The fit extrapolates beyond the observed grades, so grades at the edges of the scale can get PDs "
"no observation supports. A default rate of zero says only that the grade is safe, not how safe: "
"the smoothed rate :math:`0.5 / n_k` stands in for it."
msgstr "拟合会外推到观测到的等级之外，因此标尺两端的等级可能得到没有任何观测支持的 PD。违约率为零只说明该等级安全，而不说明有多安全：用平滑后的违约率 :math:`0.5 / n_k` 代替它。"

msgid ""
"The grades are an ordered categorical of the labels of the scale, so `calibration_table` counts "
"them directly, in the order of the scale, for the tests of each grade."
msgstr "等级是标尺标签的有序分类变量，因此 `calibration_table` 可以直接按标尺的顺序统计各等级，供逐个等级的检验使用。"

msgid "One-dimensional predicted PDs between 0 and 1. Missing values stay missing."
msgstr "一维的预测 PD，介于 0 和 1 之间。缺失值保持缺失。"

msgid "**scale**"
msgstr "**scale**"

msgid ""
"Master scale, as returned by `master_scale`: one row per grade, indexed by unique labels, with "
"the columns ``lower`` and ``upper``. The first grade must start at 0, each grade where the one "
"before it ends, and the last one must end at 1."
msgstr ""
"主标尺，即 `master_scale` 的返回值：每个等级一行，以唯一的标签为索引，包含 ``lower`` 和 ``upper`` 两列。第一个等级必须从 0 "
"开始，每个等级从上一个等级结束处开始，最后一个等级必须在 1 结束。"

msgid ""
"Grade of each PD, an ordered categorical whose categories are the labels of the scale from the "
"lowest risk to the highest. A Series input gives a Series with the same index and name."
msgstr "每个 PD 的等级，为有序分类变量，其类别是标尺的标签，从风险最低到最高排列。输入为 Series 时返回 Series，索引和名称保持不变。"

msgid ""
"If `probability` is not one-dimensional, is not real and numeric, or has values outside [0, 1], "
"or `scale` is not a DataFrame with unique, non-missing labels and ``lower`` and ``upper`` columns"
" that cover [0, 1] with increasing, adjacent grades."
msgstr ""
"如果 `probability` 不是一维、不是实数数值或有取值超出 [0, 1]，或者 `scale` 不是这样的 DataFrame：具有唯一且非缺失的标签，其 ``lower`` 和 "
"``upper`` 列用递增且首尾相接的等级覆盖 [0, 1]。"

msgid "Build the scale."
msgstr "构建标尺。"

msgid "Compare the observed and predicted default rates of each grade."
msgstr "比较每个等级的观测违约率与预测违约率。"

msgid "Assign values to intervals given by their edges."
msgstr "按边界把取值分配到各区间。"

msgid ""
"Grade :math:`k` holds the PDs above its ``lower`` bound up to and including its ``upper`` bound, "
"as the intervals of ``pandas.cut`` are closed on the right, and a PD of 0 belongs to the first "
"grade, as with ``include_lowest=True``. The result equals ``pandas.cut(probability, edges, "
"labels=scale.index, include_lowest=True)`` for the edges ``[0, *scale[\"upper\"]]``; the "
"``upper`` column, not the PDs, decides the grade. The 0.2 versions of kivi gave a PD on a bound "
"the grade above it instead."
msgstr ""
"等级 :math:`k` 包含高于其 ``lower`` 界限、直到并包括其 ``upper`` 界限的 PD，因为 ``pandas.cut`` 的区间是左开右闭的；PD 为 0 "
"时属于第一个等级，与 ``include_lowest=True`` 相同。结果等于以 ``[0, *scale[\"upper\"]]`` 为边界的 "
"``pandas.cut(probability, edges, labels=scale.index, include_lowest=True)`` ；决定等级的是 ``upper`` "
"列，而不是各等级的 PD。kivi 0.2 版本则把恰好落在界限上的 PD 归入上面的等级。"

msgid ""
"The slope and intercept are fitted once, on a development or calibration sample, and "
"`platt_predict` applies them to the scores of any sample."
msgstr "斜率和截距只需在开发样本或校准样本上拟合一次，再由 `platt_predict` 应用到任何样本的评分上。"

msgid "**score**"
msgstr "**score**"

msgid ""
"Finite numeric scores, such as the log odds of a model, a PD or scorecard points. The direction "
"does not matter: a score that falls as the risk rises gets a negative slope."
msgstr "有限的数值评分，例如模型的对数几率、PD 或评分卡分值。方向无关紧要：风险越高评分越低时，斜率为负。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event. Both classes must be present. If `score` and `target`"
" are both pandas Series, they must have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by "
"position."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件。两个类别都必须出现。如果 `score` 和 `target` 都是 pandas Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative frequency weight of each observation, matched like `target`: a weight of 2 counts an"
" observation twice."
msgstr "每个观测的非负频数权重，对应方式与 `target` 相同：权重为 2 的观测计为两次。"

msgid "**slope**"
msgstr "**slope**"

msgid "Coefficient of the score in the log odds of the event."
msgstr "评分在事件对数几率中的系数。"

msgid "Log odds of the event at a score of 0."
msgstr "评分为 0 时事件的对数几率。"

msgid "kivi.selection.SeparationError"
msgstr "kivi.selection.SeparationError"

msgid ""
"If the score separates the classes, so that the slope that maximizes the likelihood is infinite. "
"It is a ValueError."
msgstr "如果评分把两类完全分开，以致使似然最大的斜率为无穷大。该异常属于 ValueError。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` "
"has a label other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of them, `score` is not real and numeric, has a "
"missing or infinite value or does not vary, or `weights` is invalid or leaves a class without "
"weight."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，索引或长度不一致，`target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签或缺少其中之一，`score` 不是实数数值、含有缺失值或无穷值或者没有变化，或者 `weights` "
"无效或使某一类没有权重。"

msgid "RuntimeWarning"
msgstr "RuntimeWarning"

msgid "If the fit does not converge."
msgstr "如果拟合未能收敛。"

msgid ":obj:`platt_predict`"
msgstr ":obj:`platt_predict`"

msgid "Apply the slope and intercept to scores."
msgstr "把斜率和截距应用到评分上。"

msgid ":obj:`isotonic_fit`"
msgstr ":obj:`isotonic_fit`"

msgid "A calibration that only assumes that the rate rises."
msgstr "只假定事件率随评分上升的校准。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.selection.logistic_regression`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.selection.logistic_regression`"

msgid "The same kind of fit with standard errors."
msgstr "同类拟合，并给出标准误。"

msgid "The event probability at score :math:`s` is modelled as"
msgstr "评分为 :math:`s` 时的事件概率建模为"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "p(s) = \\frac{1}{1 + \\exp(-(a s + b))},"
msgstr "p(s) = \\frac{1}{1 + \\exp(-(a s + b))},"

msgid ""
"and the slope :math:`a` and the intercept :math:`b` maximize the log-likelihood, fitted by "
"iteratively reweighted least squares as in `kivi.selection.logistic_regression`. At the maximum, "
"the mean fitted probability equals the event rate of the sample, weighted with `weights`."
msgstr ""
"其中斜率 :math:`a` 和截距 :math:`b` 使对数似然最大，与 `kivi.selection.logistic_regression` "
"一样用迭代重加权最小二乘法拟合。在最大值处，拟合概率的均值等于样本的事件率（按 `weights` 加权）。"

msgid ""
"When the score is the log odds of a model, this is the logistic recalibration of Cox "
"[Rd112ce059dd4-2]_: a slope of 1 and an intercept of 0 mean that the model is calibrated on the "
"sample, and a slope below 1 that its probabilities are too extreme, as after overfitting."
msgstr ""
"当评分是某个模型的对数几率时，这就是 Cox 的逻辑再校准 [Rd112ce059dd4-2]_ ：斜率为 1、截距为 0 说明模型在该样本上是校准的；斜率小于 1 "
"则说明其概率过于极端，例如过拟合之后。"

msgid ""
"Platt [Rd112ce059dd4-1]_, and scikit-learn's ``CalibratedClassifierCV`` after him, replace the "
"labels 1 and 0 with :math:`(n_1 + 1) / (n_1 + 2)` and :math:`1 / (n_0 + 2)` for :math:`n_1` "
"events and :math:`n_0` non-events. This matters only in small samples, where it also keeps the "
"slope finite when the score separates the classes. Here the labels are used as they are, so a "
"separating score raises an error instead; `isotonic_fit` handles such a score."
msgstr ""
"Platt [Rd112ce059dd4-1]_ 以及沿用其做法的 scikit-learn ``CalibratedClassifierCV`` ，在有 :math:`n_1` 个事件和 "
":math:`n_0` 个非事件时，把标签 1 和 0 替换为 :math:`(n_1 + 1) / (n_1 + 2)` 和 :math:`1 / (n_0 + 2)` "
"。这只在小样本中有影响，在评分把两类完全分开时还能让斜率保持有限。这里直接使用原始标签，因此完全分开两类的评分会引发错误；这种评分可以改用 `isotonic_fit` 处理。"

msgid ""
"J. C. Platt, \"Probabilistic outputs for support vector machines and comparisons to regularized "
"likelihood methods\", in Advances in Large Margin Classifiers, MIT Press, pp. 61-74, 1999."
msgstr ""
"J. C. Platt, \"Probabilistic outputs for support vector machines and comparisons to regularized "
"likelihood methods\", in Advances in Large Margin Classifiers, MIT Press, pp. 61-74, 1999."

msgid ""
"D. R. Cox, \"Two further applications of a model for binary regression\", Biometrika, 45(3-4), "
"pp. 562-565, 1958."
msgstr ""
"D. R. Cox, \"Two further applications of a model for binary regression\", Biometrika, 45(3-4), "
"pp. 562-565, 1958."

msgid "[Rd112ce059dd4-1]_, [Rd112ce059dd4-2]_"
msgstr "[Rd112ce059dd4-1]_, [Rd112ce059dd4-2]_"

msgid ""
"The probabilities follow the logistic curve with the slope and intercept from `platt_fit`, so the"
" same calibration applies to the development sample, a validation sample and new applicants."
msgstr "概率沿着由 `platt_fit` 得到的斜率和截距所确定的逻辑曲线，因此开发样本、验证样本和新申请人都使用同一个校准。"

msgid "Numeric scores on the scale of the fit. Missing values give missing probabilities."
msgstr "与拟合时尺度相同的数值评分。缺失值对应的概率也为缺失。"

msgid "Coefficient of the score, as returned by `platt_fit`."
msgstr "评分的系数，即 `platt_fit` 的返回值。"

msgid "Intercept, as returned by `platt_fit`."
msgstr "截距，即 `platt_fit` 的返回值。"

msgid ""
"Event probabilities with the shape of `score`. A Series input gives a Series with the same index "
"and name, and a scalar gives a float."
msgstr "事件概率，形状与 `score` 相同。输入为 Series 时返回 Series，索引和名称保持不变；输入为标量时返回 float。"

msgid "If `score` is not real and numeric, or `slope` or `intercept` is not a finite number."
msgstr "如果 `score` 不是实数数值，或者 `slope` 或 `intercept` 不是有限数。"

msgid ":obj:`platt_fit`"
msgstr ":obj:`platt_fit`"

msgid "Fit the slope and intercept."
msgstr "拟合斜率和截距。"

msgid ":obj:`isotonic_predict`"
msgstr ":obj:`isotonic_predict`"

msgid "Apply an isotonic calibration."
msgstr "应用保序校准。"

msgid ""
"The probability is :math:`1 / (1 + \\exp(-(a s + b)))` for slope :math:`a`, intercept :math:`b` "
"and score :math:`s`, computed without overflow for extreme scores."
msgstr "对斜率 :math:`a` 、截距 :math:`b` 和评分 :math:`s` ，概率为 :math:`1 / (1 + \\exp(-(a s + b)))` ，对极端评分也不会溢出。"

msgid ""
"The score range is split into bands whose event rates rise with the score, so the calibration "
"assumes only that a higher score means a higher risk. Fit the bands once and apply them to the "
"scores of any sample with `isotonic_predict`."
msgstr "把评分范围划分为若干分段，各段的事件率随评分上升，因此这种校准只假定评分越高风险越高。分段只需拟合一次，再用 `isotonic_predict` 应用到任何样本的评分上。"

msgid "Finite numeric scores, such as a PD or the log odds of a model."
msgstr "有限的数值评分，例如 PD 或模型的对数几率。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative frequency weight of each observation, matched like `target`: a weight of 2 counts an"
" observation twice. Scores whose weights sum to zero are ignored."
msgstr "每个观测的非负频数权重，对应方式与 `target` 相同：权重为 2 的观测计为两次。权重之和为零的评分会被忽略。"

msgid "**increasing**"
msgstr "**increasing**"

msgid "bool, default True"
msgstr "bool，默认 True"

msgid ""
"Whether the probability rises with the score, as for a PD. Pass False for scorecard points, which"
" are higher for a lower risk."
msgstr "概率是否随评分上升，PD 就是如此。评分卡分值越高表示风险越低，因此对其传入 False。"

msgid ""
"Increasing band edges from ``-inf`` to ``inf``, like those of `kivi.binning.bin_edges`. The bands"
" are closed on the right, as in ``pandas.cut``, and each interior edge is the highest score of "
"the band below it."
msgstr ""
"从 ``-inf`` 到 ``inf`` 递增的分段边界，与 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` 的结果形式相同。各分段与 ``pandas.cut`` "
"一样为右闭区间，每个内部边界是其下方分段中的最高评分。"

msgid "**probabilities**"
msgstr "**probabilities**"

msgid ""
"Event rate of each band, one fewer than `edges`. The rates are strictly increasing, or strictly "
"decreasing with ``increasing=False``."
msgstr "每个分段的事件率，个数比 `edges` 少一个。事件率严格递增；若 ``increasing=False`` ，则严格递减。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` "
"has a label other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of them, `score` is not real and numeric or has a "
"missing or infinite value, `weights` is invalid or leaves a class without weight, or `increasing`"
" is not a boolean."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，索引或长度不一致，`target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签或缺少其中之一，`score` 不是实数数值或含有缺失值、无穷值，`weights` "
"无效或使某一类没有权重，或者 `increasing` 不是布尔值。"

msgid "Apply the bands to scores."
msgstr "把分段应用到评分上。"

msgid "A calibration by a logistic curve."
msgstr "用逻辑曲线进行的校准。"

msgid "Compare the bands with the outcomes of another sample."
msgstr "将分段与另一个样本的实际结果进行比较。"

msgid ""
"Among all probabilities :math:`p_i` that rise with the score, isotonic regression minimizes "
":math:`\\sum_i w_i (y_i - p_i)^2`, and the same solution maximizes the binomial likelihood "
"[R79aaa79b7808-1]_. The pool-adjacent-violators algorithm finds it: each distinct score starts as"
" a band with its event rate, and adjacent bands are merged while the lower one has a rate at "
"least as high as the one above it. The probability of a band is then its pooled event rate. Tied "
"scores always share a band, and since bands with equal rates are merged too, no two adjacent "
"bands have the same probability."
msgstr ""
"在所有随评分上升的概率 :math:`p_i` 中，保序回归使 :math:`\\sum_i w_i (y_i - p_i)^2` 最小，同一个解也使二项似然最大 "
"[R79aaa79b7808-1]_ 。相邻违序合并算法（pool-adjacent-"
"violators）可以求出这个解：每个不同的评分起初各成一段，取其事件率；只要较低一段的事件率不低于其上方一段，就把这两段合并。每段的概率就是合并后的事件率。相同的评分总在同一段中；由于事件率相等的相邻分段也会合并，任意两个相邻分段的概率都不相同。"

msgid ""
"The outer edges are infinite, so a score below or above the fitted range gets the probability of "
"the lowest or highest band. A score between the observed scores of two bands falls into the upper"
" one, whose interval it belongs to; with ``increasing=False``, that is the band with the lower "
"risk. scikit-learn's ``IsotonicRegression`` interpolates linearly between the bands instead; both"
" give the same probability at every score of the fitted sample [R79aaa79b7808-2]_."
msgstr ""
"两端边界为无穷，因此低于或高于拟合范围的评分分别取最低或最高分段的概率。落在两个分段的观测评分之间的评分属于上方的分段，因为它在该段的区间内；若 ``increasing=False`` "
"，这就是风险较低的分段。scikit-learn 的 ``IsotonicRegression`` 则在分段之间线性插值；在拟合样本的每个评分上，两者给出的概率相同 "
"[R79aaa79b7808-2]_ 。"

msgid ""
"A band without events has probability 0 and a band with only events has probability 1; a score "
"that separates the classes gives just these two bands. Floor the probabilities where 0 is not "
"allowed, for example before `kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score`. The bands can also serve as the grades "
"of `calibration_table`, by cutting the scores at `edges`."
msgstr ""
"没有事件的分段概率为 0，只有事件的分段概率为 1；把两类完全分开的评分只会得到这两个分段。在不允许概率为 0 的场合（例如调用 `kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score` "
"之前），请为概率设定下限。按 `edges` 切分评分后，这些分段也可以作为 `calibration_table` 的等级。"

msgid ""
"M. Ayer, H. D. Brunk, G. M. Ewing, W. T. Reid and E. Silverman, \"An empirical distribution "
"function for sampling with incomplete information\", The Annals of Mathematical Statistics, "
"26(4), pp. 641-647, 1955."
msgstr ""
"M. Ayer, H. D. Brunk, G. M. Ewing, W. T. Reid and E. Silverman, \"An empirical distribution "
"function for sampling with incomplete information\", The Annals of Mathematical Statistics, "
"26(4), pp. 641-647, 1955."

msgid ""
"B. Zadrozny and C. Elkan, \"Transforming classifier scores into accurate multiclass probability "
"estimates\", Proceedings of the 8th ACM SIGKDD Conference, pp. 694-699, 2002."
msgstr ""
"B. Zadrozny and C. Elkan, \"Transforming classifier scores into accurate multiclass probability "
"estimates\", Proceedings of the 8th ACM SIGKDD Conference, pp. 694-699, 2002."

msgid "[R79aaa79b7808-1]_, [R79aaa79b7808-2]_"
msgstr "[R79aaa79b7808-1]_, [R79aaa79b7808-2]_"

msgid ""
"The bands come from `isotonic_fit` on a development or calibration sample, so the same step "
"function applies to every later sample."
msgstr "分段由 `isotonic_fit` 在开发样本或校准样本上得到，因此之后的每个样本都使用同一个阶梯函数。"

msgid "Increasing band edges from ``-inf`` to ``inf``, as returned by `isotonic_fit`."
msgstr "从 ``-inf`` 到 ``inf`` 递增的分段边界，即 `isotonic_fit` 的返回值。"

msgid "Probability of each band, between 0 and 1, one fewer than `edges`."
msgstr "每个分段的概率，介于 0 和 1 之间，个数比 `edges` 少一个。"

msgid ""
"If `score` is not real and numeric, `edges` is not increasing from ``-inf`` to ``inf``, or "
"`probabilities` does not give one value between 0 and 1 for each band."
msgstr "如果 `score` 不是实数数值， `edges` 不是从 ``-inf`` 到 ``inf`` 递增，或者 `probabilities` 没有为每个分段给出一个介于 0 和 1 之间的值。"

msgid "Fit the bands and their probabilities."
msgstr "拟合分段及其概率。"

msgid "Apply a Platt scaling."
msgstr "应用 Platt 缩放。"

msgid ""
"The bands are closed on the right, as in ``pandas.cut``: a score equal to an interior edge gets "
"the probability of the band below the edge. Since the outer edges are infinite, every score that "
"is not missing falls into a band."
msgstr "与 ``pandas.cut`` 一样，各分段为右闭区间：等于某个内部边界的评分取该边界下方分段的概率。由于两端边界为无穷，每个非缺失的评分都会落入某个分段。"

msgid "Conventions"
msgstr "约定"

msgid ""
"Every public function of kivi follows the rules on this page. The module pages and the guides "
"take them for granted, and the docstrings mention only where a function departs from them or adds"
" to them."
msgstr "kivi 的每个公共函数都遵守本页的规则。模块页面和各篇指南默认这些规则成立，docstring 只说明某个函数与之不同或在其之外补充的地方。"

msgid "Imports"
msgstr "导入"

msgid ""
"kivi has no top-level imports. Import each function from its module, as in ``from kivi.woe import"
" woe_table``; each module has its own page in this reference."
msgstr "kivi 没有顶层导入。请从各自所在的模块导入函数，例如 ``from kivi.woe import woe_table`` ；每个模块在本参考中都有自己的页面。"

msgid "Arguments"
msgstr "参数"

msgid ""
"The data come first and the target follows them, as in ``woe_table(groups, target)``, "
"``roc_auc(score, target)``, ``stepwise(X, target)`` and ``fit_spec(frame, target)``. A function "
"with several data arguments takes all of them before the target, as ``swap_set(current, new, "
"target)`` does, and a predicted probability comes after the target, as in "
"``calibration_table(groups, target, probability)``. scikit-learn's metrics take the target first,"
" so check the order when porting code from them."
msgstr ""
"数据在前，目标变量在数据之后，例如 ``woe_table(groups, target)`` 、 ``roc_auc(score, target)`` 、 ``stepwise(X, "
"target)`` 和 ``fit_spec(frame, target)`` 。有多个数据参数的函数先接收全部数据参数，再接收目标变量，例如 ``swap_set(current, new, "
"target)`` ；预测概率放在目标变量之后，例如 ``calibration_table(groups, target, probability)`` 。scikit-learn "
"的指标函数把目标变量放在前面，从那里移植代码时请检查参数顺序。"

msgid ""
"A predicted probability of an event, such as a PD, is always called ``probability``, as in "
"``brier_score(probability, target)``, ``calibration_table(groups, target, probability)`` and "
"``expected_loss(probability, lgd, ead)``. What a ``score`` is depends on the module; see :ref"
":`conventions-scores`."
msgstr ""
"事件的预测概率（例如 PD）一律称为 ``probability`` ，例如 ``brier_score(probability, target)`` 、 "
"``calibration_table(groups, target, probability)`` 和 ``expected_loss(probability, lgd, ead)`` 。 "
"``score`` 的含义因模块而异，见 :ref:`conventions-scores` 。"

msgid ""
"The data, and the fitted results that a function applies, such as the edges of "
":func:`~kivi.binning.cut` or the table of :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform`, are positional "
"arguments. Every option after them is keyword-only. The number of bins of "
":func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` is the one option that can also be passed by position:"
msgstr ""
"数据以及函数要应用的拟合结果（例如 :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` 的边界或 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` "
"的表）是位置参数。其后的所有选项都仅限关键字。 :func:`~kivi.binning.bin_edges` 的箱数是唯一也可以按位置传入的选项："

msgid "Inputs and results"
msgstr "输入与结果"

msgid ""
"A one-dimensional input is array_like: a list, a NumPy array or a pandas Series. A function that "
"works on several columns at once, such as :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` or "
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec`, takes a DataFrame."
msgstr ""
"一维输入是类数组（array_like）：列表、NumPy 数组或 pandas Series。同时处理多列的函数，例如 :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` 或 "
":func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` ，接收 DataFrame。"

msgid ""
"A result with one value per input value is shaped like the input. A Series gives a Series with "
"the same index and name, other array_like input gives a NumPy array, and a single number gives a "
"float. :func:`~kivi.binning.cut` and :func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` return groups, so "
"for input other than a Series they return a ``pandas.Categorical``:"
msgstr ""
"每个输入值对应一个结果值时，结果的形状与输入相同。传入 Series 得到索引和名称都相同的 Series，传入其他类数组得到 NumPy 数组，传入单个数得到 float。 "
":func:`~kivi.binning.cut` 和 :func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` 返回的是分组，因此输入不是 Series 时，它们返回 "
"``pandas.Categorical`` ："

msgid ""
"Series that describe the same observations, such as the data, the target, the probabilities and "
"the weights, must have identical indices; they are not aligned. Any other combination of these "
"inputs is matched by position. Inputs that describe other observations, such as the two samples "
"of :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` or the rejected applicants of "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling`, can have any index."
msgstr ""
"描述同一批观测的 Series，例如数据、目标变量、概率和权重，必须具有完全相同的索引；它们不会被对齐。这些输入的其他任何组合都按位置对应。描述其他观测的输入，例如 "
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 的两个样本或 :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling` "
"的拒绝申请人，可以使用任意索引。"

msgid ""
"Tables are DataFrames. A table with one row per group is indexed by the group labels, in an index"
" named ``bin``. A total is the sum of a column, such as ``woe_table(groups, "
"target)[\"iv\"].sum()``."
msgstr ""
"表格都是 DataFrame。每组一行的表以分组标签为索引，索引名为 ``bin`` 。合计是某一列之和，例如 ``woe_table(groups, "
"target)[\"iv\"].sum()`` 。"

msgid ""
"Functions do not modify their inputs. Random draws come from a local generator seeded by ``rng``,"
" so they never change NumPy's global state, and the same seed gives the same result."
msgstr "函数不会修改输入。随机抽样来自以 ``rng`` 为种子的局部生成器，因此不会改变 NumPy 的全局状态，相同的种子给出相同的结果。"

msgid "Targets, scores and probabilities"
msgstr "目标变量、评分与概率"

msgid ""
"A target is 1 for an event, such as a default, and 0 for a non-event. Any other label, and a "
"missing label, raises an error. :func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` is the exception: it reads a "
"missing label as an outcome that is not known."
msgstr "目标变量中 1 表示事件（例如违约），0 表示非事件。其他任何标签以及缺失标签都会引发错误。 :func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` 是例外：它把缺失标签视为结果未知。"

msgid ""
"In :mod:`kivi.metrics` and :mod:`kivi.strategy`, a score rises with the event probability. Pass a"
" PD as it is, and negate scorecard points, which fall as the risk rises. A cut-off of "
":mod:`kivi.strategy` approves the scores at or below it."
msgstr ""
"在 :mod:`kivi.metrics` 和 :mod:`kivi.strategy` 中，评分随事件概率升高而增大。PD 可直接传入；评分卡分值随风险升高而降低，须先取负。 "
":mod:`kivi.strategy` 的截断点通过不高于它的评分。"

msgid ""
"In :mod:`kivi.scorecard`, a ``score`` is scorecard points, which fall as the risk rises: "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd` gives a lower PD for a higher score."
msgstr ""
"在 :mod:`kivi.scorecard` 中， ``score`` 是评分卡分值，随风险升高而降低： :func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd` "
"对更高的评分给出更低的 PD。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` accepts a score in either direction and fits a negative slope"
" to one that falls as the risk rises. :func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` assumes a rising "
"score unless ``increasing=False``."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` 接受任一方向的评分，对随风险升高而降低的评分会拟合出负的斜率。 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.isotonic_fit` 默认评分随风险升高而增大，除非设置 ``increasing=False`` 。"

msgid ""
"True and False count as 1 and 0 in targets, scores and probabilities. Weights, LGDs, exposures "
"and losses reject them, and so do most numeric options, such as ``bins``, ``max_bins``, "
"``factor`` and the cut-offs:"
msgstr ""
"在目标变量、评分和概率中，True 和 False 分别计为 1 和 0。权重、LGD、敞口和损失拒绝布尔值，大多数数值选项也是如此，例如 ``bins`` 、 ``max_bins`` 、 "
"``factor`` 和各截断点："

msgid "Groups and missing values"
msgstr "分组与缺失值"

msgid ""
"The functions that count groups, such as :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table`, "
":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` and :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table`, take the "
"labels as they are: the intervals of ``pandas.cut`` or :func:`kivi.binning.cut`, strings, numbers"
" or categories."
msgstr ""
"对分组计数的函数，例如 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 、 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` ，按原样接收标签： ``pandas.cut`` 或 :func:`kivi.binning.cut` "
"的区间、字符串、数字或类别。"

msgid "Missing values form a group of their own."
msgstr "缺失值单独成组。"

msgid ""
"Only observed groups appear. Unused categories are left out, and so are the groups whose weights "
"sum to zero."
msgstr "只列出实际观测到的组。未使用的类别不会出现，权重之和为零的组也不会出现。"

msgid ""
"Categorical groups, including the intervals of ``pandas.cut``, follow the order of their "
"categories, with the missing group last. Other labels follow the order in which they first "
"appear."
msgstr "分类型分组（包括 ``pandas.cut`` 的区间）按类别顺序排列，缺失组排在最后。其他标签按首次出现的次序排列。"

msgid ""
"The functions that count, rank or fit, such as :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc`, "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table`, :func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` and "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit`, raise an error for a missing score or probability instead, "
"so decide how missing values are scored before passing them in. The functions that convert each "
"value on its own, such as :func:`~kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score`, "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_predict` and :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss`, return NaN for "
"a missing value, and :func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` returns a missing grade."
msgstr ""
"进行计数、排序或拟合的函数，例如 :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc` 、 :func:`~kivi.calibration.calibration_table` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` 和 :func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_fit` "
"，遇到缺失的评分或概率则会引发错误，因此请在传入之前决定如何为缺失值打分。逐个转换取值的函数，例如 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score` 、 "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.platt_predict` 和 :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss` ，对缺失值返回 NaN， "
":func:`~kivi.calibration.assign_grades` 则返回缺失的等级。"

msgid "Sample weights"
msgstr "样本权重"

msgid ""
"Most functions that count observations or fit a model take ``weights``: one finite, non-negative "
"number per observation, matched to the data like the target. :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` "
"and :func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` take one set for each sample, ``reference_weights`` and "
"``current_weights``."
msgstr ""
"大多数对观测计数或拟合模型的函数都接受 ``weights`` ：每个观测一个有限的非负数，与数据的对应方式和目标变量相同。 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` "
"和 :func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` 为每个样本各接收一组权重，即 ``reference_weights`` 和 ``current_weights`` 。"

msgid ""
"Counts become sums of weights, and observations with zero weight are left out. Integer weights "
"therefore give the same counts as repeating each row that many times."
msgstr "计数变为权重之和，权重为零的观测会被排除。因此整数权重与把每一行重复相应次数得到的计数相同。"

msgid ""
"Weighted quantiles use the inverted CDF, so every interior quantile edge is an observed value, "
"while unweighted quantiles interpolate between observations. Weighted edges therefore agree with "
"repeated rows only where no interpolation is needed, and weights of 1 do not give the same edges "
"as no weights."
msgstr ""
"加权分位数采用逆累积分布（inverted CDF），因此每个内部分位数边界都是实际观测到的取值，而不加权的分位数会在观测之间插值。因此加权边界只在不需要插值时与重复行的结果一致，权重全为 1 "
"也不等同于不加权。"

msgid "``smoothing`` replaces an empty cell in units of weight and is not rescaled with the weights."
msgstr "``smoothing`` 以权重为单位替换空单元格，不会随权重缩放。"

msgid ""
":func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` and :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` read the weights"
" as frequency weights, so their standard errors count the total weight as the number of "
"observations."
msgstr ""
":func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` 和 :func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` "
"把权重视为频数权重，因此它们的标准误把权重总和当作观测数。"

msgid "Errors and warnings"
msgstr "错误与警告"

msgid ""
"Invalid input raises ``ValueError``, and so does a model that cannot be fitted, such as one with "
"separated classes, which raises :exc:`kivi.selection.SeparationError`. The message names the "
"argument and, where a single value is at fault, shows the value that was received:"
msgstr ""
"无效输入会引发 ``ValueError`` ，无法拟合的模型也是如此，例如类别完全分离时会引发 :exc:`kivi.selection.SeparationError` "
"。错误信息会写明参数名；如果问题出在某个取值上，还会给出收到的值："

msgid ""
"A ``UserWarning`` means that the result differs from the request, for example fewer bins than "
"requested because of tied values, and says what to change. :func:`kivi.univariate.profile_table` "
"records such ties in a column instead, so that profiling many columns raises no warnings."
msgstr ""
"``UserWarning`` 表示结果与请求不同，例如因取值重复而得到的箱数少于请求的箱数，并说明应如何修改。 :func:`kivi.univariate.profile_table` "
"则把这类重合记录在一列中，因此分析很多列时不会产生警告。"

msgid "A ``RuntimeWarning`` means that a fit stopped before it converged."
msgstr "``RuntimeWarning`` 表示拟合在收敛之前停止。"

msgid "A ``FutureWarning`` announces a change of the public API one minor version before it takes effect."
msgstr "``FutureWarning`` 会在公共 API 的变更生效前提前一个次版本发出通知。"

msgid "Example data"
msgstr "示例数据"

msgid ""
"Example data for the guides: the bank marketing data of :func:`~kivi.datasets.load_bank`, and the"
" synthetic loan panel and loan applications of :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel` and "
":func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications`."
msgstr ""
"各篇指南使用的示例数据： :func:`~kivi.datasets.load_bank` 提供的银行营销数据，以及 :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel`"
" 和 :func:`~kivi.datasets.make_applications` 生成的合成贷款面板和合成贷款申请。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/datasets` for their columns and how the synthetic data are simulated."
msgstr "各列含义以及合成数据的模拟方式见 :doc:`/user_guide/datasets` 。"

msgid ":py:obj:`load_bank <kivi.datasets.load_bank>`\\ \\(\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`load_bank <kivi.datasets.load_bank>`\\ \\(\\)"

msgid "Load 4,521 observations from UCI Bank Marketing."
msgstr "读取 UCI Bank Marketing 的 4,521 条营销记录。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`make_loan_panel <kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel>`\\ \\(\\*\\[\\, n\\_loans\\, "
"n\\_months\\, rng\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`make_loan_panel <kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel>`\\ \\(\\*\\[\\, n\\_loans\\, "
"n\\_months\\, rng\\]\\)"

msgid "Generate a synthetic monthly panel of instalment loans."
msgstr "生成分期贷款的合成月度面板数据。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`make_applications <kivi.datasets.make_applications>`\\ \\(\\*\\[\\, n\\_applicants\\, "
"rng\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`make_applications <kivi.datasets.make_applications>`\\ \\(\\*\\[\\, n\\_applicants\\, "
"rng\\]\\)"

msgid "Generate synthetic loan applications with an approval decision."
msgstr "生成带审批决策的合成贷款申请数据。"

msgid ":py:obj:`Dataset.bank_data <kivi.datasets.Dataset.bank_data>`\\ \\(\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`Dataset.bank_data <kivi.datasets.Dataset.bank_data>`\\ \\(\\)"

msgid "The ``y`` response of the original data is returned as the binary ``target`` column."
msgstr "原始数据中的响应列 ``y`` 以二分类的 ``target`` 列返回。"

msgid "Sixteen features and the integer target. A value of 1 indicates a term deposit subscription."
msgstr "返回 16 个特征和整数标签 target。1 表示客户认购了定期存款。"

msgid "Relate a feature to ``target``."
msgstr "将某个特征与 ``target`` 关联起来。"

msgid ":obj:`make_loan_panel`"
msgstr ":obj:`make_loan_panel`"

msgid "Synthetic monthly history of a loan portfolio."
msgstr "贷款资产组合的合成月度历史。"

msgid ""
"Bank Marketing by S. Moro, P. Rita and P. Cortez (2014) is distributed under CC BY 4.0. The "
"bundled CSV was converted from the legacy workbook."
msgstr "Bank Marketing 由 S. Moro、P. Rita 和 P. Cortez 于 2014 年发布，按 CC BY 4.0 授权。随包 CSV 由旧版工作簿转换而来。"

msgid ""
"S. Moro, P. Rita and P. Cortez, \"Bank Marketing\", UCI Machine Learning Repository, 2014. "
"https://doi.org/10.24432/C5K306"
msgstr ""
"S. Moro, P. Rita and P. Cortez, \"Bank Marketing\", UCI Machine Learning Repository, 2014. "
"https://doi.org/10.24432/C5K306"

msgid "[Rd093f8221f97-1]_"
msgstr "[Rd093f8221f97-1]_"

msgid ""
"The loans are originated over `n_months` months and observed at the end of every month on book "
"until the month after the last origination month. Delinquency rolls forward when a borrower "
"misses instalments and cures when the arrears are paid, and a loan that reaches 90 days past due "
"stays there. The data is simulated, not drawn from a real portfolio."
msgstr ""
"贷款在 `n_months` 个月内陆续发放，并在每个账龄月的月末观测一次，直到最后一个放款月的下一个月。借款人漏缴期款时逾期向前滚动，还清欠款后回到正常；逾期达到 90 "
"天的贷款会一直停留在该状态。数据是模拟生成的，并非取自真实的资产组合。"

msgid "**n_loans**"
msgstr "**n_loans**"

msgid "int, default 5000"
msgstr "int，默认 5000"

msgid "Number of loans, each assigned to an origination month at random."
msgstr "贷款笔数，每笔贷款随机分配到一个放款月。"

msgid "**n_months**"
msgstr "**n_months**"

msgid "int, default 24"
msgstr "int，默认 24"

msgid ""
"Number of origination months, starting with January 2024. The oldest cohort is observed for "
"`n_months` months on book and the youngest for one."
msgstr "放款月份数，从 2024 年 1 月开始。最早的批次观测 `n_months` 个账龄月，最晚的批次只观测一个。"

msgid "**rng**"
msgstr "**rng**"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{None, int, numpy.random.Generator}, optional"
msgstr "{None, int, numpy.random.Generator}，可选"

msgid ""
"Seed or generator passed to `numpy.random.default_rng`. The global NumPy random state is not "
"used, so the same seed always returns the same panel."
msgstr "传给 `numpy.random.default_rng` 的种子或生成器。不使用 NumPy 的全局随机状态，因此同一个种子总是返回同样的面板数据。"

msgid ""
"One row per loan and month on book, sorted by loan and then by month on book, with the columns "
"described in the Notes."
msgstr "每笔贷款的每个账龄月一行，先按贷款、再按账龄排序。各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid "If `n_loans` or `n_months` is not a positive integer."
msgstr "如果 `n_loans` 或 `n_months` 不是正整数。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.vintage.vintage_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.vintage.vintage_table`"

msgid "Cumulative bad rates by cohort and month on book."
msgstr "按批次和账龄统计的累计坏账率。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.vintage.transition_matrix`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.vintage.transition_matrix`"

msgid "Movements between delinquency buckets."
msgstr "贷款在逾期档位之间的迁移。"

msgid ":obj:`load_bank`"
msgstr ":obj:`load_bank`"

msgid "Real data with a binary target."
msgstr "带二分类目标的真实数据。"

msgid "The columns are:"
msgstr "各列为："

msgid "``loan_id``: integer identifier, increasing with the origination month;"
msgstr "``loan_id`` ：整数标识，随放款月份递增；"

msgid "``cohort``: the origination month, a monthly ``pandas.Period``;"
msgstr "``cohort`` ：放款月份，为月度 ``pandas.Period`` ；"

msgid "``month``: the month of the observation, ``cohort + month_on_book``;"
msgstr "``month`` ：观测所在月份，即 ``cohort + month_on_book`` ；"

msgid "``month_on_book``: months since origination, from 1;"
msgstr "``month_on_book`` ：放款后经过的月数（账龄），从 1 开始；"

msgid "``term``: contractual number of monthly instalments, 12, 24 or 36;"
msgstr "``term`` ：合同约定的月供期数，为 12、24 或 36；"

msgid "``amount``: amount lent;"
msgstr "``amount`` ：放款金额；"

msgid "``balance``: outstanding principal at the end of the month;"
msgstr "``balance`` ：月末的剩余本金；"

msgid ""
"``status``: days past due at the end of the month, an ordered categorical with the categories "
"``current``, ``1-29``, ``30-59``, ``60-89`` and ``90+``."
msgstr "``status`` ：月末的逾期天数，为有序分类变量，类别依次为 ``current`` 、 ``1-29`` 、 ``30-59`` 、 ``60-89`` 和 ``90+`` 。"

#, python-format
msgid ""
"Each loan is repaid in equal monthly instalments at 1% interest a month. Its status counts the "
"months since its oldest unpaid instalment fell due: one is ``1-29``, two ``30-59``, three "
"``60-89`` and four or more ``90+``. Within the term this is the number of instalments past due, "
"and a loan that is still behind after its term keeps rolling."
msgstr ""
"每笔贷款按月等额本息还款，月利率为 1%。其状态记录自最早一期未还期款到期以来的月数：一个月为 ``1-29`` ，两个月为 ``30-59`` ，三个月为 ``60-89`` ，四个月及以上为"
" ``90+`` 。在期限内，这就是逾期未还的期数；期限结束后仍有欠款的贷款会继续滚动。"

msgid ""
"Every month, a current loan misses its instalment with a probability that rises over the first "
"six months on book and then declines, scaled by a risk factor of the loan and one of its cohort, "
"so cohorts differ in quality. A delinquent loan pays all its arrears and becomes current, pays "
"one instalment and keeps its status, or pays nothing and rolls to the next bucket; the chance of "
"curing falls and that of rolling rises with the days past due. A ``90+`` loan makes no further "
"payments, so its balance stays the same. A loan leaves the panel after its last instalment is "
"paid; loans are not charged off."
msgstr ""
"每个月，正常贷款漏缴当期期款的概率在放款后前六个月逐渐上升，之后下降，并乘以该贷款和所在批次各自的风险系数，因此不同批次的质量不同。逾期贷款要么还清全部欠款、回到正常，要么只还一期、保持原状态，要么完全不还、滚动到下一个逾期档位；逾期天数越长，回到正常的概率越低，滚动的概率越高。"
" ``90+`` 的贷款不再还款，因此余额保持不变。贷款还清最后一期后离开面板；贷款不会被核销。"

msgid ""
"Every applicant has a few numeric and categorical features, the PD of an incumbent scorecard and "
"a true default flag. The incumbent PD and two policy rules decide who is approved, so the data "
"show the selection that reject inference corrects for. The data is simulated, not drawn from a "
"real portfolio."
msgstr ""
"每个申请人都有若干数值型和类别型特征、现行评分卡给出的 PD 以及真实的违约标记。现行评分卡的 PD "
"和两条政策规则决定谁获批，因此数据带有拒绝推断所要纠正的样本选择。数据是模拟的，并非取自真实的资产组合。"

msgid "**n_applicants**"
msgstr "**n_applicants**"

msgid "int, default 10000"
msgstr "int，默认 10000"

msgid "Number of applications."
msgstr "申请笔数。"

msgid ""
"Seed or generator passed to `numpy.random.default_rng`. The global NumPy random state is not "
"used, so the same seed always returns the same applications."
msgstr "传给 `numpy.random.default_rng` 的种子或生成器。不使用 NumPy 的全局随机状态，因此同一个种子总是返回同样的申请数据。"

msgid "One row per application with the columns described in the Notes."
msgstr "每笔申请一行，各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid "If `n_applicants` is not a positive integer."
msgstr "如果 `n_applicants` 不是正整数。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation`"

msgid "Infer the outcomes of rejected applicants."
msgstr "推断拒绝申请人的结果。"

msgid "``age``: age in years, from 18 to 75;"
msgstr "``age`` ：年龄（岁），从 18 到 75；"

msgid "``income``: monthly income, rounded to tens;"
msgstr "``income`` ：月收入，取整到十位；"

msgid "``debt_to_income``: monthly debt payments over income, rounded to hundredths;"
msgstr "``debt_to_income`` ：每月还债额与收入之比，保留两位小数；"

msgid "``inquiries``: number of credit inquiries in the last six months;"
msgstr "``inquiries`` ：近六个月的征信查询次数；"

msgid "``housing``: a categorical with the categories ``own``, ``mortgage`` and ``rent``;"
msgstr "``housing`` ：分类变量，类别为 ``own`` 、 ``mortgage`` 和 ``rent`` ；"

msgid ""
"``employment``: a categorical with the categories ``permanent``, ``temporary`` and "
"``self_employed``;"
msgstr "``employment`` ：分类变量，类别为 ``permanent`` 、 ``temporary`` 和 ``self_employed`` ；"

msgid "``incumbent_pd``: the PD of the scorecard that decided the application, rounded to four decimals;"
msgstr "``incumbent_pd`` ：决定该申请的评分卡给出的 PD，保留四位小数；"

msgid ""
"``policy_decline``: True if a policy rule declined the application, whatever its PD: a debt-to-"
"income ratio above 0.6 or an age below 21;"
msgstr "``policy_decline`` ：若某条政策规则拒绝了该申请（无论其 PD 如何）则为 True，规则为负债收入比高于 0.6 或年龄低于 21 岁；"

msgid "``approved``: True if ``incumbent_pd`` is below 0.15 and no policy rule declined the application;"
msgstr "``approved`` ：若 ``incumbent_pd`` 低于 0.15 且没有政策规则拒绝该申请，则为 True；"

msgid "``target``: 1 if the applicant defaults, else 0."
msgstr "``target`` ：申请人违约为 1，否则为 0。"

msgid ""
"The default probability rises with the debt-to-income ratio and the number of inquiries, falls "
"with age and income, and is higher for renters and for temporary and self-employed applicants. A "
"hidden risk factor that no column holds also raises it, and the number of inquiries rises with "
"that factor."
msgstr "违约概率随负债收入比和征信查询次数上升，随年龄和收入下降，租房者以及临时雇佣和自雇的申请人违约概率更高。一个不在任何列中的隐藏风险因子也会提高违约概率，征信查询次数也随该因子增加。"

msgid ""
"The incumbent scorecard weighs the features differently, ignores ``housing`` and, like an "
"underwriter with a credit bureau report, sees part of the hidden risk factor. Rejected applicants"
" are therefore riskier than approved applicants with the same features, so a model fitted on the "
"approved applicants alone underestimates their default rate."
msgstr ""
"现行评分卡对各特征的权重不同，不使用 ``housing`` "
"，并且像手握征信报告的审批人员一样，能看到隐藏风险因子的一部分。因此，在特征相同时，拒绝申请人比获批申请人风险更高，只用获批申请人拟合的模型会低估他们的违约率。"

msgid ""
"In practice, the outcome is known only for approved applicants. Here ``target`` is also given for"
" rejected applicants, but only to evaluate reject inference: a model must not be fitted on it, or"
" reject inference would be pointless."
msgstr "实际中只有获批申请人的结果是已知的。这里也给出了拒绝申请人的 ``target`` ，但只用于评估拒绝推断：不能用它拟合模型，否则拒绝推断就失去了意义。"

msgid ""
"The rejected applicants default three times as often as the approved ones, an outcome that only "
"synthetic data can show:"
msgstr "拒绝申请人的违约频率是获批申请人的三倍，这只有合成数据才能展示："

msgid ""
"This is the same as `load_bank`, which new code should use instead. It is kept for existing code "
"and does not warn."
msgstr "与 `load_bank` 相同，新代码应改用 `load_bank` 。保留此方法是为了兼容已有代码，调用时不会发出警告。"

msgid "The same data."
msgstr "相同的数据。"

msgid "Glossary"
msgstr "术语表"

msgid ""
"The terms of credit risk modeling as the guides and the docstrings use them. Each entry links to "
"the guide that explains the term with an example."
msgstr "本页按各篇指南和 docstring 中的用法列出信用风险建模的术语。每个条目都链接到用示例解释该术语的指南。"

msgid "Accepts and rejects"
msgstr "通过样本与拒绝样本"

msgid ""
"The applicants that a previous policy approved and declined. The outcome is known only for the "
"accepts, so a model developed on them alone may misjudge the rejects; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference`."
msgstr "以往策略批准和拒绝的申请人。只有通过样本的结果是已知的，因此只在它们上面开发的模型可能误判拒绝样本；见 :doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference` 。"

msgid "Area under the ROC curve (AUC)"
msgstr "ROC 曲线下面积（AUC）"

msgid ""
"The probability that a randomly chosen event scores higher than a randomly chosen non-event, with"
" ties counted as one half. A score unrelated to the target has an AUC of about 0.5; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/metrics`."
msgstr "随机抽取的一个事件比随机抽取的一个非事件评分更高的概率，评分相同时计为二分之一。与目标变量无关的评分 AUC 约为 0.5；见 :doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid ""
"Dividing the values of a numeric variable into intervals, the bins, whose edges are fitted on a "
"reference sample and then applied to every other sample. Scorecard development calls it classing:"
" fine classing forms many small bins, and coarse classing merges them into a few that are large "
"enough to be stable; see :doc:`/user_guide/binning`."
msgstr ""
"把数值变量的取值划分为若干区间（即箱）：边界在基准样本上拟合，然后应用于其他每个样本。评分卡开发中也称为 classing：细分箱（fine "
"classing）先形成许多小箱，粗分箱（coarse classing）再把它们合并为少数几个足够大、足够稳定的箱；见 :doc:`/user_guide/binning` 。"

msgid "Binning specification"
msgstr "分箱方案"

msgid ""
"The edges, special codes and WOE tables of every column of a model, fitted together and saved as "
"versioned JSON, so that production data are grouped and encoded exactly as the development "
"sample; see :doc:`/user_guide/spec`."
msgstr "模型每一列的边界、特殊值和 WOE 表，一起拟合并保存为带版本号的 JSON，使生产数据的分组和编码与开发样本完全一致；见 :doc:`/user_guide/spec` 。"

msgid "Characteristic stability index (CSI)"
msgstr "特征稳定性指标（CSI）"

msgid ""
"The change of a variable's average scorecard points from a reference sample to a current one: the"
" change of each group's share times the group's points, summed over the groups. Over all the "
"variables of a scorecard, the CSI values add up to the change of the average score; see :ref"
":`characteristic-stability`."
msgstr ""
"变量的平均评分卡分值从基准样本到当前样本的变化：每组占比的变化乘以该组的分值，再对所有组求和。对评分卡的全部变量，CSI 之和等于平均分的变化；见 :ref:`characteristic-"
"stability` 。"

msgid "Cohort"
msgstr "放款批次"

msgid ""
"The loans originated in the same period, usually a month, followed together as they age in a "
"vintage table; see :doc:`/user_guide/vintage`."
msgstr "同一时期（通常是同一个月）发放的贷款，在 Vintage 表中随账龄一起跟踪；见 :doc:`/user_guide/vintage` 。"

msgid "Cut-off"
msgstr "截断点"

msgid ""
"The score that separates approval from decline. kivi approves the scores at or below the cut-off,"
" because its scores rise with the risk; see :doc:`/user_guide/strategy`."
msgstr "区分通过与拒绝的评分。kivi 的评分随风险升高而增大，因此通过不高于截断点的评分；见 :doc:`/user_guide/strategy` 。"

msgid "Event and non-event"
msgstr "事件与非事件"

msgid ""
"The two outcomes of a binary target: an event has target 1, such as a default or another bad "
"outcome, and a non-event has target 0. The guides read the subscription of the bundled bank data "
"as the event; see :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv`."
msgstr "二元目标变量的两种结果：事件的目标值为 1，例如违约或其他不良结果；非事件的目标值为 0。各篇指南把内置银行数据中的认购视为事件；见 :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 。"

msgid "Event rate"
msgstr "事件率"

msgid ""
"The share of events among the observations of a group, called the bad rate when the event is a "
"default. It is computed from the raw counts, without smoothing; see :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv`."
msgstr "某组观测中事件所占的比例，事件为违约时称为坏账率。它按原始计数计算，不做平滑；见 :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 。"

msgid "Ever bad"
msgstr "曾经为坏（ever bad）"

msgid ""
"A loan is ever bad by a month on book if it was bad at any month on book up to then, even if it "
"has cured since. The cumulative bad rates of a vintage table count the loans that are ever bad; "
"see :doc:`/user_guide/vintage`."
msgstr ""
"如果一笔贷款在某个账龄及之前的任一账龄为坏，即使之后已经恢复正常，它在该账龄也算曾经为坏。Vintage 表的累计坏账率统计的就是曾经为坏的贷款；见 "
":doc:`/user_guide/vintage` 。"

msgid "Expected loss (EL)"
msgstr "预期损失（EL）"

msgid ""
"The loss that an exposure is expected to cause: its probability of default times its loss given "
"default times its exposure at default; see :doc:`/user_guide/strategy`."
msgstr "一笔敞口预期造成的损失：违约概率乘以违约损失率再乘以违约风险敞口；见 :doc:`/user_guide/strategy` 。"

msgid "Exposure at default (EAD)"
msgstr "违约风险敞口（EAD）"

msgid ""
"The amount owed when a borrower defaults, such as the outstanding balance of a loan; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/strategy`."
msgstr "借款人违约时所欠的金额，例如贷款的未偿余额；见 :doc:`/user_guide/strategy` 。"

msgid "Gains table"
msgstr "增益表"

msgid ""
"A table of score bands from the riskiest to the safest, with the event rate and lift of each band"
" and the cumulative shares of events and non-events; see :doc:`/user_guide/metrics`."
msgstr "按评分段从风险最高到最低排列的表，列出每段的事件率和提升度，以及事件和非事件的累计占比；见 :doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid "Gini coefficient"
msgstr "Gini 系数"

msgid ""
"Twice the AUC minus 1: 0 for a score unrelated to the target and 1 for a score that ranks every "
"event above every non-event. Scorecard development reports it more often than the AUC itself; see"
" :doc:`/user_guide/metrics`."
msgstr ""
"AUC 的两倍减 1：与目标变量无关的评分为 0，把每个事件都排在每个非事件之前的评分为 1。评分卡开发中报告 Gini 系数比报告 AUC 本身更常见；见 "
":doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid "Grade"
msgstr "等级"

msgid ""
"One class of a rating system or master scale, with a PD of its own and bounds that decide which "
"predicted PDs fall into it; see :doc:`/user_guide/calibration`."
msgstr "评级体系或主标尺中的一个类别，有自己的 PD，并由上下界决定哪些预测 PD 落入其中；见 :doc:`/user_guide/calibration` 。"

msgid "Information value (IV)"
msgstr "信息值（IV）"

msgid ""
"The sum of the differences between the event share and the non-event share of each group, each "
"times the group's WOE. It measures how strongly a grouped variable separates events from non-"
"events on its own; see :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv`."
msgstr "每组事件占比与非事件占比之差乘以该组 WOE，再对所有组求和。它衡量一个分组后的变量单独区分事件与非事件的能力；见 :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 。"

msgid "Kolmogorov-Smirnov statistic (KS)"
msgstr "Kolmogorov-Smirnov 统计量（KS）"

msgid ""
"The largest absolute gap between the distribution functions of the scores of events and of non-"
"events; see :doc:`/user_guide/metrics`."
msgstr "事件评分与非事件评分的分布函数之间的最大绝对差距；见 :doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid "Lift"
msgstr "提升度（lift）"

msgid ""
"The event rate of a group divided by the event rate of the whole sample. A lift above 1 marks a "
"group that is riskier than average; see :doc:`/user_guide/metrics`."
msgstr "某组的事件率除以整个样本的事件率。提升度大于 1 表示该组风险高于平均水平；见 :doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid "Loss given default (LGD)"
msgstr "违约损失率（LGD）"

msgid ""
"The share of the exposure that is lost when a borrower defaults, after recoveries and collateral;"
" see :doc:`/user_guide/strategy`."
msgstr "借款人违约时，扣除回收和抵押品之后损失的敞口比例；见 :doc:`/user_guide/strategy` 。"

msgid "Master scale"
msgstr "主标尺"

msgid ""
"A fixed set of grades that divides the PD range from 0 to 1, so that ratings from different "
"models share one meaning; see :doc:`/user_guide/calibration`."
msgstr "把 0 到 1 的 PD 区间划分为一组固定等级，使不同模型给出的评级具有同一含义；见 :doc:`/user_guide/calibration` 。"

msgid "Month on book"
msgstr "账龄（month on book）"

msgid ""
"The number of months since a loan was originated. A vintage table compares cohorts at the same "
"month on book; see :doc:`/user_guide/vintage`."
msgstr "贷款发放以来的月数。Vintage 表在相同账龄上比较各放款批次；见 :doc:`/user_guide/vintage` 。"

msgid "Points to double the odds (PDO)"
msgstr "好坏比翻倍所需分数（PDO）"

msgid ""
"The number of scorecard points by which the score rises when the good:bad odds double. Together "
"with a base score and the odds at that score, it sets the scale of a scorecard; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/scorecard`."
msgstr "好坏比翻倍时评分增加的分数。它与基准分及基准分对应的好坏比一起确定评分卡的刻度；见 :doc:`/user_guide/scorecard` 。"

msgid "Population stability index (PSI)"
msgstr "群体稳定性指标（PSI）"

msgid ""
"A measure of how much the distribution of a variable or a score has shifted between a reference "
"sample and a current one, summed over the groups from the change of each group's share; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/psi`."
msgstr "衡量变量或评分的分布在基准样本与当前样本之间偏移了多少，由每组占比的变化计算并对所有组求和；见 :doc:`/user_guide/psi` 。"

msgid "Probability of default (PD)"
msgstr "违约概率（PD）"

msgid ""
"The probability that a borrower defaults within a given horizon, usually twelve months. kivi "
"calls a predicted PD, or any other predicted event probability, ``probability``; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/calibration`."
msgstr ""
"借款人在给定期限内（通常为十二个月）违约的概率。kivi 把预测的 PD 以及其他任何预测的事件概率都称为 ``probability`` ；见 "
":doc:`/user_guide/calibration` 。"

msgid "Reason codes"
msgstr "原因码"

msgid ""
"The variables that lowered an applicant's score most, compared with the best group of each "
"variable, as given to a declined applicant; see :doc:`/user_guide/scorecard`."
msgstr "与每个变量的最优分组相比，使申请人评分降低最多的变量，通常告知被拒绝的申请人；见 :doc:`/user_guide/scorecard` 。"

msgid "Reject inference"
msgstr "拒绝推断"

msgid ""
"Methods that supply outcomes for rejected applicants, as rows with weights or as weights for the "
"accepts, so that a model can be refitted on all applicants; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference`."
msgstr "为被拒绝的申请人补充结果的方法，结果以带权重的行或通过样本的权重给出，从而可以在全部申请人上重新拟合模型；见 :doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference` 。"

msgid "Roll rate"
msgstr "滚动率"

msgid ""
"The share of the loans in a delinquency bucket at one month end that are in the next worse bucket"
" at the next month end; see :doc:`/user_guide/vintage`."
msgstr "某个月末处于某一逾期档位的贷款中，到下一个月末进入更差一档的比例；见 :doc:`/user_guide/vintage` 。"

msgid "Smoothing"
msgstr "平滑"

msgid ""
"The value that replaces an empty count before shares are computed, 0.5 by default, so that the "
"WOE, the IV and the PSI of a group stay finite. Counts are reported as observed, and only the "
"shares are smoothed; see :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv`."
msgstr "计算占比之前用来替换空计数的值，默认为 0.5，使每组的 WOE、IV 和 PSI 保持有限。计数按观测值报告，只有占比经过平滑；见 :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 。"

msgid "Special codes"
msgstr "特殊编码"

msgid ""
"Values that stand for a state rather than a measurement, such as -1 for \"never contacted\" or "
"999 for \"no record\". Passed in ``special``, they are left out of the fit of the edges and each "
"gets a group of its own; see :ref:`special-values`."
msgstr ""
"表示某种状态而不是测量值的取值，例如表示“从未联系”的 -1 或表示“无记录”的 999。传入 ``special`` 后，它们不参与边界拟合，并且各自单独成组；见 :ref:`special-"
"values` 。"

msgid "Swap set"
msgstr "交换集"

msgid ""
"The four groups of applicants that two scores, each with its cut-off, approve or decline. The "
"swap-outs are approved only by the current score and the swap-ins only by the new one; see "
":doc:`/user_guide/strategy`."
msgstr "两个评分各按自己的截断点通过或拒绝申请人，由此形成的四组申请人。换出是只有现行评分通过的申请人，换入是只有新评分通过的申请人；见 :doc:`/user_guide/strategy` 。"

msgid "Transition matrix"
msgstr "转移矩阵"

msgid ""
"A table that counts the loans or obligors that moved from each state to each other state between "
"two dates, such as delinquency buckets or rating grades; see :doc:`/user_guide/vintage`."
msgstr "统计贷款或债务人在两个日期之间从每种状态转移到其他每种状态的数量的表，状态可以是逾期档位或评级等级；见 :doc:`/user_guide/vintage` 。"

msgid "Vintage table"
msgstr "Vintage 表"

msgid "The cumulative ever-bad rate of each cohort by month on book; see :doc:`/user_guide/vintage`."
msgstr "每个放款批次按账龄统计的累计曾经为坏比例；见 :doc:`/user_guide/vintage` 。"

msgid "Weight of evidence (WOE)"
msgstr "证据权重（WOE）"

msgid ""
"The logarithm of a group's share of all events over its share of all non-events. A positive WOE "
"marks a group that is relatively more common among events; see :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv`."
msgstr "某组在全部事件中的占比与在全部非事件中的占比之比的对数。WOE 为正表示该组在事件中相对更常见；见 :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 。"

msgid "Model performance"
msgstr "模型表现"

msgid ""
"Measure how well a score that rises with the event probability separates events from non-events. "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc`, :func:`~kivi.metrics.gini` and :func:`~kivi.metrics.ks` summarize "
"the ranking, :func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table` breaks it down by score band, and "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.brier_score` compares probabilities with outcomes."
msgstr ""
"衡量随事件概率升高而增大的评分区分事件与非事件的能力。 :func:`~kivi.metrics.roc_auc` 、 :func:`~kivi.metrics.gini` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.ks` 概括排序能力， :func:`~kivi.metrics.gains_table` 按评分段分解， "
":func:`~kivi.metrics.brier_score` 把概率与实际结果比较。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/metrics` for the definitions, examples and how to read a gains table."
msgstr "定义、示例以及如何解读增益表，见 :doc:`/user_guide/metrics` 。"

msgid ":py:obj:`roc_auc <kivi.metrics.roc_auc>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`roc_auc <kivi.metrics.roc_auc>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the area under the ROC curve of a score."
msgstr "计算评分的 ROC 曲线下面积。"

msgid ":py:obj:`gini <kivi.metrics.gini>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`gini <kivi.metrics.gini>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the Gini coefficient of a score."
msgstr "计算评分的 Gini 系数。"

msgid ":py:obj:`ks <kivi.metrics.ks>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`ks <kivi.metrics.ks>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the Kolmogorov-Smirnov statistic of a score."
msgstr "计算评分的 Kolmogorov-Smirnov 统计量。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`gains_table <kivi.metrics.gains_table>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, bins\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`gains_table <kivi.metrics.gains_table>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, bins\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Summarize events by score band, from the highest scores to the lowest."
msgstr "按评分段汇总事件，从最高评分到最低评分排列。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`brier_score <kivi.metrics.brier_score>`\\ \\(probability\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`brier_score <kivi.metrics.brier_score>`\\ \\(probability\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the Brier score of predicted event probabilities."
msgstr "计算预测事件概率的 Brier 分数。"

msgid ""
"The AUC is the probability that a randomly chosen event has a higher score than a randomly chosen"
" non-event, with ties counted as one half."
msgstr "AUC 是随机抽取的一个事件比随机抽取的一个非事件评分更高的概率，评分相同时计为二分之一。"

msgid ""
"The score comes first and the target second, as in `kivi.woe.woe_table`; scikit-learn's metrics "
"take the target first."
msgstr "评分在前、目标在后，与 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 相同；scikit-learn 的指标函数则把目标放在前面。"

msgid ""
"Finite numeric scores that are higher for a higher event probability. Negate scorecard points, "
"which are higher for a lower risk."
msgstr "有限的数值评分，事件概率越高，评分越高。评分卡分数越高表示风险越低，因此须取负后再传入。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, such as the inverse of its sampling rate, matched like "
"`target`. Every count becomes a sum of weights, so integer weights give the same result as "
"repeating rows."
msgstr "每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` 相同。每个计数都变为权重之和，因此整数权重与重复相应行的结果相同。"

msgid ""
"The AUC, from 0 to 1. A score unrelated to the target gives about 0.5, and a value below 0.5 "
"suggests that the score runs the other way."
msgstr "AUC，取值 0 到 1。与目标无关的评分约为 0.5，低于 0.5 则说明评分方向可能相反。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` "
"has a label other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of them, or `score` is not real and numeric or has a "
"missing or infinite value. Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one "
"finite, non-negative weight, has an index other than that of `score`, or leaves a class without "
"weight."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，索引或长度不一致，`target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签或缺少其中之一，或 `score` 不是实数数值或含有缺失值、无穷值。此外，如果 `weights` "
"不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负的权重、索引与 `score` 不同，或使某一类没有权重。"

msgid ":obj:`gini`"
msgstr ":obj:`gini`"

msgid "The same ranking measure on a scale from -1 to 1."
msgstr "同一排序度量，取值范围为 -1 到 1。"

msgid ":obj:`ks`"
msgstr ":obj:`ks`"

msgid "Largest gap between the score distributions of the two classes."
msgstr "两个类别评分分布之间的最大差距。"

msgid ":obj:`gains_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`gains_table`"

msgid "Event rates and captured events by score band."
msgstr "各评分段的事件率和捕获的事件。"

msgid ""
"With :math:`n_1` events and :math:`n_0` non-events, let :math:`R_1` be the sum of the ranks of "
"the events among all scores, where tied scores share their average rank. The Mann-Whitney "
"statistic gives"
msgstr "设有 :math:`n_1` 个事件和 :math:`n_0` 个非事件，:math:`R_1` 为事件在全部评分中的秩之和，相同评分取平均秩。由 Mann-Whitney 统计量得"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{AUC} = \\frac{R_1 - n_1 (n_1 + 1) / 2}{n_1 n_0}."
msgstr "\\mathrm{AUC} = \\frac{R_1 - n_1 (n_1 + 1) / 2}{n_1 n_0}."

msgid ""
"With weights, each pair of an event :math:`i` and a non-event :math:`j` counts with weight "
":math:`w_i w_j`, and :math:`n_1` and :math:`n_0` are the total weights of the two classes."
msgstr "使用权重时，每一对事件 :math:`i` 与非事件 :math:`j` 以权重 :math:`w_i w_j` 计入， :math:`n_1` 和 :math:`n_0` 则是两类的权重总和。"

msgid ""
"J. A. Hanley and B. J. McNeil, \"The meaning and use of the area under a receiver operating "
"characteristic (ROC) curve\", Radiology, 143(1), pp. 29-36, 1982."
msgstr ""
"J. A. Hanley and B. J. McNeil, \"The meaning and use of the area under a receiver operating "
"characteristic (ROC) curve\", Radiology, 143(1), pp. 29-36, 1982."

msgid "[R8309ac12020d-1]_"
msgstr "[R8309ac12020d-1]_"

msgid "Scorecard points are higher for a lower risk, so negate them:"
msgstr "评分卡分数越高表示风险越低，因此要取负："

msgid ""
"The Gini coefficient rescales the AUC to run from -1 to 1, so that a score unrelated to the "
"target gives about 0."
msgstr "Gini 系数把 AUC 换算到 -1 到 1 的范围，使与目标无关的评分约为 0。"

msgid "The Gini coefficient, from -1 to 1. A negative value suggests that the score runs the other way."
msgstr "Gini 系数，取值 -1 到 1。负值说明评分方向可能相反。"

msgid ":obj:`roc_auc`"
msgstr ":obj:`roc_auc`"

msgid "The area under the ROC curve."
msgstr "ROC 曲线下面积。"

msgid "The Gini coefficient, also called the accuracy ratio, is"
msgstr "Gini 系数也称为准确性比率（accuracy ratio），其定义为"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{Gini} = 2\\,\\mathrm{AUC} - 1."
msgstr "\\mathrm{Gini} = 2\\,\\mathrm{AUC} - 1."

msgid ""
"The KS statistic is the largest gap between the cumulative distribution of the scores of events "
"and that of non-events."
msgstr "KS 统计量是事件评分的累计分布与非事件评分的累计分布之间的最大差距。"

msgid "Finite numeric scores, such as predicted event probabilities."
msgstr "有限的数值评分，例如预测的事件概率。"

msgid "The largest gap, from 0 to 1."
msgstr "最大差距，取值 0 到 1。"

msgid "The gap at the edge of each score band."
msgstr "每个评分段边界处的差距。"

msgid "The probability that an event scores higher than a non-event."
msgstr "事件评分高于非事件评分的概率。"

msgid ""
"Let :math:`F_1` and :math:`F_0` be the empirical distribution functions of the scores of events "
"and of non-events. Then"
msgstr "设 :math:`F_1` 和 :math:`F_0` 分别为事件评分和非事件评分的经验分布函数，则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{KS} = \\max_t \\, \\lvert F_1(t) - F_0(t) \\rvert,"
msgstr "\\mathrm{KS} = \\max_t \\, \\lvert F_1(t) - F_0(t) \\rvert,"

msgid ""
"where :math:`t` runs over the observed scores. With weights, the distribution functions are "
"weighted. As in the two-sample Kolmogorov-Smirnov test, the gap is taken in absolute value, so "
"negated scores give the same KS; use the sign of `gini` to check the direction."
msgstr ""
"其中 :math:`t` 取遍观测到的评分。使用权重时，分布函数按权重计算。与双样本 Kolmogorov-Smirnov 检验一样，差距取绝对值，因此评分取负后 KS 不变；请用 `gini`"
" 的符号检查方向。"

msgid ""
"The largest gap can come from a region where the score runs the wrong way, for example when "
"events gather among the lowest scores as well as the highest. The KS then measures how far apart "
"the two distributions are rather than how well the score ranks events above non-events. The "
"cumulative shares in `gains_table` show where the gap occurs."
msgstr ""
"最大差距可能来自评分方向相反的区域，例如事件既集中在最高评分处，也集中在最低评分处。此时 KS 衡量的是两个分布相距多远，而不是评分把事件排在非事件之前的能力。`gains_table` "
"中的累计占比可以显示差距出现的位置。"

msgid "L. C. Thomas, D. B. Edelman and J. N. Crook, \"Credit Scoring and Its Applications\", SIAM, 2002."
msgstr "L. C. Thomas, D. B. Edelman and J. N. Crook, \"Credit Scoring and Its Applications\", SIAM, 2002."

msgid "[Rbfc1ea3c8bbd-1]_"
msgstr "[Rbfc1ea3c8bbd-1]_"

msgid ""
"Each row shows how many events a band holds and what share of all events is captured by reviewing"
" that band and every band above it."
msgstr "每行给出该评分段的事件数，以及审查该段及其以上各段时捕获的事件占全部事件的比例。"

msgid "int or array_like, default 10"
msgstr "int 或 array_like，默认 10"

msgid ""
"Number of quantile bands, or increasing band edges. An integer is the same as passing "
"``kivi.binning.bin_edges(score, bins=bins)``, so tied scores can leave fewer bands than "
"requested. Pass the edges fitted on a development sample to compare later samples on the same "
"bands. With `weights`, an integer gives weighted quantile edges, as ``bin_edges(score, bins=bins,"
" weights=weights)`` does."
msgstr ""
"分位数评分段的数量，或递增的分段边界。整数等同于传入 ``kivi.binning.bin_edges(score, "
"bins=bins)``，因此相同评分可能使评分段少于请求的数量。传入在开发样本上拟合的边界，即可在同一组评分段上比较后续样本。使用 `weights` 时，整数会得到加权分位数边界，与 "
"``bin_edges(score, bins=bins, weights=weights)`` 相同。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, such as the inverse of its sampling rate, matched like "
"`target`. The counts become sums of weights. On the same edges, integer weights give the same "
"table as repeating rows; an integer `bins` can give other edges, because weighted quantiles use "
"the inverted CDF."
msgstr ""
"每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` 相同。计数变为权重之和。在相同边界上，整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同；而整数 `bins` "
"可能得到不同的边界，因为加权分位数采用逆累积分布（inverted CDF）。"

msgid ""
"One row per score band, from the highest band to the lowest, indexed by the interval of the band."
" The columns are described in the Notes."
msgstr "每个评分段一行，从最高段到最低段排列，以评分段的区间为索引。各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` "
"has a label other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of them, `score` is not real and numeric or has a "
"missing or infinite value, `bins` is neither a positive integer nor increasing edges, or a score "
"lies outside the edges. Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one "
"finite, non-negative weight, has an index other than that of `score`, or leaves a class without "
"weight."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，索引或长度不一致，`target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签或缺少其中之一，`score` 不是实数数值或含有缺失值、无穷值，`bins` "
"既不是正整数也不是递增的边界，或有评分落在边界之外。此外，如果 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负的权重、索引与 `score` 不同，或使某一类没有权重。"

msgid ""
"If `bins` is an integer and tied scores leave fewer bands than requested, as in "
"`kivi.binning.bin_edges`."
msgstr "如果 `bins` 是整数，且相同评分使评分段少于请求的数量，与 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` 相同。"

msgid "The largest gap over all scores rather than band edges."
msgstr "在全部评分上而非仅在分段边界上取的最大差距。"

msgid "Ranking quality over all pairs of events and non-events."
msgstr "在全部事件与非事件配对上衡量的排序质量。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.binning.bin_edges`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.binning.bin_edges`"

msgid "Fit band edges on a development sample."
msgstr "在开发样本上拟合分段边界。"

msgid ""
"Bands are intervals closed on the right, as in ``pandas.cut``, so tied scores always share a "
"band. Every band is reported, including bands without observations, so samples cut on the same "
"edges give tables with the same rows. An empty band has a NaN ``event_rate`` and ``lift``, and "
"``cum_lift`` is NaN until the first band with observations."
msgstr ""
"评分段是右闭区间，与 ``pandas.cut`` 相同，因此相同评分总在同一段。结果列出每个评分段，包括没有观测的评分段，因此用相同边界切分的样本得到的表行相同。空评分段的 "
"``event_rate`` 和 ``lift`` 为 NaN，在第一个有观测的评分段之前 ``cum_lift`` 也为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"``non_event``, ``event`` and ``total``: non-events, events and all observations in the band, or "
"the sums of their weights;"
msgstr "``non_event``、``event`` 和 ``total``：该段的非事件数、事件数和总观测数，或者它们的权重之和；"

msgid "``event_rate``: ``event`` divided by ``total``;"
msgstr "``event_rate``：``event`` 除以 ``total``；"

msgid "``lift``: ``event_rate`` divided by the event rate of the sample;"
msgstr "``lift``：``event_rate`` 除以整个样本的事件率；"

msgid ""
"``cum_non_event_share``, ``cum_event_share`` and ``cum_total_share``: shares of all non-events, "
"events and observations in the band and the bands above it;"
msgstr "``cum_non_event_share``、``cum_event_share`` 和 ``cum_total_share``：该段及其以上各段占全部非事件、事件和观测的比例；"

msgid "``ks``: the absolute difference between ``cum_event_share`` and ``cum_non_event_share``;"
msgstr "``ks``：``cum_event_share`` 与 ``cum_non_event_share`` 之差的绝对值；"

msgid "``cum_lift``: ``cum_event_share`` divided by ``cum_total_share``."
msgstr "``cum_lift``：``cum_event_share`` 除以 ``cum_total_share``。"

msgid ""
"The largest ``ks`` is at most the value of `ks`, and the two are equal when each distinct score "
"forms its own band."
msgstr "``ks`` 列的最大值不超过 `ks` 的结果；当每个不同的评分各自成段时，二者相等。"

msgid ""
"The Brier score is the mean squared difference between the predicted probability and the observed"
" outcome, so a lower value is better."
msgstr "Brier 分数是预测概率与观测结果之差的平方的均值，因此越低越好。"

msgid ""
"The probabilities come first and the target second, as in `kivi.woe.woe_table`; scikit-learn's "
"metrics take the target first."
msgstr "概率在前、目标在后，与 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 相同；scikit-learn 的指标函数则把目标放在前面。"

msgid "Predicted event probabilities from 0 to 1."
msgstr "预测的事件概率，取值 0 到 1。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event. If `probability` and `target` are both pandas Series,"
" they must have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by position."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件。如果 `probability` 和 `target` 都是 pandas Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, matched like `target`. The score is then the weighted "
"mean of the squared differences."
msgstr "每个观测的非负权重，对应方式与 `target` 相同。此时 Brier 分数为平方差的加权平均。"

msgid "The Brier score, from 0 for perfect forecasts to 1."
msgstr "Brier 分数，取值从 0（完美预测）到 1。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` "
"has a label other than 0 and 1, or `probability` is not real and numeric or has a missing value "
"or a value outside 0 to 1. Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one "
"finite, non-negative weight with a positive total, or has an index other than that of "
"`probability`."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，索引或长度不一致，`target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签，或 `probability` 不是实数数值、含有缺失值或含有 0 到 1 以外的值。此外，如果 "
"`weights` 不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负且总和为正的权重，或者索引与 `probability` 不同。"

msgid "Ranking quality, which ignores the probability scale."
msgstr "排序质量，与概率的尺度无关。"

msgid "For outcomes :math:`y_i` and probabilities :math:`p_i`,"
msgstr "对结果 :math:`y_i` 和概率 :math:`p_i`，"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{BS} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (p_i - y_i)^2,"
msgstr "\\mathrm{BS} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (p_i - y_i)^2,"

msgid "or :math:`\\sum_i w_i (p_i - y_i)^2 / \\sum_i w_i` with weights."
msgstr "使用权重时则为 :math:`\\sum_i w_i (p_i - y_i)^2 / \\sum_i w_i` 。"

msgid ""
"Unlike the ranking measures, the Brier score depends on the probability values themselves, so it "
"rewards calibration, and it is defined even when the sample has only one class. Predicting the "
"event rate :math:`\\bar y` for everyone scores :math:`\\bar y (1 - \\bar y)`, a useful baseline."
msgstr ""
"与排序度量不同，Brier 分数取决于概率值本身，因此会奖励校准良好的预测，并且在样本只有一个类别时也有定义。对所有人都预测事件率 :math:`\\bar y` 的得分为 "
":math:`\\bar y (1 - \\bar y)`，可作为有用的基准。"

msgid ""
"G. W. Brier, \"Verification of forecasts expressed in terms of probability\", Monthly Weather "
"Review, 78(1), pp. 1-3, 1950."
msgstr ""
"G. W. Brier, \"Verification of forecasts expressed in terms of probability\", Monthly Weather "
"Review, 78(1), pp. 1-3, 1950."

msgid "[R88e41552d980-1]_"
msgstr "[R88e41552d980-1]_"

msgid "Model monitoring"
msgstr "模型监控"

msgid ""
"Track a score and its variables period by period. :func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` gives"
" the population, the events, the discrimination and the PSI of a score in every period, and "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` the PSI of every grouped variable."
msgstr ""
"按期跟踪评分及其变量。 :func:`~kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table` 给出评分在每一期的样本量、事件、区分能力和 PSI， "
":func:`~kivi.monitoring.stability_table` 给出每个已分组变量的 PSI。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/monitoring` for examples on synthetic applications."
msgstr "基于合成申请数据的示例见 :doc:`/user_guide/monitoring` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`monitoring_table <kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table>`\\ \\(score\\, period\\[\\, "
"target\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`monitoring_table <kivi.monitoring.monitoring_table>`\\ \\(score\\, period\\[\\, "
"target\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Monitor the population, event rate, discrimination and stability of a score."
msgstr "监控评分的样本量、事件率、区分能力和稳定性。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`stability_table <kivi.monitoring.stability_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, period\\, \\*\\, "
"reference\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`stability_table <kivi.monitoring.stability_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, period\\, \\*\\, "
"reference\\)"

msgid "Monitor the population stability of grouped variables over time."
msgstr "按期监控已分组变量的群体稳定性。"

msgid ""
"Each row summarizes one period, such as a month or a quarter: how many observations it has, how "
"many events among those with a known outcome, how well the score separates the two classes and "
"how far the distribution of the score has moved from a reference sample."
msgstr "每行汇总一期，例如一个月或一个季度：该期有多少观测、结果已知的观测中有多少事件、评分区分两类结果的能力如何，以及评分分布相对基准样本偏移了多少。"

msgid ""
"Finite numeric scores that are higher for a higher event probability, such as a PD. Negate "
"scorecard points, which are higher for a lower risk."
msgstr "有限的数值评分，事件概率越高，评分越高，例如 PD。评分卡分数越高表示风险越低，因此须取负后再传入。"

msgid "**period**"
msgstr "**period**"

msgid ""
"Period of each observation, such as the month of application, without missing values. Periods are"
" sorted, and categorical periods follow the order of their categories. If `score` and `period` "
"are both pandas Series, they must have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by position."
msgstr ""
"每个观测所属的期，例如申请月份，不能有缺失值。各期按排序排列，分类型的期按类别顺序排列。如果 `score` 和 `period` 都是 pandas "
"Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event, and missing values for outcomes that are not known "
"yet, such as those of loans that have not reached the end of the outcome window, matched like "
"`period`. Without `target`, every outcome is unknown and the table only has the columns ``total``"
" and ``psi``."
msgstr ""
"二元标签，1 表示事件；结果尚未得知时为缺失值，例如尚未走完表现期的贷款，对应方式与 `period` 相同。不给出 `target` 时，所有结果都视为未知，表中只有 ``total`` 和 "
"``psi`` 两列。"

msgid "**reference**"
msgstr "**reference**"

msgid "scalar, tuple or array_like"
msgstr "标量、元组或 array_like"

msgid ""
"The sample that the distribution of each period is compared with: either the label of one period,"
" such as the first month after the development sample, or the scores of a reference sample, such "
"as the development sample itself, as a list, an array or a Series. A string that names one period"
" of datetime periods, such as ``\"2024-01\"`` for monthly dates, selects that period."
msgstr ""
"与每一期的分布作比较的样本：可以是某一期的标签，例如开发样本之后的第一个月；也可以是基准样本的评分，例如开发样本本身，以列表、数组或 Series "
"传入。如果各期是日期时间，指向其中一期的字符串（例如月度日期的 ``\"2024-01\"`` ）会选中该期。"

msgid ""
"Number of quantile bands of the reference scores, or increasing band edges. An integer is the "
"same as passing ``kivi.binning.bin_edges(reference_score, bins=bins)``, with the weights of the "
"reference as ``weights``, so tied scores can leave fewer bands than requested. Every period is "
"compared on the same bands."
msgstr ""
"基准评分的分位数评分段个数，或递增的评分段边界。整数等同于传入 ``kivi.binning.bin_edges(reference_score, bins=bins)`` "
"，并以基准样本的权重作为 ``weights`` ，因此并列的评分可能使评分段少于请求的数量。每一期都在同一组评分段上比较。"

msgid ""
"Positive replacement for a zero count when calculating the PSI, as in `kivi.stability.psi_table`,"
" in units of weight with `weights`."
msgstr "计算 PSI 时用这个正数替代零计数，含义与 `kivi.stability.psi_table` 相同；给出 `weights` 时以权重为单位。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, such as the inverse of its sampling rate, matched like "
"`period`. Counts become sums of weights, and the discrimination and the PSI are weighted. On the "
"same band edges, integer weights give the same table as repeating rows."
msgstr "每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `period` 相同。计数变为权重之和，区分能力和 PSI 也按权重计算。在相同的评分段边界上，整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同。"

msgid "**reference_weights**"
msgstr "**reference_weights**"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation of a reference sample passed as `reference`, matched like"
" the sample. A reference period takes its weights from `weights`."
msgstr "作为 `reference` 传入的基准样本中每个观测的非负权重，对应方式与该样本相同。基准期的权重取自 `weights` 。"

msgid "One row per period, indexed by ``period``, with the columns described in the Notes."
msgstr "每期一行，索引名为 ``period`` ，各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If `score` or `period` is empty, an input is not one-dimensional, the inputs have different "
"lengths or are Series with different indices, `score` is not real and numeric or has a missing or"
" infinite value, `target` has a value other than 0, 1 and missing, or `period` has a missing "
"value. Also if `reference` is neither a period of `period` with observations nor a non-empty "
"sample of finite scores, `reference_weights` is given with a reference period, `bins` is neither "
"a positive integer nor increasing edges, a score lies outside the edges, `smoothing` is not "
"finite and positive, or a weight array is not numeric, does not give each observation one finite,"
" non-negative weight with a positive total, or has an index other than that of its sample."
msgstr ""
"如果 `score` 或 `period` 为空，某个输入不是一维的，输入长度不同或是索引不同的 Series， `score` 不是实数型数值或含有缺失值或无穷值， `target` 含有 "
"0、1 和缺失值以外的值，或 `period` 含有缺失值。此外，如果 `reference` 既不是 `period` 中有观测的某一期，也不是由有限评分组成的非空样本，给出基准期的同时给出了"
" `reference_weights` ， `bins` 既不是正整数也不是递增边界，某个评分落在边界之外， `smoothing` "
"不是有限正数，或者某个权重数组不是数值型、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负且总和为正的权重，或其索引与对应样本的索引不同。"

msgid ""
"If `bins` is an integer and tied reference scores leave fewer bands than requested, as in "
"`kivi.binning.bin_edges`."
msgstr "如果 `bins` 是整数，且并列的基准评分使评分段少于请求的数量，与 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` 相同。"

msgid ":obj:`stability_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`stability_table`"

msgid "The PSI of each variable of the score in each period."
msgstr "评分各变量在每一期的 PSI。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.metrics.roc_auc`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.metrics.roc_auc`"

msgid "The AUC of one sample."
msgstr "单个样本的 AUC。"

msgid "The PSI of one sample and its contributions."
msgstr "单个样本的 PSI 及各组贡献。"

msgid ""
"``total``: observations in the period, or the sum of their weights, including those whose outcome"
" is not known yet;"
msgstr "``total`` ：该期的观测数或其权重之和，包括结果尚未得知的观测；"

msgid "``known``: observations with a known outcome;"
msgstr "``known`` ：结果已知的观测数；"

msgid "``event``: events among them;"
msgstr "``event`` ：其中的事件数；"

msgid "``event_rate``: ``event`` divided by ``known``, NaN without known outcomes;"
msgstr "``event_rate`` ： ``event`` 除以 ``known`` ，没有已知结果时为 NaN；"

msgid ""
"``auc``, ``gini`` and ``ks``: `kivi.metrics.roc_auc`, `kivi.metrics.gini` and `kivi.metrics.ks` "
"of the known outcomes of the period, NaN unless both classes are present;"
msgstr ""
"``auc`` 、 ``gini`` 和 ``ks`` ：该期已知结果的 `kivi.metrics.roc_auc` 、 `kivi.metrics.gini` 和 "
"`kivi.metrics.ks` ，两类结果不全时为 NaN；"

msgid ""
"``psi``: the population stability index of the period's scores against the reference scores, on "
"the bands described under `bins`."
msgstr "``psi`` ：该期评分相对基准评分的群体稳定性指标，基于 `bins` 所描述的评分段。"

msgid ""
"Without a target the columns are ``total`` and ``psi``. Each row equals what the metric functions"
" and ``psi_table(pandas.cut(reference_score, edges), pandas.cut(period_score, edges))`` give for "
"the period alone, with the weights of the two samples as ``reference_weights`` and "
"``current_weights``. For a band :math:`i` with shares :math:`q_i` of the reference scores and "
":math:`p_i` of the period's scores, after smoothing,"
msgstr ""
"没有目标变量时，表中只有 ``total`` 和 ``psi`` 两列。每一行都等于仅对该期计算时指标函数和 ``psi_table(pandas.cut(reference_score, "
"edges), pandas.cut(period_score, edges))`` 的结果，两个样本的权重分别作为 ``reference_weights`` 和 "
"``current_weights`` 传入。记 :math:`q_i` 和 :math:`p_i` 为评分段 :math:`i` 在基准评分和该期评分中平滑后的占比，则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{PSI} = \\sum_i (p_i - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i},"
msgstr "\\mathrm{PSI} = \\sum_i (p_i - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i},"

msgid ""
"where bands empty in both samples are left out. The reference period, if `reference` names one, "
"has a PSI of 0."
msgstr "其中两个样本中都为空的评分段不计入。如果 `reference` 指向某一期，该基准期的 PSI 为 0。"

msgid ""
"A period of a categorical `period` without observations, or whose weights sum to zero, keeps its "
"row with zero counts and NaN in the other columns, so that tables of different samples line up. "
"Other periods exist only through their observations, and those whose weights sum to zero are left"
" out, as repeated rows would leave them out."
msgstr "分类型 `period` 中没有观测或权重之和为零的期仍保留一行，计数为零，其他列为 NaN，以便不同样本的表能够对齐。其他类型的期只由其观测产生，权重之和为零的期会被排除，与重复相应行时一样。"

msgid ""
"The discrimination of the most recent periods usually rests on few known outcomes, and the PSI of"
" a small period mostly reflects sampling noise, so read both together with ``known`` and "
"``total``."
msgstr "最近几期的区分能力通常只基于很少的已知结果，而小样本期的 PSI 主要反映抽样噪声，因此应结合 ``known`` 和 ``total`` 一起解读。"

msgid ""
"The March outcomes of two observations are not known yet, so its discrimination rests on the "
"other two."
msgstr "3 月有两个观测的结果尚未得知，因此其区分能力只基于另外两个。"

msgid ""
"Each entry is the PSI of one variable in one period against a reference sample, as "
"`kivi.stability.psi_table` computes it for the period alone. With the groups of a scorecard's "
"variables this is the variable part of a stability report, and the variables that move explain a "
"shift of the score that `monitoring_table` shows."
msgstr ""
"每个值是某个变量在某一期相对基准样本的 PSI，与 `kivi.stability.psi_table` "
"仅对该期计算的结果相同。对评分卡各变量的分组而言，这就是稳定性报告中的变量部分，发生变化的变量可以解释 `monitoring_table` 所显示的评分偏移。"

msgid ""
"One column per variable, holding labels or values binned using the same edges in every period, "
"such as the result of ``kivi.spec.BinningSpec.cut``. Missing values form a group, and groups "
"observed in only one sample are included."
msgstr "每个变量一列，存放标签或在每一期都使用相同边界分箱后的值，例如 ``kivi.spec.BinningSpec.cut`` 的结果。缺失值单独成组，只在一个样本中出现的组也会包含在内。"

msgid ""
"Period of each row of `groups`, without missing values. Periods are sorted, and categorical "
"periods follow the order of their categories. A Series must have the index of `groups`."
msgstr "`groups` 每一行所属的期，不能有缺失值。各期按排序排列，分类型的期按类别顺序排列。Series 的索引必须与 `groups` 相同。"

msgid "scalar, tuple or pandas.DataFrame"
msgstr "标量、元组或 pandas.DataFrame"

msgid ""
"The sample that each period is compared with: either the label of one period, as for "
"`monitoring_table`, or the groups of a reference sample, such as the development sample, with "
"every column of `groups`. Other columns of a reference DataFrame are ignored."
msgstr ""
"与每一期作比较的样本：可以是某一期的标签，与 `monitoring_table` 相同；也可以是基准样本（例如开发样本）的分组，须包含 `groups` 的每一列。基准 DataFrame "
"的其他列会被忽略。"

msgid "Positive replacement for a zero count when calculating shares, in units of weight with `weights`."
msgstr "计算占比时用这个正数替代零计数；给出 `weights` 时以权重为单位。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each row of `groups`, matched like `period`. Counts become sums of "
"weights, so integer weights give the same table as repeating rows."
msgstr "`groups` 每一行的非负权重，对应方式与 `period` 相同。计数变为权重之和，因此整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each row of a reference sample passed as `reference`. A reference period "
"takes its weights from `weights`."
msgstr "作为 `reference` 传入的基准样本中每一行的非负权重。基准期的权重取自 `weights` 。"

msgid ""
"One row per period, indexed by ``period``, and one column per variable, with the columns of "
"`groups` and the column index named ``variable``. Each entry is the PSI of the variable in the "
"period."
msgstr "每期一行，索引名为 ``period`` ；每个变量一列，列与 `groups` 的列相同，列索引名为 ``variable`` 。每个值是该变量在该期的 PSI。"

msgid ""
"If `groups` is not a DataFrame, has no rows, no columns, repeated column names or more than one "
"level of column names, `period` is not one-dimensional, does not have one value per row or has a "
"missing value, or a Series argument has an index other than that of `groups`. Also if `reference`"
" is neither a period of `period` with observations nor a non-empty DataFrame with every column of"
" `groups`, `reference_weights` is given with a reference period, `smoothing` is not finite and "
"positive, or a weight array is not numeric, does not give each row one finite, non-negative "
"weight with a positive total, or has an index other than that of its sample."
msgstr ""
"如果 `groups` 不是 DataFrame，没有行、没有列、列名重复或列名不止一层， `period` 不是一维的、不是每行一个值或含有缺失值，或某个 Series 参数的索引与 "
"`groups` 的索引不同。此外，如果 `reference` 既不是 `period` 中有观测的某一期，也不是包含 `groups` 每一列的非空 "
"DataFrame，给出基准期的同时给出了 `reference_weights` ， `smoothing` "
"不是有限正数，或者某个权重数组不是数值型、没有为每一行给出一个有限非负且总和为正的权重，或其索引与对应样本的索引不同。"

msgid ":obj:`monitoring_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`monitoring_table`"

msgid "The population, discrimination and PSI of the score."
msgstr "评分的样本量、区分能力和 PSI。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.stability.csi_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.stability.csi_table`"

msgid "The change of a variable's average points."
msgstr "变量平均分值的变化。"

msgid ""
"For a group :math:`i` of a variable, with shares :math:`q_i` of the reference sample and "
":math:`p_i` of the period, after smoothing,"
msgstr "对变量的第 :math:`i` 组，记 :math:`q_i` 和 :math:`p_i` 为其在基准样本和该期中平滑后的占比，则"

msgid ""
"over the groups observed in the reference sample or in the period. The reference period, if "
"`reference` names one, has a PSI of 0."
msgstr "求和范围为在基准样本或该期中出现的组。如果 `reference` 指向某一期，该基准期的 PSI 为 0。"

msgid ""
"A period of a categorical `period` without observations, or whose weights sum to zero, keeps its "
"row with NaN entries. Other periods exist only through their rows, and those whose weights sum to"
" zero are left out, as repeated rows would leave them out."
msgstr "分类型 `period` 中没有观测或权重之和为零的期仍保留一行，其值为 NaN。其他类型的期只由其行产生，权重之和为零的期会被排除，与重复相应行时一样。"

msgid "One value of the February region is missing, a group that January does not have."
msgstr "2 月有一个 region 值缺失，这是 1 月没有的一组。"

msgid ""
"Supply outcomes for rejected applicants, so that a model developed on the approved applicants can"
" be refitted on all of them. :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation` and "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling` return inferred rows with weights, and "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` returns weights for the approved applicants."
msgstr ""
"为被拒绝的申请人补充结果，从而可以把在获批申请人上开发的模型在全部申请人上重新拟合。 :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.reject_inference.parceling` 返回带权重的推断行， :func:`~kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` "
"返回获批申请人的权重。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference` for a comparison of the methods on synthetic applications."
msgstr "各方法在合成申请数据上的比较见 :doc:`/user_guide/reject_inference` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`fuzzy_augmentation <kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation>`\\ \\(probability\\, "
"\\*\\[\\, factor\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`fuzzy_augmentation <kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation>`\\ \\(probability\\, "
"\\*\\[\\, factor\\]\\)"

msgid "Split each rejected applicant into a bad and a good row with fractional weights."
msgstr "把每个拒绝申请人拆成带小数权重的一行坏样本和一行好样本。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`parceling <kivi.reject_inference.parceling>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, reject\\_score\\, "
"\\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`parceling <kivi.reject_inference.parceling>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, reject\\_score\\, "
"\\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Label rejected applicants bad or good at the bad rate of their score band."
msgstr "按所在评分段的坏账率把拒绝申请人标记为坏或好。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`reweighting <kivi.reject_inference.reweighting>`\\ \\(score\\, reject\\_score\\, "
"\\*\\[\\, bins\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`reweighting <kivi.reject_inference.reweighting>`\\ \\(score\\, reject\\_score\\, "
"\\*\\[\\, bins\\]\\)"

msgid "Weight accepted applicants to stand in for the rejected applicants of their score band."
msgstr "给获批申请人加权，使其代表同一评分段的拒绝申请人。"

msgid ""
"The PD of a reject under the model fitted on the accepted applicants alone gives the weight of "
"its bad row, and the rest of its weight of 1 goes to its good row. Concatenate the rows with the "
"accepted applicants at weight 1 and refit the model with weights."
msgstr "拒绝申请人在仅用获批申请人拟合的模型下的 PD 作为其坏样本行的权重，总权重 1 的其余部分归其好样本行。把这些行与权重为 1 的获批申请人拼接起来，再带权重重新拟合模型。"

msgid "PD of each rejected applicant under the accepts-only model, between 0 and 1."
msgstr "每个拒绝申请人在仅用通过样本拟合的模型下的 PD，介于 0 和 1 之间。"

msgid "**factor**"
msgstr "**factor**"

msgid "float, default 1"
msgstr "float，默认 1"

msgid ""
"Positive multiplier of the PDs. A factor above 1 assumes that the rejects are riskier than "
"accepted applicants with the same PD, as when the approval used information that the model does "
"not have."
msgstr "PD 的正乘数。大于 1 的倍数假定拒绝样本比 PD 相同的获批申请人风险更高，例如审批时用到了模型所没有的信息。"

msgid ""
"Two rows per rejected applicant, the bad row first, with the columns ``target``, 1 and then 0, "
"and ``weight``, the PD times `factor` clipped to [0, 1] and its complement. The index repeats the"
" index of `probability`, or its positions when it is not a Series. When `probability` is a Series"
" with the unique index of the rejects, ``rejects.loc[result.index]`` gives the features of every "
"row."
msgstr ""
"每个拒绝申请人两行，坏样本行在前，列为 ``target`` （先 1 后 0）和 ``weight`` （PD 乘以 `factor` 后截断到 [0, 1] 的值及其补数）。索引重复 "
"`probability` 的索引，不是 Series 时重复其位置。当 `probability` 是索引与拒绝样本相同且不重复的 Series 时， "
"``rejects.loc[result.index]`` 给出每一行的特征。"

msgid ""
"If `probability` is empty, not one-dimensional or not numeric, or has a value that is missing or "
"outside [0, 1]; or if `factor` is not a positive finite number."
msgstr "如果 `probability` 为空、不是一维或不是数值，或有缺失值或位于 [0, 1] 之外的值；或者 `factor` 不是有限正数。"

msgid ":obj:`parceling`"
msgstr ":obj:`parceling`"

msgid "Infer the outcomes from the bad rate of a score band."
msgstr "根据评分段的坏账率推断结果。"

msgid ":obj:`reweighting`"
msgstr ":obj:`reweighting`"

msgid "Weight the accepted applicants instead."
msgstr "改为给获批申请人加权。"

msgid "Refit the model with ``weights``."
msgstr "用 ``weights`` 重新拟合模型。"

msgid "A reject with PD :math:`p` and the factor :math:`k` gets the rows"
msgstr "PD 为 :math:`p` 、倍数为 :math:`k` 的拒绝申请人得到以下两行"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"(y = 1,\\ w = \\min(k p, 1)) \\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n"
"(y = 0,\\ w = 1 - \\min(k p, 1))."
msgstr ""
"(y = 1,\\ w = \\min(k p, 1)) \\quad \\text{和} \\quad\n"
"(y = 0,\\ w = 1 - \\min(k p, 1))."

msgid ""
"Clipping keeps both weights in [0, 1]: when :math:`k p \\ge 1`, the reject counts as bad with its"
" whole weight and its good row has weight 0, which kivi's ``weights`` arguments ignore. Each "
"reject keeps a total weight of 1, so the weighted bad rate of its rows is the mean of "
":math:`\\min(k p_i, 1)`."
msgstr ""
"截断使两个权重都在 [0, 1] 之内：当 :math:`k p \\ge 1` 时，拒绝申请人以全部权重计为坏样本，其好样本行的权重为 0，kivi 的 ``weights`` "
"参数会忽略这样的行。每个拒绝申请人的总权重保持为 1，因此这些行的加权坏账率是 :math:`\\min(k p_i, 1)` 的均值。"

msgid ""
"With ``factor=1``, refitting the same logistic regression on the same encoding returns the "
"coefficients of the accepts-only model exactly: at those coefficients, the weight of each "
"reject's bad row equals its fitted PD, so the inferred rows leave the score equations unchanged. "
"The refit only narrows the standard errors, although the inferred rows add no information: with "
"these weights, the standard errors of `kivi.selection.logistic_regression` are too small. The "
"model changes only with a factor other than 1, with another encoding, such as WOE refitted on the"
" augmented sample, or with other variables."
msgstr ""
"当 ``factor=1`` 时，在同一编码上重新拟合同一个逻辑回归，得到的恰好是仅用通过样本拟合的模型的系数：在这组系数下，每个拒绝申请人坏样本行的权重等于其拟合 "
"PD，因此推断出的行不改变得分方程。重新拟合只会缩小标准误，尽管推断出的行并没有增加任何信息：在这样的权重下， `kivi.selection.logistic_regression` "
"的标准误偏小。只有倍数不为 1、换用其他编码（例如在扩充后的样本上重新拟合 WOE）或换用其他变量时，模型才会改变。"

msgid ""
"N. Siddiqi, \"Credit Risk Scorecards: Developing and Implementing Intelligent Credit Scoring\", "
"Wiley, 2006."
msgstr ""
"N. Siddiqi, \"Credit Risk Scorecards: Developing and Implementing Intelligent Credit Scoring\", "
"Wiley, 2006."

msgid "[R163332bd4527-1]_"
msgstr "[R163332bd4527-1]_"

msgid ""
"The scores of the accepted and the rejected applicants are divided into bands. In each band, the "
"bad rate of the rejects is `factor` times the observed bad rate of the accepted applicants, at "
"most 1, and that share of the band's rejects, chosen at random, is labelled bad."
msgstr "把获批申请人和拒绝申请人的评分划分为若干评分段。在每个评分段内，拒绝样本的坏账率为获批申请人观测坏账率的 `factor` 倍（最多为 1），并随机选取该比例的拒绝样本标记为坏。"

msgid ""
"Finite numeric scores of the accepted applicants, such as their PD under the accepts-only model. "
"The direction does not matter."
msgstr "获批申请人的有限数值评分，例如其在仅用通过样本拟合的模型下的 PD。方向无关紧要。"

msgid ""
"Observed outcomes of the accepted applicants, 1 for bad and 0 for good, with both present. If "
"`score` and `target` are both pandas Series, they must have identical indices; otherwise they are"
" matched by position."
msgstr "获批申请人观测到的结果，1 表示坏、0 表示好，两者都必须出现。如果 `score` 和 `target` 都是 pandas Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid "**reject_score**"
msgstr "**reject_score**"

msgid "Finite numeric scores of the rejected applicants, on the scale of `score`."
msgstr "拒绝申请人的有限数值评分，与 `score` 的尺度相同。"

msgid ""
"Number of quantile bands, fitted with `kivi.binning.bin_edges` on the scores of accepted and "
"rejected applicants together, so tied scores can leave fewer bands; or increasing band edges, "
"closed on the right, that hold every score."
msgstr "分位数评分段的个数，由 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` 在获批和拒绝申请人的评分合并后拟合，因此评分并列时评分段可能更少；或者递增的右闭评分段边界，须包含所有评分。"

msgid ""
"Positive multiplier of the accepted applicants' bad rate in each band. A factor above 1 assumes "
"that the rejects are riskier than accepted applicants with the same score."
msgstr "各评分段内获批申请人坏账率的正乘数。大于 1 的倍数假定拒绝样本比评分相同的获批申请人风险更高。"

msgid "**expected**"
msgstr "**expected**"

msgid ""
"Return two rows per reject, weighted with the band's inferred bad rate and its complement as in "
"`fuzzy_augmentation`, instead of a random label."
msgstr "每个拒绝申请人返回两行，像 `fuzzy_augmentation` 那样以该评分段推断的坏账率及其补数为权重，而不是随机标签。"

msgid ""
"Seed or generator passed to `numpy.random.default_rng` to draw the labels. The global NumPy "
"random state is not used, so the same seed gives the same labels. Not used with "
"``expected=True``."
msgstr ""
"传给 `numpy.random.default_rng` 、用于抽取标签的种子或生成器。不使用 NumPy 的全局随机状态，因此同一个种子总是给出同样的标签。 "
"``expected=True`` 时不使用。"

msgid ""
"The columns ``target`` and ``weight``, indexed like `reject_score`, or by position when it is not"
" a Series. One row per rejected applicant with its label and the weight 1, or, with "
"``expected=True``, two rows per rejected applicant as returned by `fuzzy_augmentation`."
msgstr ""
"包含 ``target`` 和 ``weight`` 两列，索引与 `reject_score` 相同（不是 Series 时为位置）。每个拒绝申请人一行，带其标签和权重 1；或者在 "
"``expected=True`` 时，每个拒绝申请人两行，与 `fuzzy_augmentation` 的返回值相同。"

msgid ""
"If `score` and `target` are invalid as for `kivi.metrics.gains_table`; if `reject_score` is "
"empty, not one-dimensional or not numeric, or has a missing or infinite value; if `bins` is "
"neither a positive integer nor at least two increasing edges, or a score lies outside the edges; "
"if a band holds rejected applicants but no accepted one, so that its bad rate is unknown; or if "
"`factor` is not a positive finite number or `expected` is not a boolean."
msgstr ""
"如果 `score` 和 `target` 不符合 `kivi.metrics.gains_table` 的要求；如果 `reject_score` "
"为空、不是一维或不是数值，或含有缺失值或无穷值；如果 `bins` "
"既不是正整数，也不是至少两个递增的边界，或者有评分落在边界之外；如果某个评分段有拒绝申请人却没有获批申请人，因而其坏账率未知；或者 `factor` 不是有限正数，或 `expected` "
"不是布尔值。"

msgid "If tied scores leave fewer quantile bands than `bins`."
msgstr "如果评分并列使分位数评分段少于 `bins` 。"

msgid ":obj:`fuzzy_augmentation`"
msgstr ":obj:`fuzzy_augmentation`"

msgid "Infer the outcomes from each reject's own PD."
msgstr "根据每个拒绝申请人自己的 PD 推断结果。"

msgid "Weight the accepted applicants of each band instead."
msgstr "改为给各评分段的获批申请人加权。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.metrics.gains_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.metrics.gains_table`"

msgid "Bad rates by score band."
msgstr "各评分段的坏账率。"

msgid ""
"In a band with :math:`a` accepted applicants of whom :math:`b` are bad, and :math:`n` rejects, "
"the inferred bad rate is :math:`r = \\min(k b / a, 1)` for the factor :math:`k`. The number of "
"bad rejects is :math:`r n` rounded down or up at random, up with a probability equal to its "
"fractional part, so it is :math:`r n` on average and never further from it than 1. With "
"``expected=True``, each reject instead gets a bad row with the weight :math:`r` and a good row "
"with :math:`1 - r`, which removes the noise of the draw."
msgstr ""
"若一个评分段有 :math:`a` 个获批申请人（其中 :math:`b` 个为坏）和 :math:`n` 个拒绝申请人，则倍数为 :math:`k` 时推断的坏账率为 :math:`r = "
"\\min(k b / a, 1)` 。坏的拒绝申请人个数为 :math:`r n` 随机向下或向上取整，向上取整的概率等于其小数部分，因此平均为 :math:`r n` ，且与之相差从不超过 "
"1。 ``expected=True`` 时，每个拒绝申请人改为得到权重为 :math:`r` 的坏样本行和权重为 :math:`1 - r` 的好样本行，从而消除抽样噪声。"

msgid ""
"Parceling uses the score only: within a band, it treats every reject alike, whatever its "
"features. A reject's inferred bad rate depends on the accepted applicants of its band, which are "
"few in the bands where the approval rate is low."
msgstr "打包法只使用评分：在一个评分段内，它对每个拒绝申请人一视同仁，不论其特征如何。拒绝申请人推断的坏账率取决于其所在评分段的获批申请人，而在通过率低的评分段里，获批申请人很少。"

msgid "[Rc29e884af050-1]_"
msgstr "[Rc29e884af050-1]_"

msgid ""
"The accepted applicants have the bad rate 1/4 in the low band and 3/4 in the high band. Three of "
"the four rejects of the high band are therefore labelled bad, and the one reject of the low band "
"is bad with the probability 1/4:"
msgstr "获批申请人在低评分段的坏账率为 1/4，在高评分段为 3/4。因此高评分段的四个拒绝申请人中有三个被标记为坏，低评分段唯一的拒绝申请人以 1/4 的概率为坏："

msgid ""
"With ``expected=True``, every reject instead gets the bad rate of its band as the weight of its "
"bad row:"
msgstr "``expected=True`` 时，每个拒绝申请人改为以所在评分段的坏账率作为其坏样本行的权重："

msgid ""
"In each band of the score, every accepted applicant gets the weight (accepted + rejected) / "
"accepted, the inverse of the band's approval rate. The weighted accepted applicants then add up "
"to all the applicants of their band, so a model refitted with these weights gives each band its "
"share of the applicant population."
msgstr ""
"在每个评分段内，每个获批申请人得到权重（获批 + 拒绝）/ "
"获批，即该评分段通过率的倒数。加权后的获批申请人合计等于该评分段的全部申请人，因此用这些权重重新拟合的模型让每个评分段占有其在申请人总体中的份额。"

msgid ""
"Weight of each accepted applicant, at least 1. A Series named ``weight`` with the index of "
"`score` when `score` is a Series, otherwise an array."
msgstr "每个获批申请人的权重，至少为 1。 `score` 是 Series 时返回名为 ``weight`` 、索引与 `score` 相同的 Series，否则返回数组。"

msgid ""
"If `score` or `reject_score` is empty, not one-dimensional or not numeric, or has a missing or "
"infinite value; if `bins` is neither a positive integer nor at least two increasing edges, or a "
"score lies outside the edges; or if a band holds rejected applicants but no accepted one."
msgstr ""
"如果 `score` 或 `reject_score` 为空、不是一维或不是数值，或含有缺失值或无穷值；如果 `bins` "
"既不是正整数，也不是至少两个递增的边界，或者有评分落在边界之外；或者某个评分段有拒绝申请人却没有获批申请人。"

msgid "Infer outcomes for the rejects instead."
msgstr "改为推断拒绝样本的结果。"

msgid "Label the rejects of each band at its bad rate."
msgstr "按各评分段的坏账率标记其中的拒绝样本。"

msgid ""
"With :math:`a` accepted and :math:`n` rejected applicants in a band, each accepted applicant of "
"the band gets the weight"
msgstr "若一个评分段有 :math:`a` 个获批申请人和 :math:`n` 个拒绝申请人，该评分段的每个获批申请人得到权重"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "w = \\frac{a + n}{a}."
msgstr "w = \\frac{a + n}{a}."

msgid ""
"Reweighting assumes that, within a band, the rejects default like the accepted applicants. It "
"changes how much each band weighs in the fit, but adds no outcomes, so the rejects are predicted "
"to be as risky as accepted applicants with the same score. It cannot represent applicants that no"
" accepted applicant resembles: a band of rejects without accepted applicants raises an error. "
"Bands of a score that decided the approval with a hard cut-off have no accepted applicants beyond"
" the cut-off, so use a score on which accepted and rejected applicants overlap, such as the PD of"
" the accepts-only model."
msgstr ""
"重新加权假定在一个评分段内，拒绝样本与获批申请人的违约情况相同。它改变各评分段在拟合中的分量，但不增加任何结果，因此拒绝样本被预测为与评分相同的获批申请人风险相当。它无法代表与任何获批申请人都不相似的申请人：只有拒绝样本而没有获批申请人的评分段会引发错误。若某个评分以硬截断决定审批，按它划分的评分段在截断点以外没有获批申请人，因此应使用获批与拒绝申请人有重叠的评分，例如仅用通过样本拟合的模型的"
" PD。"

msgid ""
"The weights add up to more than the number of accepted applicants, so the standard errors of a "
"fit with them are too small, as if the outcomes of all applicants had been observed."
msgstr "这些权重之和大于获批申请人的个数，因此用它们拟合得到的标准误偏小，就好像所有申请人的结果都被观测到了一样。"

msgid "[R0bbcb3cec2a1-1]_"
msgstr "[R0bbcb3cec2a1-1]_"

msgid "The low band has 4 accepted applicants and 1 reject, the high band 2 and 4:"
msgstr "低评分段有 4 个获批申请人和 1 个拒绝申请人，高评分段分别为 2 个和 4 个："

msgid "Scorecard"
msgstr "评分卡"

msgid ""
"Turn a logistic regression on WOE values into points. :func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_scaling`, "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score` and :func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd` set and apply the "
"scale, :func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` and :func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` give the "
"points, and :func:`~kivi.scorecard.reason_codes` lists the variables that lowered a score most."
msgstr ""
"把基于 WOE 的逻辑回归转换为分值。 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_scaling` 、 :func:`~kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score` 和"
" :func:`~kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd` 设定并应用刻度， :func:`~kivi.scorecard.points_table` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` 给出分值， :func:`~kivi.scorecard.reason_codes` 列出使评分降低最多的变量。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/scorecard` for a scorecard built on the bundled data."
msgstr "基于内置数据构建的评分卡见 :doc:`/user_guide/scorecard` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`score_scaling <kivi.scorecard.score_scaling>`\\ \\(\\*\\, pdo\\, base\\_score\\, "
"base\\_odds\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`score_scaling <kivi.scorecard.score_scaling>`\\ \\(\\*\\, pdo\\, base\\_score\\, "
"base\\_odds\\)"

msgid "Return the factor and offset that turn log odds into a score."
msgstr "返回把对数几率转换为分数的因子（factor）和偏移量（offset）。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`pd_to_score <kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score>`\\ \\(probability\\, \\*\\, pdo\\, "
"base\\_score\\, ...\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`pd_to_score <kivi.scorecard.pd_to_score>`\\ \\(probability\\, \\*\\, pdo\\, "
"base\\_score\\, ...\\)"

msgid "Convert event probabilities to scorecard scores."
msgstr "把事件概率转换为评分卡分数。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`score_to_pd <kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd>`\\ \\(score\\, \\*\\, pdo\\, base\\_score\\, "
"base\\_odds\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`score_to_pd <kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd>`\\ \\(score\\, \\*\\, pdo\\, base\\_score\\, "
"base\\_odds\\)"

msgid "Convert scorecard scores to event probabilities."
msgstr "把评分卡分数转换为事件概率。"

msgid ":py:obj:`points_table <kivi.scorecard.points_table>`\\ \\(tables\\, coefficients\\, ...\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`points_table <kivi.scorecard.points_table>`\\ \\(tables\\, coefficients\\, ...\\)"

msgid "Turn a logistic regression on WOE values into points for each group."
msgstr "把基于 WOE 的逻辑回归转换为每个分组的分值。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`woe_to_points <kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points>`\\ \\(woe\\, coefficients\\, intercept\\, "
"...\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`woe_to_points <kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points>`\\ \\(woe\\, coefficients\\, intercept\\, "
"...\\)"

msgid "Give each applicant the points of each variable from its WOE values."
msgstr "根据 WOE 值给出每个申请人在各变量上的分值。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`reason_codes <kivi.scorecard.reason_codes>`\\ \\(points\\, table\\, \\*\\[\\, top\\, "
"atol\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`reason_codes <kivi.scorecard.reason_codes>`\\ \\(points\\, table\\, \\*\\[\\, top\\, "
"atol\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Name the variables that cost each applicant the most points."
msgstr "列出让每个申请人失分最多的变量。"

msgid ""
"A scorecard score is linear in the log of the good:bad odds. It equals `base_score` at odds of "
"`base_odds` and rises by `pdo` points each time the odds double."
msgstr "评分卡分数与好坏比（good:bad odds）的对数呈线性关系。几率为 `base_odds` 时分数等于 `base_score` ，几率每翻一倍，分数增加 `pdo` 分。"

msgid "**pdo**"
msgstr "**pdo**"

msgid "Points to double the odds. Must be positive."
msgstr "几率翻倍所需增加的分数（PDO），必须为正数。"

msgid "**base_score**"
msgstr "**base_score**"

msgid "Score at the base odds."
msgstr "基准几率对应的分数。"

msgid "**base_odds**"
msgstr "**base_odds**"

msgid "Good:bad odds at the base score, such as 50 for 50 non-events per event. Must be positive."
msgstr "基准分数对应的好坏比，例如 50 表示每个事件对应 50 个非事件。必须为正数。"

msgid "Points per unit of log odds, ``pdo / ln 2``."
msgstr "对数几率每增加一个单位对应的分数，即 ``pdo / ln 2`` 。"

msgid "**offset**"
msgstr "**offset**"

msgid "Score at even odds, ``base_score - factor * ln(base_odds)``."
msgstr "几率为 1:1 时的分数，即 ``base_score - factor * ln(base_odds)`` 。"

msgid "If an argument is not a finite number, or `pdo` or `base_odds` is not positive."
msgstr "如果某个参数不是有限数值，或者 `pdo` 或 `base_odds` 不是正数。"

msgid ":obj:`pd_to_score`"
msgstr ":obj:`pd_to_score`"

msgid "Convert event probabilities to scores."
msgstr "把事件概率转换为分数。"

msgid ":obj:`score_to_pd`"
msgstr ":obj:`score_to_pd`"

msgid "Convert scores to event probabilities."
msgstr "把分数转换为事件概率。"

msgid "With odds :math:`o = (1 - p) / p` for an event probability :math:`p`,"
msgstr "对事件概率 :math:`p` ，记几率 :math:`o = (1 - p) / p` ，则"

msgid ""
"\\mathrm{score} = \\mathrm{offset} + \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\ln o,\n"
"\n"
"\\mathrm{factor} = \\frac{\\mathrm{pdo}}{\\ln 2}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{offset} = \\mathrm{base\\_score} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\ln \\mathrm{base\\_odds}."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{score} = \\mathrm{offset} + \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\ln o,\n"
"\n"
"\\mathrm{factor} = \\frac{\\mathrm{pdo}}{\\ln 2}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{offset} = \\mathrm{base\\_score} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\ln \\mathrm{base\\_odds}."

msgid ""
"A lower probability of the event, such as a default, gives a higher score. The scaling is set by "
"`pdo`, `base_score` and `base_odds`, as in `score_scaling`."
msgstr "事件（例如违约）的概率越低，分数越高。刻度由 `pdo` 、 `base_score` 和 `base_odds` 决定，与 `score_scaling` 相同。"

msgid "Event probabilities strictly between 0 and 1. Missing values give missing scores."
msgstr "严格介于 0 与 1 之间的事件概率。缺失值对应的分数也为缺失。"

msgid "Good:bad odds at the base score. Must be positive."
msgstr "基准分数对应的好坏比，必须为正数。"

msgid ""
"Scores with the shape of `probability`. A Series input gives a Series with the same index and "
"name, and a scalar gives a float."
msgstr "分数，形状与 `probability` 相同。输入为 Series 时返回 Series，索引和名称保持不变；输入为标量时返回 float。"

msgid ""
"If `probability` has values outside the open interval (0, 1), or the scaling arguments are "
"invalid."
msgstr "如果 `probability` 含有开区间 (0, 1) 以外的值，或者刻度参数无效。"

msgid "The inverse conversion."
msgstr "反向转换。"

msgid ":obj:`score_scaling`"
msgstr ":obj:`score_scaling`"

msgid "The factor and offset of the scaling."
msgstr "刻度的因子和偏移量。"

msgid ""
"The score is ``offset + factor * ln((1 - probability) / probability)``. A probability of exactly "
"0 or 1 has no finite score and raises an error; see `score_to_pd` for the scores whose "
"probability rounds to 1."
msgstr ""
"分数为 ``offset + factor * ln((1 - probability) / probability)`` 。概率恰好为 0 或 1 "
"时没有有限的分数，会引发错误；哪些分数对应的概率会舍入为 1，参见 `score_to_pd` 。"

msgid ""
"This is the inverse of `pd_to_score` for the same scaling, so it gives the probability of the "
"event implied by each score."
msgstr "在相同刻度下，这是 `pd_to_score` 的逆运算，给出每个分数所隐含的事件概率。"

msgid "Scores. Missing values give missing probabilities."
msgstr "分数。缺失值对应的概率也为缺失。"

msgid "If the scaling arguments are invalid."
msgstr "如果刻度参数无效。"

msgid ""
"The probability is ``1 / (1 + exp((score - offset) / factor))``, computed without overflow for "
"extreme scores. In double precision it rounds to exactly 1 for scores more than about ``36.7 * "
"factor`` below the offset, -572 for the scale in the example, and `pd_to_score` rejects such "
"probabilities. Scores that low do not occur on a practical scale."
msgstr ""
"概率为 ``1 / (1 + exp((score - offset) / factor))`` ，计算方式保证极端分数也不会溢出。在双精度下，比偏移量低约 ``36.7 * factor`` "
"以上的分数（示例刻度下为 -572）对应的概率会舍入为 1，而 `pd_to_score` 不接受这样的概率。在实际使用的刻度上不会出现这么低的分数。"

msgid ""
"The points of an applicant's groups, one per variable, add up to the score that `pd_to_score` "
"gives for the model's probability. The intercept is spread evenly across the variables."
msgstr "申请人在各变量上所属分组的分值（每个变量一个）之和，等于 `pd_to_score` 对模型概率给出的分数。截距平均分摊到各个变量。"

msgid "**tables**"
msgstr "**tables**"

msgid "mapping"
msgstr "mapping"

msgid ""
"For each variable, its `kivi.woe.woe_table` result or a Series of WOE values indexed by group. "
"Tables of variables without a coefficient are ignored."
msgstr "每个变量对应其 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 结果，或以分组为索引的 WOE 值 Series。没有系数的变量的表会被忽略。"

msgid "**coefficients**"
msgstr "**coefficients**"

msgid "mapping or pandas.Series"
msgstr "mapping 或 pandas.Series"

msgid ""
"Logistic regression coefficient of each variable's WOE, for a model of the event probability. The"
" rows follow this order."
msgstr "事件概率模型中各变量 WOE 的逻辑回归系数。结果各行按此顺序排列。"

msgid "Intercept of the same model."
msgstr "同一模型的截距。"

msgid ""
"One row per variable and group, indexed by ``variable``, with the group label ``bin`` and the "
"group's ``woe`` and ``points``. Select a variable's rows with ``table.loc[[variable]]``."
msgstr ""
"每个变量的每个分组一行，以 ``variable`` 为索引，列出分组标签 ``bin`` 以及该组的 ``woe`` 和 ``points`` 。用 "
"``table.loc[[variable]]`` 选出某个变量的各行。"

msgid ""
"If `tables` is not a mapping or lacks a variable of `coefficients`, a table has no ``woe`` "
"column, repeats a group or has non-finite WOE values, the coefficients are empty, repeated or not"
" finite numbers, or the scaling arguments are invalid."
msgstr ""
"如果 `tables` 不是映射或缺少 `coefficients` 中的某个变量、某张表没有 ``woe`` 列、有重复分组或含有非有限的 WOE "
"值、系数为空、重复或不是有限数值，或者刻度参数无效。"

msgid ":obj:`woe_to_points`"
msgstr ":obj:`woe_to_points`"

msgid "The points of each applicant."
msgstr "每个申请人的分值。"

msgid ":obj:`reason_codes`"
msgstr ":obj:`reason_codes`"

msgid "The variables that cost an applicant the most points."
msgstr "让申请人失分最多的变量。"

msgid "Fit the WOE of each group."
msgstr "拟合每个分组的 WOE。"

msgid ""
"With kivi's WOE, :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)` for event and non-event shares :math:`p_i` and "
":math:`q_i`, the model is :math:`\\ln \\frac{\\mathrm{PD}}{1 - \\mathrm{PD}} = \\beta_0 + \\sum_j"
" \\beta_j \\mathrm{WOE}_j`. A higher WOE means more risk and, for a positive coefficient, fewer "
"points. Group :math:`i` of variable :math:`j`, one of :math:`m` variables, receives"
msgstr ""
"kivi 的 WOE 为 :math:`\\ln(p_i / q_i)` ，其中 :math:`p_i` 和 :math:`q_i` 分别为事件占比和非事件占比，模型为 :math:`\\ln "
"\\frac{\\mathrm{PD}}{1 - \\mathrm{PD}} = \\beta_0 + \\sum_j \\beta_j \\mathrm{WOE}_j` 。WOE "
"越高表示风险越高；系数为正时，分值越低。共有 :math:`m` 个变量时，变量 :math:`j` 的第 :math:`i` 组得到"

msgid ""
"\\mathrm{points}_{ij} = \\frac{\\mathrm{offset} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_0}{m}\n"
"- \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j \\, \\mathrm{WOE}_{ij},"
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{points}_{ij} = \\frac{\\mathrm{offset} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_0}{m}\n"
"- \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j \\, \\mathrm{WOE}_{ij},"

msgid ""
"with the factor and offset of `score_scaling`. Each variable carries the same share of the "
"intercept and offset, so the points of a variable's groups differ only by their WOE term."
msgstr "其中因子和偏移量来自 `score_scaling` 。每个变量分摊相同份额的截距和偏移量，因此同一变量各分组的分值只在 WOE 项上有差别。"

msgid ""
"The group labels stay in a column rather than an index level, so labels that compare equal across"
" variables, such as ``True`` and ``1``, keep their own values."
msgstr "分组标签放在列中而不是索引层级中，因此不同变量中比较结果相等的标签（例如 ``True`` 和 ``1`` ）仍保留各自的取值。"

msgid "[Rc133f1fff48a-1]_"
msgstr "[Rc133f1fff48a-1]_"

msgid ""
"The points are those of `points_table` for the same model and scaling. Their row sums are the "
"scores, equal to `pd_to_score` of the model's probabilities."
msgstr "对相同的模型和刻度，这些分值与 `points_table` 一致。每行之和即为分数，等于 `pd_to_score` 对模型概率给出的结果。"

msgid "**woe**"
msgstr "**woe**"

msgid "pandas.DataFrame or mapping"
msgstr "pandas.DataFrame 或 mapping"

msgid ""
"WOE values with one column per variable, such as the result of `kivi.woe.woe_transform` for each "
"variable. Columns without a coefficient are ignored."
msgstr "WOE 值，每个变量一列，例如对每个变量调用 `kivi.woe.woe_transform` 的结果。没有系数的列会被忽略。"

msgid ""
"Logistic regression coefficient of each variable's WOE, for a model of the event probability. The"
" columns follow this order."
msgstr "事件概率模型中各变量 WOE 的逻辑回归系数。结果各列按此顺序排列。"

msgid "Points with the index of `woe` and one column per variable."
msgstr "分值，索引与 `woe` 相同，每个变量一列。"

msgid ""
"If `woe` is not a DataFrame or mapping, lacks or repeats a variable of `coefficients` or has non-"
"finite values, the coefficients are empty, repeated or not finite, or the scaling arguments are "
"invalid."
msgstr "如果 `woe` 不是 DataFrame 或映射、缺少或重复 `coefficients` 中的某个变量或含有非有限值、系数为空、重复或不是有限值，或者刻度参数无效。"

msgid ":obj:`points_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`points_table`"

msgid "The points of every group."
msgstr "每个分组的分值。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The points of variable :math:`j` are :math:`(\\mathrm{offset} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_0)"
" / m - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j \\, \\mathrm{WOE}_j` for :math:`m` variables, as in "
"`points_table`. They are computed in the same way, so rounding both gives the same points."
msgstr ""
"共有 :math:`m` 个变量时，变量 :math:`j` 的分值为 :math:`(\\mathrm{offset} - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_0) "
"/ m - \\mathrm{factor} \\cdot \\beta_j \\, \\mathrm{WOE}_j` ，与 `points_table` "
"相同。两者的计算方式完全一致，因此取整后得到相同的分值。"

msgid ""
"A variable costs an applicant the difference between the points of the variable's best group and "
"the points of the applicant's group. Variables are listed from the largest cost; those that cost "
"nothing are not listed."
msgstr "某个变量让申请人损失的分数，是该变量最佳分组的分值与申请人所在分组的分值之差。变量按损失从大到小列出；没有造成损失的变量不列出。"

msgid "**points**"
msgstr "**points**"

msgid "Points of each applicant, as returned by `woe_to_points`."
msgstr "每个申请人的分值，即 `woe_to_points` 的返回结果。"

msgid "**table**"
msgstr "**table**"

msgid "The `points_table` result for the same model and scaling."
msgstr "相同模型和刻度下 `points_table` 的结果。"

msgid "**top**"
msgstr "**top**"

msgid "int, default 3"
msgstr "int，默认 3"

msgid "Number of reasons per applicant."
msgstr "每个申请人列出的原因个数。"

msgid "**atol**"
msgstr "**atol**"

msgid "float, default 1e-4"
msgstr "float，默认 1e-4"

msgid ""
"Largest difference, in points, between an applicant's points and the points of a group for the "
"applicant to be in that group. It absorbs rounding, for example of WOE values stored with six "
"decimals."
msgstr "申请人分值与某个分组分值之间允许的最大差值（以分计），差值不超过它时即认为申请人属于该分组。它可以吸收舍入误差，例如以六位小数存储的 WOE 值带来的误差。"

msgid "**unseen_points**"
msgstr "**unseen_points**"

msgid "float, mapping or pandas.Series, optional"
msgstr "float、mapping 或 pandas.Series，可选"

msgid ""
"Points of applicants in groups that `kivi.woe.woe_transform` encoded with ``unseen``, one value "
"for every variable or values by variable. Points that match no group but lie within `atol` of "
"their variable's `unseen_points` cost nothing, so the variable is not a reason for those "
"applicants. They are the `woe_to_points` result for the WOE passed as ``unseen``; see the "
"Examples. By default every point must match a group."
msgstr ""
"`kivi.woe.woe_transform` 用 ``unseen`` 编码的分组中申请人的分值，可以是所有变量共用的一个值，也可以按变量给出。与任何分组都不匹配、但与其变量的 "
"`unseen_points` 相差不超过 `atol` 的分值视为没有造成损失，因此该变量不会成为这些申请人的原因。这些分值就是对 ``unseen`` 所给 WOE 调用 "
"`woe_to_points` 的结果；参见示例。默认情况下，每个分值都必须匹配某个分组。"

msgid ""
"Variable names in columns ``reason_1`` to ``reason_<top>``, with the index of `points`. An "
"applicant with fewer costly variables has None in the remaining columns."
msgstr "变量名位于 ``reason_1`` 到 ``reason_<top>`` 各列，索引与 `points` 相同。造成损失的变量较少的申请人，其余各列为 None。"

msgid ""
"If `points` is not a DataFrame or has non-finite values, `table` is not a `points_table` result "
"or lacks a variable of `points`, some points are farther than `atol` from every group of their "
"variable and from its `unseen_points`, `top` is not a positive integer, `atol` is not a finite "
"positive number, or `unseen_points` is not a finite number or a mapping or Series of finite "
"numbers."
msgstr ""
"如果 `points` 不是 DataFrame 或含有非有限值、 `table` 不是 `points_table` 的结果或缺少 `points` "
"中的某个变量、某些分值与其变量的所有分组以及其 `unseen_points` 相差都超过 `atol` 、 `top` 不是正整数、 `atol` 不是有限正数，或者 "
"`unseen_points` 既不是有限数，也不是由有限数组成的映射或 Series。"

msgid ""
"Each applicant's points are matched to the nearest group of the variable in `table`, and the "
"costs are differences between the points of `table`'s groups. Costs that differ by less than "
"about `atol` count as equal, so such variables keep the order of the columns of `points`, and a "
"cost below about `atol` is no cost."
msgstr ""
"每个申请人的分值会匹配到 `table` 中该变量最接近的分组，损失分数是 `table` 中各分组分值之差。相差不到约 `atol` 的损失视为相等，因此这些变量保持 `points` "
"中的列顺序；低于约 `atol` 的损失视为没有损失。"

msgid ""
"Points that match no group, such as those from a different intercept or scaling, or WOE values "
"rounded more coarsely than `atol` allows, raise an error rather than giving reasons against the "
"wrong groups. So do, by default, the points of applicants in a group that had no development "
"observations, such as a new category, whose WOE came from ``unseen`` in `kivi.woe.woe_transform`."
" That WOE is a value chosen for the group, not evidence about the applicant, so with "
"`unseen_points` such points give no reason instead of the distance to the best group. Only points"
" near `unseen_points` are exempt; any other mismatch still raises. Points that lie within `atol` "
"of a group are matched to that group, even when their WOE came from ``unseen``."
msgstr ""
"与任何分组都不匹配的分值（例如来自不同截距或刻度的分值，或 WOE 的舍入比 `atol` "
"允许的更粗）会引发错误，而不是给出针对错误分组的原因。默认情况下，开发样本中没有观测的分组（例如新类别）里的申请人也是如此：其 WOE 来自 `kivi.woe.woe_transform` "
"中的 ``unseen`` 。这个 WOE 是为该分组选定的取值，并不是关于申请人的证据，因此给出 `unseen_points` "
"时，这些分值不产生原因，而不是按它与最佳分组的差距给出原因。只有接近 `unseen_points` 的分值才会豁免；其他任何不匹配仍会引发错误。与某个分组相差不超过 `atol` "
"的分值会匹配到该分组，即使其 WOE 来自 ``unseen`` 。"

msgid ""
"An applicant with a housing status that the development sample did not have was encoded with "
"``woe_transform(..., unseen=0.0)``. The points of a WOE of 0 are the `woe_to_points` result for a"
" row of zeros, the same base points for every variable. With these points as `unseen_points`, "
"housing is not one of the applicant's reasons:"
msgstr ""
"某个申请人的住房状况在开发样本中从未出现，因此用 ``woe_transform(..., unseen=0.0)`` 编码。WOE 为 0 时的分值，就是对一行全零调用 "
"`woe_to_points` 的结果，每个变量都是相同的基础分值。把这些分值作为 `unseen_points` 传入后，housing 不在该申请人的原因之中："

msgid "Variable selection"
msgstr "变量筛选"

msgid ""
"Select the variables of a scorecard and fit its logistic regression on WOE-encoded columns. "
":func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter` and :func:`~kivi.selection.vif` check the candidates "
"for collinearity, and :func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` and "
":func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` fit and select the model."
msgstr ""
"为评分卡筛选变量，并在 WOE 编码的列上拟合逻辑回归。 :func:`~kivi.selection.correlation_filter` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.selection.vif` 检查候选变量的共线性， :func:`~kivi.selection.logistic_regression` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.selection.stepwise` 拟合并筛选模型。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/selection` for a selection on the bundled data."
msgstr "基于内置数据的变量筛选见 :doc:`/user_guide/selection` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`correlation_filter <kivi.selection.correlation_filter>`\\ \\(X\\, \\*\\[\\, threshold\\,"
" priority\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`correlation_filter <kivi.selection.correlation_filter>`\\ \\(X\\, \\*\\[\\, threshold\\,"
" priority\\]\\)"

msgid "Drop one variable of each strongly correlated pair."
msgstr "对每一对强相关的变量，剔除其中一个。"

msgid ":py:obj:`vif <kivi.selection.vif>`\\ \\(X\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`vif <kivi.selection.vif>`\\ \\(X\\)"

msgid "Compute the variance inflation factor of each variable."
msgstr "计算每个变量的方差膨胀因子。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`logistic_regression <kivi.selection.logistic_regression>`\\ \\(X\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`logistic_regression <kivi.selection.logistic_regression>`\\ \\(X\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit a logistic regression and test each coefficient."
msgstr "拟合逻辑回归并检验每个系数。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`stepwise <kivi.selection.stepwise>`\\ \\(X\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, p\\_enter\\, "
"p\\_remove\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`stepwise <kivi.selection.stepwise>`\\ \\(X\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, p\\_enter\\, "
"p\\_remove\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Select variables for a logistic regression by their p-values."
msgstr "按 p 值为逻辑回归筛选变量。"

msgid ":py:obj:`SeparationError <kivi.selection.SeparationError>`"
msgstr ":py:obj:`SeparationError <kivi.selection.SeparationError>`"

msgid "The classes are separated, so the logistic regression has no estimates."
msgstr "两类被完全分开，因此逻辑回归没有估计值。"

msgid ""
"Variables are visited from the highest `priority` to the lowest. A variable is kept unless its "
"absolute Pearson correlation with a variable that is already kept exceeds `threshold`."
msgstr "按 `priority` 从高到低依次考察各变量。若某变量与已保留的某个变量的 Pearson 相关系数绝对值超过 `threshold` ，则将其剔除，否则保留。"

msgid "**X**"
msgstr "**X**"

msgid "pandas.DataFrame or array_like"
msgstr "pandas.DataFrame 或 array_like"

msgid ""
"Two-dimensional numeric values with one column per variable, such as WOE values from "
"`kivi.woe.woe_transform`."
msgstr "二维数值，每个变量一列，例如 `kivi.woe.woe_transform` 输出的 WOE 值。"

msgid "**threshold**"
msgstr "**threshold**"

msgid "float, default 0.7"
msgstr "float，默认 0.7"

msgid "Largest absolute correlation allowed between two kept variables, between 0 and 1."
msgstr "两个保留变量之间允许的最大相关系数绝对值，取值在 0 到 1 之间。"

msgid "**priority**"
msgstr "**priority**"

msgid ""
"One number per column, such as its information value; of two correlated variables, the one with "
"the higher priority is kept. A pandas Series is matched to the columns by label, other inputs by "
"position. Ties, and every column when `priority` is omitted, follow the column order, so earlier "
"columns are kept."
msgstr ""
"每列一个数值，例如该变量的信息值；两个相关变量中保留优先级较高的一个。pandas Series 按标签与列对应，其他输入按位置对应。优先级相同时，以及省略 `priority` "
"时，按列的顺序处理，因此靠前的列被保留。"

msgid "pandas.Index"
msgstr "pandas.Index"

msgid "Labels of the kept columns, in the order of `X`. Column positions when `X` is not a DataFrame."
msgstr "保留列的标签，按 `X` 中的顺序排列。当 `X` 不是 DataFrame 时为列的位置。"

msgid ""
"If `X` is not two-dimensional, has fewer than 2 rows or no columns, repeats a column label, or "
"has a column that is not numeric, contains missing or infinite values or is constant; if "
"`threshold` is not between 0 and 1; or if `priority` does not give one number for every column."
msgstr ""
"如果 `X` 不是二维、少于 2 行或没有列、列标签重复，或者某列不是数值、含有缺失值或无穷值、或为常数；如果 `threshold` 不在 0 到 1 之间；或者 `priority` "
"没有为每一列给出一个数值。"

msgid ":obj:`vif`"
msgstr ":obj:`vif`"

msgid "Measure how well the other variables explain each variable."
msgstr "衡量每个变量能被其他变量解释的程度。"

msgid ":obj:`stepwise`"
msgstr ":obj:`stepwise`"

msgid "Select variables by their significance in a logistic regression."
msgstr "按逻辑回归中的显著性筛选变量。"

msgid ""
"A variable is dropped only because of a variable that is kept. When ``a`` is correlated with "
"``b`` and ``b`` with ``c``, but ``a`` not with ``c``, and the priorities decrease from ``a`` to "
"``c``, then ``b`` is dropped and ``c`` is kept."
msgstr ""
"变量只会因为与某个保留变量相关而被剔除。若 ``a`` 与 ``b`` 相关、 ``b`` 与 ``c`` 相关，但 ``a`` 与 ``c`` 不相关，且优先级从 ``a`` 到 ``c`` "
"递减，则 ``b`` 被剔除而 ``c`` 被保留。"

msgid ""
"The VIF of a variable measures how well the other variables explain it in a linear regression. It"
" is 1 for a variable that is uncorrelated with the others and grows without bound as the variable"
" approaches a linear combination of them."
msgstr "变量的 VIF 衡量在线性回归中其他变量对它的解释程度。与其他变量不相关的变量 VIF 为 1；变量越接近其他变量的线性组合，VIF 越大，且没有上限。"

msgid "pandas.Series"
msgstr "pandas.Series"

msgid ""
"VIF of each column, indexed by the column labels of `X` (positions when `X` is not a DataFrame) "
"and named ``vif``. It is infinite for a column that is a linear combination of the others."
msgstr "每列的 VIF，以 `X` 的列标签为索引（当 `X` 不是 DataFrame 时为列的位置），名称为 ``vif`` 。某列是其他列的线性组合时，其 VIF 为无穷大。"

msgid ""
"If `X` is not two-dimensional, has fewer than 2 rows or no columns, repeats a column label, or "
"has a column that is not numeric, contains missing or infinite values or is constant."
msgstr "如果 `X` 不是二维、少于 2 行或没有列、列标签重复，或者某列不是数值、含有缺失值或无穷值、或为常数。"

msgid ":obj:`correlation_filter`"
msgstr ":obj:`correlation_filter`"

msgid ":obj:`logistic_regression`"
msgstr ":obj:`logistic_regression`"

msgid "Fit the scorecard model."
msgstr "拟合评分卡模型。"

msgid ""
"For column :math:`j`, let :math:`R_j^2` be the coefficient of determination of the least-squares "
"regression of column :math:`j` on an intercept and the other columns. Then"
msgstr "对第 :math:`j` 列，记 :math:`R_j^2` 为第 :math:`j` 列对截距项和其他各列做最小二乘回归的决定系数，则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{VIF}_j = \\frac{1}{1 - R_j^2}."
msgstr "\\mathrm{VIF}_j = \\frac{1}{1 - R_j^2}."

msgid ""
"The square root of the VIF is the factor by which collinearity inflates the standard error of the"
" variable's coefficient. With two columns of correlation :math:`r`, both have a VIF of :math:`1 /"
" (1 - r^2)`."
msgstr "VIF 的平方根是共线性使该变量系数的标准误放大的倍数。两列的相关系数为 :math:`r` 时，二者的 VIF 都是 :math:`1 / (1 - r^2)` 。"

msgid "Two columns with a correlation of 0.9 both have a VIF of :math:`1 / (1 - 0.9^2) = 5.263`:"
msgstr "相关系数为 0.9 的两列，VIF 都是 :math:`1 / (1 - 0.9^2) = 5.263` ："

msgid "Adding their sum makes every column a linear combination of the others:"
msgstr "加入二者之和后，每一列都是其他列的线性组合："

msgid ""
"The model has an intercept and one coefficient per column of `X`. The coefficients are maximum "
"likelihood estimates, and each is tested against zero with a Wald test."
msgstr "模型包含截距项，并为 `X` 的每一列估计一个系数。系数为最大似然估计，并用 Wald 检验逐一检验其是否为零。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event. If `X` is a DataFrame and `target` a Series, they "
"must have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by position."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件。如果 `X` 是 DataFrame 且 `target` 是 Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative frequency weight of each row, matched like `target`: a row with weight 2 counts as "
"two identical observations, so integer weights give the same estimates, standard errors and log-"
"likelihood as repeating rows. Rows with zero weight are left out of the fit. See the Notes on "
"weights that do not count observations."
msgstr ""
"每一行的非负频数权重，对应方式与 `target` 相同：权重为 2 "
"的行计为两个相同的观测，因此整数权重与重复行得到相同的估计值、标准误和对数似然。权重为零的行不参与拟合。关于不表示观测个数的权重见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"One row for the intercept, labelled ``intercept``, and one for each column of `X`, with the "
"coefficient, its standard error, the Wald z statistic and its two-sided p-value. The index has "
"the name of the columns of `X`. ``attrs[\"log_likelihood\"]`` holds the maximized log-likelihood "
"and ``attrs[\"converged\"]`` whether the fit converged."
msgstr ""
"截距项一行（标签为 ``intercept`` ）， `X` 的每一列各一行，包含系数、标准误、Wald z 统计量及其双侧 p 值。索引的名称与 `X` 的列名相同。 "
"``attrs[\"log_likelihood\"]`` 保存最大化后的对数似然， ``attrs[\"converged\"]`` 表示拟合是否收敛。"

msgid "SeparationError"
msgstr "SeparationError"

msgid "If the columns separate the classes, so that the estimates do not exist."
msgstr "如果各列把两类完全分开，以致估计值不存在。"

msgid ""
"If `X` is not two-dimensional, has fewer than 2 rows or no columns, repeats a column label, has a"
" column labelled ``intercept``, or has a column that is not numeric, contains missing or infinite"
" values, is constant or is a linear combination of the intercept and the columns before it, or so"
" close to one that its coefficient cannot be estimated; if `target` is not one-dimensional, its "
"index or length does not match `X`, or it does not contain both 0 and 1 or has missing or other "
"labels; or if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each row one finite, non-negative weight, "
"or leaves a class without weight. With `weights`, only the checks for constant columns and linear"
" combinations are limited to the rows with positive weight."
msgstr ""
"如果 `X` 不是二维、少于 2 行或没有列、列标签重复、有标签为 ``intercept`` "
"的列，或者某列不是数值、含有缺失值或无穷值、为常数、是截距项与前面各列的线性组合或与之过于接近以致无法估计其系数；如果 `target` 不是一维、索引或长度与 `X` 不一致，或者没有同时包含"
" 0 和 1 或含有缺失值及其他标签；或者 `weights` 不是数值、没有给每一行一个有限的非负权重，或者使某一类别没有权重。给定 `weights` "
"时，只有常数列和线性组合的检查仅针对权重为正的行。"

msgid "If the fit does not converge for a reason other than separation."
msgstr "如果拟合因分离以外的原因未能收敛。"

msgid "Select the columns of the model by their p-values."
msgstr "按 p 值筛选模型的列。"

msgid "Check the columns for collinearity."
msgstr "检查各列的共线性。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.woe.woe_transform`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.woe.woe_transform`"

msgid "Encode groups with their WOE."
msgstr "用 WOE 对分组编码。"

msgid "The model is"
msgstr "模型为"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\ln \\frac{P(y = 1)}{P(y = 0)} = \\beta_0 + \\sum_j \\beta_j x_j."
msgstr "\\ln \\frac{P(y = 1)}{P(y = 0)} = \\beta_0 + \\sum_j \\beta_j x_j."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The estimates are found by Newton-Raphson, also known as iteratively reweighted least squares, on"
" centred and scaled columns, so that an offset or the unit of a column does not affect their "
"accuracy. The standard errors are the square roots of the diagonal of the inverse Fisher "
"information, :math:`z = \\hat\\beta / \\mathrm{se}`, and the p-value is :math:`P(|Z| > |z|)` for "
"a standard normal :math:`Z`."
msgstr ""
"估计值在中心化并标准化后的列上用牛顿-拉弗森法（也称迭代重加权最小二乘法）求得，因此列的偏移量或单位不会影响其精度。标准误是 Fisher 信息矩阵之逆的对角线元素的平方根， :math:`z "
"= \\hat\\beta / \\mathrm{se}` ，p 值为 :math:`P(|Z| > |z|)` ，其中 :math:`Z` 服从标准正态分布。"

msgid "With WOE-encoded variables, the coefficients are expected to be positive: see `stepwise`."
msgstr "对 WOE 编码的变量，系数应为正，参见 `stepwise` 。"

msgid ""
"With `weights` :math:`w_i`, the estimates maximize the weighted log-likelihood :math:`\\sum_i w_i"
" [y_i \\ln p_i + (1 - y_i) \\ln(1 - p_i)]`, and the standard errors come from the weighted Fisher"
" information :math:`\\sum_i w_i p_i (1 - p_i) x_i x_i^\\top`. These are frequency weights, as in "
"statsmodels' ``GLM(freq_weights=...)``: the total weight counts as the number of independent "
"observations, so multiplying every weight by :math:`c` divides the variances by :math:`c`. "
"Integer weights that count repeated rows therefore give the standard errors of the repeated rows."
" Weights that do not count observations do not: those of "
"`kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation`, which split each rejected applicant into a bad and a "
"good row, and those of `kivi.reject_inference.reweighting`, which let each accepted applicant "
"stand for several, make the standard errors too small and the p-values too low. The inferred rows"
" and the extra weight count as observations, although they add no observed outcomes."
msgstr ""
"给定权重 `weights` :math:`w_i` 时，估计值最大化加权对数似然 :math:`\\sum_i w_i [y_i \\ln p_i + (1 - y_i) \\ln(1 - "
"p_i)]` ，标准误来自加权的 Fisher 信息 :math:`\\sum_i w_i p_i (1 - p_i) x_i x_i^\\top` 。这是频数权重，与 statsmodels "
"的 ``GLM(freq_weights=...)`` 相同：总权重被当作独立观测的个数，因此把每个权重乘以 :math:`c` 会使方差除以 :math:`c` "
"。表示重复行数的整数权重因而给出重复行的标准误。不表示观测个数的权重则不然： `kivi.reject_inference.fuzzy_augmentation` "
"把每个拒绝申请人拆成一行坏样本和一行好样本时的权重，以及 `kivi.reject_inference.reweighting` 让每个获批申请人代表多个申请人时的权重，都会使标准误偏小、p "
"值偏低。推断出的行和额外的权重被计为观测，尽管它们没有增加任何观测到的结果。"

msgid "[R238aee73b2df-1]_"
msgstr "[R238aee73b2df-1]_"

msgid ""
"With a single binary variable, the coefficient is the log odds ratio: the odds of the event are "
"1:3 at ``x = 0`` and 3:1 at ``x = 1``, so the coefficient is :math:`\\ln 9` and the intercept "
":math:`\\ln(1/3)`."
msgstr ""
"只有一个二值变量时，系数就是对数优势比：事件的优势在 ``x = 0`` 时为 1:3，在 ``x = 1`` 时为 3:1，因此系数为 :math:`\\ln 9` ，截距为 "
":math:`\\ln(1/3)` 。"

msgid ""
"Integer weights count repeated rows, so the four distinct rows with their counts give the same "
"fit:"
msgstr "整数权重表示重复的行数，因此四个不同的行加上各自的次数会得到相同的拟合结果："

msgid ""
"Forward selection starts from the intercept and adds, one at a time, the variable with the "
"smallest p-value while that p-value is below `p_enter`. Backward elimination starts from all "
"variables and removes, one at a time, the variable with the largest p-value while that p-value is"
" above `p_remove`. Selection in both directions adds variables like forward selection, but after "
"each addition removes the variables that no longer meet `p_remove`."
msgstr ""
"向前选择从只含截距的模型开始，每次加入 p 值最小的变量，直到最小的 p 值不再低于 `p_enter` 。向后剔除从包含全部变量的模型开始，每次移除 p 值最大的变量，直到最大的 p "
"值不再高于 `p_remove` 。双向逐步选择像向前选择一样加入变量，但每加入一个变量后，都会移除不再满足 `p_remove` 的变量。"

msgid ""
"Two-dimensional numeric values with one column per candidate variable, such as WOE values from "
"`kivi.woe.woe_transform`."
msgstr "二维数值，每个候选变量一列，例如 `kivi.woe.woe_transform` 输出的 WOE 值。"

msgid "**p_enter**"
msgstr "**p_enter**"

msgid ""
"A variable enters only if its p-value in the extended model is below this level, which is greater"
" than 0 and at most 1."
msgstr "只有当变量在扩展后模型中的 p 值低于该水平时才会入选；该水平大于 0 且不超过 1。"

msgid "**p_remove**"
msgstr "**p_remove**"

msgid "float, default 0.10"
msgstr "float，默认 0.10"

msgid ""
"A variable is removed if its p-value is above this level, which is greater than 0 and at most 1 "
"and, in both directions, not below `p_enter`."
msgstr "变量的 p 值高于该水平时被移除；该水平大于 0 且不超过 1，双向选择时不得低于 `p_enter` 。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "{\"both\", \"forward\", \"backward\"}, default \"both\""
msgstr "{\"both\", \"forward\", \"backward\"}，默认 \"both\""

msgid "Whether variables are added and removed, only added, or only removed."
msgstr "既加入也移除变量、只加入变量，还是只移除变量。"

msgid "**positive**"
msgstr "**positive**"

msgid ""
"Keep every coefficient of the selected model positive. A variable enters only if all coefficients"
" of the extended model are positive, and a variable whose coefficient is not positive is removed "
"before any other, starting with the smallest z statistic."
msgstr "使所选模型的每个系数都为正。只有扩展后模型的所有系数都为正时变量才会入选；系数不为正的变量优先于其他变量被移除，z 统计量最小的最先移除。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative frequency weight of each row, as in `logistic_regression`. Integer weights select "
"the same variables as repeating rows. The p-values depend on the scale of the weights as they do "
"on the sample size. The weights of reject inference make them too low, so that more variables "
"enter than the observed outcomes support; select the variables on the accepted applicants "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"每一行的非负频数权重，与 `logistic_regression` 相同。整数权重与重复行选出相同的变量。p 值取决于权重的尺度，正如取决于样本量。拒绝推断的权重会使 p "
"值偏低，从而选入超出观测结果所能支持的变量；应改为在获批申请人上选择变量。"

msgid "Labels of the selected columns, in the order of `X`. Column positions when `X` is not a DataFrame."
msgstr "入选列的标签，按 `X` 中的顺序排列。当 `X` 不是 DataFrame 时为列的位置。"

msgid "If `direction` is ``\"backward\"`` and the model with every column separates the classes."
msgstr "如果 `direction` 为 ``\"backward\"`` ，且包含全部列的模型把两类完全分开。"

msgid ""
"If `X`, `target` or `weights` is invalid as described for `logistic_regression`, in every "
"direction; if `p_enter` or `p_remove` is not greater than 0 and at most 1, or `p_enter` exceeds "
"`p_remove` when `direction` is ``\"both\"``; or if `direction` is not one of the three options or"
" `positive` is not a boolean."
msgstr ""
"如果 `X` 、 `target` 或 `weights` 不符合 `logistic_regression` 中所述的要求（任何方向都会检查）；如果 `p_enter` 或 "
"`p_remove` 不是大于 0 且不超过 1 的数，或 `direction` 为 ``\"both\"`` 时 `p_enter` 超过 `p_remove` ；或者 "
"`direction` 不是三个选项之一，或 `positive` 不是布尔值。"

msgid "If the model of the selected variables does not converge for a reason other than separation."
msgstr "如果所选变量的模型因分离以外的原因未能收敛。"

msgid "Fit the selected model and read its coefficients."
msgstr "拟合所选模型并查看其系数。"

msgid "Drop strongly correlated variables first."
msgstr "先剔除强相关的变量。"

msgid ""
"The p-values are those of the Wald tests reported by `logistic_regression`. Each candidate is "
"tested in the model made of the selected variables and the candidate, so every step refits one "
"model per candidate. A candidate does not enter if that model would separate the classes, does "
"not converge or is numerically singular. In both directions, a variable cannot enter if that "
"would recreate a set of variables that was selected before, which guarantees that the selection "
"stops."
msgstr ""
"p 值即 `logistic_regression` 报告的 Wald 检验 p "
"值。每个候选变量都在由已选变量和该候选变量组成的模型中检验，因此每一步都要为每个候选变量重新拟合一个模型。如果这个模型会使两类完全分开、无法收敛或在数值上奇异，候选变量就不会入选。双向选择时，如果加入某个变量会重现之前选过的变量组合，该变量不能入选，这保证了筛选过程一定会终止。"

msgid ""
"kivi defines the WOE of a group as the log of its share of events over its share of non-events, "
"so a higher WOE means a higher event rate. In a logistic regression of `target` on a single WOE-"
"encoded variable, the coefficient is therefore positive; it is exactly 1 when no cell needed "
"smoothing. A negative coefficient in a model with several variables means that the variable's "
"effect is reversed by the others, usually because of collinearity, and makes the scorecard points"
" of its bins contradict their event rates. ``positive=True`` rules out such models."
msgstr ""
"kivi 将分组的 WOE 定义为其事件占比与非事件占比之比的对数，因此 WOE 越高，事件率越高。所以在 `target` 对单个 WOE "
"编码变量的逻辑回归中，系数为正；没有单元格需要平滑时，系数恰好为 1。在多变量模型中，负系数表示该变量的作用被其他变量反转（通常源于共线性），会使其各箱的评分卡分数与事件率相矛盾。 "
"``positive=True`` 会排除这样的模型。"

msgid "[R44bd75d8258f-1]_, [R44bd75d8258f-2]_"
msgstr "[R44bd75d8258f-1]_, [R44bd75d8258f-2]_"

msgid ""
"A combination of the variables predicts the target without error, for every observation (complete"
" separation) or for every observation off a boundary (quasi-complete separation). The likelihood "
"then keeps growing as the coefficients grow, so the maximum likelihood estimates do not exist."
msgstr "变量的某个组合能无误地预测目标变量：对所有观测都成立（完全分离），或对边界以外的所有观测成立（准完全分离）。此时似然随系数增大而不断增大，因此最大似然估计不存在。"

msgid "Raises this error."
msgstr "会抛出此错误。"

msgid "Leaves out candidates that separate the classes."
msgstr "不选入会把两类完全分开的候选变量。"

msgid "Binning specifications"
msgstr "分箱方案"

msgid ""
"Bin and encode every column of a data frame in one step. :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` fits the "
"binning and the WOE of each column, and the resulting :class:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec` groups and "
"encodes any other sample in the same way and saves itself as versioned JSON."
msgstr ""
"一步完成数据框所有列的分箱和编码。 :func:`~kivi.spec.fit_spec` 拟合每一列的分箱和 WOE，得到的 :class:`~kivi.spec.BinningSpec` "
"以同样的方式对其他任何样本分组和编码，并能保存为带版本号的 JSON。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/spec` for examples and the file format."
msgstr "示例和文件格式见 :doc:`/user_guide/spec` 。"

msgid ":py:obj:`fit_spec <kivi.spec.fit_spec>`\\ \\(frame\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, columns\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`fit_spec <kivi.spec.fit_spec>`\\ \\(frame\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, columns\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Fit the binning and WOE of every column of a development sample."
msgstr "在开发样本上拟合每一列的分箱和 WOE。"

msgid ":py:obj:`BinningSpec <kivi.spec.BinningSpec>`\\ \\(kinds\\, edges\\, special\\, tables\\, ...\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`BinningSpec <kivi.spec.BinningSpec>`\\ \\(kinds\\, edges\\, special\\, tables\\, ...\\)"

msgid "Binning and WOE encoding of every column, fitted on a development sample."
msgstr "在开发样本上拟合的、每一列的分箱和 WOE 编码。"

msgid ""
"Numeric columns are binned with the method chosen for them and grouped with `kivi.binning.cut`; "
"other columns keep their labels as groups. The WOE of each group is then measured with "
"`kivi.woe.woe_table`. Nothing is re-binned automatically: the method, the number of bins and the "
"options of each column decide how coarse its bins are."
msgstr ""
"数值列按为其选定的方法分箱，并用 `kivi.binning.cut` 分组；其他列以自身标签作为分组。然后用 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 计算每个分组的 "
"WOE。不会自动重新分箱：每一列分箱的粗细由其方法、箱数和选项决定。"

msgid "**frame**"
msgstr "**frame**"

msgid ""
"Development sample with one column per variable. Columns with a numeric dtype other than bool are"
" binned. Columns of any other dtype, such as object, string, category or bool, are categorical: "
"each label is a group. Convert integer codes to the category dtype to keep them as labels."
msgstr ""
"开发样本，每个变量一列。数值 dtype（bool 除外）的列会被分箱。其他 dtype 的列（例如 object、string、category 或 "
"bool）是类别列：每个标签是一个分组。若要把整数编码当作标签，请先将其转换为 category dtype。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event, one per row of `frame`. A Series must have the same "
"index as `frame`; other inputs are matched by position."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件， `frame` 的每一行一个。Series 必须与 `frame` 的索引相同；其他输入按位置对应。"

msgid "**columns**"
msgstr "**columns**"

msgid "sequence of str, optional"
msgstr "str 序列，可选"

msgid "Columns to fit, in the order of the specification. By default every column of `frame`."
msgstr "要拟合的列，其顺序即分箱方案中的顺序。默认为 `frame` 的所有列。"

msgid "str or dict, default \"quantile\""
msgstr "str 或 dict，默认 \"quantile\""

msgid ""
"Binning method of the numeric columns: ``\"quantile\"`` or ``\"uniform\"`` for "
"`kivi.binning.bin_edges`, or ``\"chimerge\"``, ``\"tree\"`` or ``\"monotonic\"`` for "
"`kivi.binning.chimerge_edges`, `kivi.binning.tree_edges` or `kivi.binning.monotonic_edges`. A "
"dict maps columns to methods, and the numeric columns it leaves out use ``\"quantile\"``."
msgstr ""
"数值列的分箱方法： ``\"quantile\"`` 或 ``\"uniform\"`` 对应 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` ， ``\"chimerge\"`` 、 "
"``\"tree\"`` 或 ``\"monotonic\"`` 分别对应 `kivi.binning.chimerge_edges` 、 `kivi.binning.tree_edges` 和"
" `kivi.binning.monotonic_edges` 。dict 把列映射到方法，dict 中未列出的数值列使用 ``\"quantile\"`` 。"

msgid "int or dict, default 5"
msgstr "int 或 dict，默认 5"

msgid ""
"Number of bins, passed as ``bins`` to `kivi.binning.bin_edges` and as ``max_bins`` to the "
"supervised methods. A dict maps columns to a number of bins or to edges, which must increase from"
" ``-inf`` to ``inf`` and are used as given. With ``\"monotonic\"``, None merges bins only until "
"the WOE is monotonic. The numeric columns that a dict leaves out get 5 bins."
msgstr ""
"箱数，作为 ``bins`` 传给 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` ，作为 ``max_bins`` 传给有监督方法。dict 把列映射到箱数或边界；边界必须从 "
"``-inf`` 递增到 ``inf`` ，并按原样使用。对 ``\"monotonic\"`` ，None 表示只合并到 WOE 单调为止。dict 中未列出的数值列分为 5 箱。"

msgid "dict, optional"
msgstr "dict，可选"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Special codes of numeric columns, such as ``{\"pdays\": [-1]}``. The codes must be numbers, "
"possibly infinite. They are left out of the fit, and each code forms its own group."
msgstr "数值列的特殊值编码，例如 ``{\"pdays\": [-1]}`` 。编码必须是数值，可以是无穷。拟合时排除这些编码，每个编码单独成组。"

msgid "**options**"
msgstr "**options**"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Further keyword arguments for the binning function of each column, such as ``{\"balance\": "
"{\"alpha\": None}}`` with ``\"chimerge\"``. The special codes, the weights, the number of bins "
"and, for ``\"monotonic\"``, the smoothing are passed by `fit_spec` and cannot be given here."
msgstr ""
"传给每一列分箱函数的其他关键字参数，例如配合 ``\"chimerge\"`` 使用的 ``{\"balance\": {\"alpha\": None}}`` 。特殊值、权重、箱数以及 "
"``\"monotonic\"`` 的平滑参数由 `fit_spec` 传入，不能在这里指定。"

msgid "**unseen**"
msgstr "**unseen**"

msgid "float, \"raise\" or dict, default \"raise\""
msgstr "float、\"raise\" 或 dict，默认 \"raise\""

msgid ""
"WOE for values whose group is not in a column's table when a sample is encoded: a new category, a"
" special code or an interval without development observations, or missing values when development"
" had none. By default such values raise an error. A dict maps columns to a WOE or ``\"raise\"``, "
"and the columns it leaves out raise."
msgstr ""
"编码样本时，分组不在该列 WOE 表中的取值所用的 WOE：新类别、开发样本中没有观测值的特殊值或区间，或开发样本没有缺失值时的缺失值。默认情况下，这类取值会引发错误。dict 把列映射到 "
"WOE 或 ``\"raise\"`` ，dict 中未列出的列会引发错误。"

msgid ""
"Positive replacement for a zero count when calculating the WOE, as in `kivi.woe.woe_table`. "
"``\"monotonic\"`` binning uses the same value, so its trend holds in the tables."
msgstr "计算 WOE 时用这个正数替代零计数，含义与 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 相同。 ``\"monotonic\"`` 分箱使用同一取值，因此其单调趋势在 WOE 表中同样成立。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each row, matched like `target`, for the binning functions and "
"`kivi.woe.woe_table`. Counts are then sums of weights, and `smoothing` is in units of weight."
msgstr "每一行的非负权重，对应方式与 `target` 相同，会传给分箱函数和 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 。此时计数为权重之和， `smoothing` 也以权重为单位。"

msgid "BinningSpec"
msgstr "BinningSpec"

msgid "The kind, edges, special codes, WOE table and unseen policy of every column."
msgstr "每一列的类型、边界、特殊值、WOE 表和未见分组策略。"

msgid ""
"If `frame` is not a DataFrame or has no columns to fit, `columns` repeats a column or names one "
"that `frame` lacks, a column name is not a string, the columns include the target, or `target` "
"does not give each row a label 0 or 1 or lacks one of the two classes. If a dict names a column "
"that is not fitted, `method`, `bins`, `special` or `options` names a categorical column, or a "
"value is invalid, such as a special code that is not a number. Also if `smoothing` or `weights` "
"are invalid, a numeric column has infinite values that are not special codes, or the binning of a"
" column fails; the message then names the column."
msgstr ""
"如果 `frame` 不是 DataFrame 或没有可拟合的列， `columns` 重复某一列或指定了 `frame` 中没有的列，列名不是字符串，拟合的列包含目标变量，或 `target`"
" 的标签不是每行一个 0 或 1，或者缺少两类中的一类。如果某个 dict 指定了未拟合的列， `method` 、 `bins` 、 `special` 或 `options` "
"指定了类别列，或某个取值无效，例如特殊值编码不是数值。此外，如果 `smoothing` 或 `weights` "
"无效，某个数值列含有不属于特殊值的无穷值，或某一列分箱失败；此时错误信息会指明该列。"

msgid ""
"If tied quantiles leave a column with fewer bins than requested, as in `kivi.binning.bin_edges`, "
"if a numeric column has no values to fit apart from missing, special and zero-weight values, so "
"that its edges are ``[-inf, inf]``, or if a column of dtype object holds only numbers, which "
"makes each distinct number a group. The message names the column."
msgstr ""
"如果重合的分位数使某一列的箱数少于期望值（与 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` 相同），某个数值列除缺失值、特殊值和零权重的取值外没有可拟合的值，从而其边界为 ``[-inf, "
"inf]`` ，或者某个 object dtype 的列只含数值，使每个不同的数值各成一组。警告信息会指明该列。"

msgid ":obj:`BinningSpec`"
msgstr ":obj:`BinningSpec`"

msgid "Group, encode and save the fitted columns."
msgstr "对拟合好的列分组、编码并保存。"

msgid "Fit the edges of one column."
msgstr "拟合单列的边界。"

msgid "The WOE table of one column."
msgstr "单列的 WOE 表。"

msgid ""
"Each column is fitted on its own with the public functions, so a column of the specification has "
"the same edges and table as the steps of :doc:`/user_guide/binning` and :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv`"
" applied to it alone."
msgstr ""
"每一列都用公开函数单独拟合，因此分箱方案中某一列的边界和 WOE 表，与单独对该列执行 :doc:`/user_guide/binning` 和 "
":doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 中的步骤所得的结果相同。"

msgid ""
"For each column, a specification records whether it is numeric or categorical, the edges and "
"special codes of a numeric column, the WOE table of its groups and the policy for groups that are"
" not in the table. `cut` groups any sample with the same edges, `woe_transform` encodes it with "
"the same WOE, and `to_json` and `from_json` save and load the specification without changing its "
"groups or its encoding. Fit a specification with `fit_spec` rather than calling the constructor."
msgstr ""
"对每一列，分箱方案记录：它是数值列还是类别列、数值列的边界和特殊值、其各分组的 WOE 表，以及不在表中的分组的处理策略。 `cut` 用同样的边界对任意样本分组， "
"`woe_transform` 用同样的 WOE 编码， `to_json` 和 `from_json` 保存并加载分箱方案，且不会改变分组和编码。请用 `fit_spec` "
"拟合分箱方案，而不是直接调用构造函数。"

msgid ""
"A specification is immutable. Its mappings are read-only, and ``edges`` and ``tables`` return a "
"new copy of an array or a table on each access, so changing the copy leaves the specification as "
"it was. To change a field, such as the unseen policy, use `dataclasses.replace`, which validates "
"the result again."
msgstr ""
"分箱方案不可变。其映射是只读的， ``edges`` 和 ``tables`` 每次访问都返回数组或表的新副本，因此修改副本不会影响分箱方案。若要修改某个字段（例如未见分组策略），请使用 "
"`dataclasses.replace` ，它会重新校验结果。"

msgid "**kinds**"
msgstr "**kinds**"

msgid "``\"numeric\"`` or ``\"categorical\"`` for each column, in the order of the specification."
msgstr "每一列为 ``\"numeric\"`` 或 ``\"categorical\"`` ，顺序即分箱方案中的顺序。"

msgid "Edges of each numeric column, increasing from ``-inf`` to ``inf``."
msgstr "每个数值列的边界，从 ``-inf`` 递增到 ``inf`` 。"

msgid ""
"Special codes of each numeric column, possibly none. The codes are numbers, and each forms its "
"own group, as in `kivi.binning.cut`."
msgstr "每个数值列的特殊值，可以为空。这些编码是数值，与 `kivi.binning.cut` 相同，每个编码单独成组。"

msgid ""
"The `kivi.woe.woe_table` result of each column. The groups of a numeric column are its special "
"codes and the intervals of its edges. Missing values form a group labelled NaN."
msgstr "每一列的 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 结果。数值列的分组是其特殊值和由边界构成的区间。缺失值单独成组，标签为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"``\"raise\"`` or a finite WOE for each column, used for values whose group is not in the column's"
" table."
msgstr "每一列为 ``\"raise\"`` 或一个有限的 WOE，用于分组不在该列 WOE 表中的取值。"

msgid "Smoothing with which the tables were computed."
msgstr "计算 WOE 表时所用的平滑参数。"

msgid "**kivi_version**"
msgstr "**kivi_version**"

msgid "str, optional"
msgstr "str，可选"

msgid "Version of kivi that fitted the specification. By default, or if None, the installed version."
msgstr "拟合该分箱方案的 kivi 版本。默认或为 None 时取已安装的版本。"

msgid "Attributes"
msgstr "属性"

msgid "**format_version**"
msgstr "**format_version**"

msgid "int"
msgstr "int"

msgid "Version of the JSON format that `to_json` writes."
msgstr "`to_json` 写出的 JSON 格式的版本。"

msgid ""
"If `kinds` is empty or has a name that is not a string or a kind other than the two above, if "
"`edges` and `special` do not have one entry per numeric column or `tables` and `unseen` one entry"
" per column, or if an entry is invalid: edges that do not increase from ``-inf`` to ``inf``, a "
"missing or unsupported special code, a table without a finite ``woe`` column or with a repeated "
"group, a group of a numeric column that is neither one of its special codes nor an interval of "
"its edges, or an unseen policy that is neither ``\"raise\"`` nor a finite number. Also if "
"`smoothing` is not finite and positive or `kivi_version` is not a string."
msgstr ""
"如果 `kinds` 为空、含有非字符串的列名或上述两种以外的类型；如果 `edges` 和 `special` 不是每个数值列恰好一项，或 `tables` 和 `unseen` "
"不是每列恰好一项；或某一项无效：边界没有从 ``-inf`` 递增到 ``inf`` 、特殊值缺失或类型不受支持、WOE 表没有有限的 ``woe`` "
"列或有重复分组、数值列的某个分组既不是其特殊值也不是其边界构成的区间，或未见分组策略既不是 ``\"raise\"`` 也不是有限数值。此外，如果 `smoothing` 不是有限正数，或 "
"`kivi_version` 不是字符串。"

msgid ":obj:`fit_spec`"
msgstr ":obj:`fit_spec`"

msgid "Fit a specification on a development sample."
msgstr "在开发样本上拟合分箱方案。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.binning.cut`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.binning.cut`"

msgid "Group one numeric column."
msgstr "对单个数值列分组。"

msgid "Encode one column with its WOE table."
msgstr "用单列的 WOE 表对该列编码。"

msgid ""
"Labels of categorical columns must be strings, integers, floats, booleans or intervals, which the"
" JSON format keeps apart. Within a column, labels that compare equal, such as ``True`` and ``1``,"
" form one group, because `kivi.woe.woe_table` and `kivi.woe.woe_transform` match labels by "
"equality."
msgstr ""
"类别列的标签必须是字符串、整数、浮点数、布尔值或区间，JSON 格式会区分这些类型。在同一列中，相等的标签（例如 ``True`` 和 ``1`` ）属于同一分组，因为 "
"`kivi.woe.woe_table` 和 `kivi.woe.woe_transform` 按相等关系匹配标签。"

msgid ""
"Two specifications are equal when `to_json` gives the same text for both, which includes "
"`kivi_version`. The text is computed once and kept, so comparing and hashing a specification "
"again is cheap."
msgstr "当 `to_json` 为两个分箱方案给出相同的文本时，二者相等；文本中包含 `kivi_version` 。文本只计算一次并保留下来，因此再次比较或计算哈希的开销很小。"

msgid "Names of the columns in the specification."
msgstr "分箱方案中各列的名称。"

msgid ""
"The columns are in the order in which they were fitted, which is the order of the columns of "
"`cut` and `woe_transform`."
msgstr "各列按拟合时的顺序排列，也就是 `cut` 和 `woe_transform` 结果中列的顺序。"

msgid ":obj:`select`"
msgstr ":obj:`select`"

msgid "A specification of some of the columns."
msgstr "只含部分列的分箱方案。"

msgid "Group every column of a sample as in development."
msgstr "按开发时的方式对样本的每一列分组。"

msgid ""
"Numeric columns are assigned to their bins with `kivi.binning.cut`, using the fitted edges and "
"special codes. Categorical columns are returned unchanged, because their labels are their groups."
msgstr "数值列用 `kivi.binning.cut` 按拟合的边界和特殊值分箱。类别列原样返回，因为其标签就是分组。"

msgid "Sample that has every column of the specification. Other columns are ignored."
msgstr "包含分箱方案中所有列的样本。其他列会被忽略。"

msgid ""
"The groups of each column of the specification, in its order, with the index of `frame`. Numeric "
"columns are categorical, with the special codes followed by every interval of the edges."
msgstr "分箱方案中每一列的分组，按分箱方案的顺序排列，索引与 `frame` 相同。数值列为分类型，类别依次为特殊值和由边界构成的全部区间。"

msgid ""
"If `frame` is not a DataFrame, lacks a column of the specification or has it twice, or a column "
"fitted as numeric has values but not a numeric dtype, which could hide its special codes; convert"
" such a column with ``pandas.to_numeric``. The message names the column."
msgstr ""
"如果 `frame` 不是 DataFrame、缺少分箱方案中的某一列或该列出现两次，或者按数值列拟合的某一列有取值但不是数值 dtype，这可能使其特殊值无法匹配；请用 "
"``pandas.to_numeric`` 转换这样的列。错误信息会指明该列。"

msgid ":obj:`woe_transform`"
msgstr ":obj:`woe_transform`"

msgid "Encode the groups with the fitted WOE."
msgstr "用拟合的 WOE 对分组编码。"

msgid "Encode every column of a sample with the WOE fitted in development."
msgstr "用开发时拟合的 WOE 对样本的每一列编码。"

msgid ""
"The columns are grouped as by `cut`, and each group is replaced with its WOE by "
"`kivi.woe.woe_transform`. A group that is not in a column's table, such as a new category, gets "
"the column's unseen policy, which by default raises an error."
msgstr ""
"各列先按 `cut` 的方式分组，再由 `kivi.woe.woe_transform` 把每个分组替换为其 WOE。不在该列 WOE "
"表中的分组（例如新类别）按该列的未见分组策略处理，默认会引发错误。"

msgid "Float WOE values of each column of the specification, in its order, with the index of `frame`."
msgstr "分箱方案中每一列的浮点 WOE 值，按分箱方案的顺序排列，索引与 `frame` 相同。"

msgid ""
"If `frame` is not a DataFrame, lacks a column of the specification or has it twice, a column "
"fitted as numeric has values but not a numeric dtype, or a column with the unseen policy "
"``\"raise\"`` has values whose group is not in its table. The message names the column."
msgstr ""
"如果 `frame` 不是 DataFrame、缺少分箱方案中的某一列或该列出现两次，按数值列拟合的某一列有取值但不是数值 dtype，或者未见分组策略为 ``\"raise\"`` "
"的列含有分组不在其 WOE 表中的取值。错误信息会指明该列。"

msgid "Group the columns without encoding them."
msgstr "只对各列分组，不编码。"

msgid "Encode one column."
msgstr "对单列编码。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points`"

msgid "Turn the WOE values into points."
msgstr "把 WOE 值转换为分值。"

msgid ""
"The intervals of the edges are closed on the right, so ``-inf`` falls outside every interval. "
"`cut` leaves it missing, as ``pandas.cut`` does, and `woe_transform` treats it as unseen rather "
"than giving it the WOE of missing values."
msgstr ""
"由边界构成的区间为左开右闭，因此 ``-inf`` 不落入任何区间。 `cut` 与 ``pandas.cut`` 一样把它留为缺失值，而 `woe_transform` "
"把它视为未见分组，而不是赋予缺失组的 WOE。"

msgid "With an unseen WOE for ``housing``, the new label gets 0:"
msgstr "为 ``housing`` 指定未见分组的 WOE 后，新标签得到 0："

msgid "Return the specification of some of the columns."
msgstr "返回只含部分列的分箱方案。"

msgid ""
"Use it to keep only the variables of the final model before saving the specification for "
"production. The selected columns keep their edges, special codes, tables and unseen policies."
msgstr "在为生产环境保存分箱方案之前，可用它只保留最终模型的变量。选中的列保留各自的边界、特殊值、WOE 表和未见分组策略。"

msgid "sequence of str"
msgstr "str 序列"

msgid "Columns to keep, in the order of the new specification."
msgstr "要保留的列，其顺序即新分箱方案中的顺序。"

msgid "A specification of `columns` only."
msgstr "只含 `columns` 的分箱方案。"

msgid ""
"If `columns` is a string, is empty, repeats a column or names a column that is not in the "
"specification."
msgstr "如果 `columns` 是字符串、为空、重复某一列，或指定了分箱方案中没有的列。"

msgid ":obj:`columns`"
msgstr ":obj:`columns`"

msgid "The columns of the specification."
msgstr "分箱方案中的列。"

msgid ":obj:`to_json`"
msgstr ":obj:`to_json`"

msgid "Save the specification."
msgstr "保存分箱方案。"

msgid "Return the specification as a dict of JSON types."
msgstr "以由 JSON 类型构成的 dict 返回分箱方案。"

msgid ""
"The result holds only dicts, lists, strings, numbers, booleans and None, so ``json.dumps`` can "
"write it without further conversion. Its keys are always in the same order. `to_json` writes this"
" dict."
msgstr "结果只包含 dict、list、字符串、数值、布尔值和 None，因此 ``json.dumps`` 无需额外转换即可写出。其键的顺序始终相同。 `to_json` 写出的就是这个 dict。"

msgid "dict"
msgstr "dict"

msgid ""
"The keys ``format``, ``format_version``, ``kivi_version``, ``smoothing`` and ``variables``, a "
"list with one dict per column. See the user guide for the format."
msgstr ""
"包含键 ``format`` 、 ``format_version`` 、 ``kivi_version`` 、 ``smoothing`` 和 ``variables`` ；后者是每列一个 "
"dict 的列表。格式说明见用户指南。"

msgid ":obj:`from_dict`"
msgstr ":obj:`from_dict`"

msgid "Rebuild the specification."
msgstr "重建分箱方案。"

msgid "Write the dict as JSON."
msgstr "把该 dict 写成 JSON。"

msgid "Rebuild a specification from the result of `to_dict`."
msgstr "由 `to_dict` 的结果重建分箱方案。"

msgid ""
"The dict is checked before the specification is built, so that a damaged or hand-edited file "
"fails with a message that names the problem instead of encoding wrong values."
msgstr "构建分箱方案之前会先检查该 dict，因此损坏或被手工改动的文件会报错并指明问题，而不会编码出错误的值。"

msgid "**data**"
msgstr "**data**"

msgid "A dict in the format of `to_dict`, for example from ``json.load``."
msgstr "符合 `to_dict` 格式的 dict，例如来自 ``json.load`` 。"

msgid "The specification, equal to the one that wrote `data`."
msgstr "分箱方案，与写出 `data` 的那个相等。"

msgid ""
"If `data` is not a kivi binning specification, has a ``format_version`` newer than this version "
"of kivi reads, lacks a key or has an unknown one, or holds an invalid value. The message names "
"the column."
msgstr "如果 `data` 不是 kivi 分箱方案、其 ``format_version`` 比当前 kivi 能读取的版本更新、缺少某个键或含有未知的键，或含有无效的值。错误信息会指明相应的列。"

msgid ":obj:`to_dict`"
msgstr ":obj:`to_dict`"

msgid "The dict format."
msgstr "dict 格式。"

msgid ":obj:`from_json`"
msgstr ":obj:`from_json`"

msgid "Read the specification from JSON text."
msgstr "从 JSON 文本读取分箱方案。"

msgid "Return the specification as JSON text."
msgstr "以 JSON 文本返回分箱方案。"

msgid ""
"The text is the dict of `to_dict` written by ``json.dumps``. The same specification always gives "
"the same text, so saved specifications can be compared and kept under version control. Non-ASCII "
"labels are written as they are, so save the text as UTF-8."
msgstr ""
"该文本就是由 ``json.dumps`` 写出的 `to_dict` 的 dict。同一个分箱方案总是得到相同的文本，因此保存的分箱方案可以相互比较，并纳入版本控制。非 ASCII "
"标签按原样写出，因此请以 UTF-8 保存文本。"

msgid "**indent**"
msgstr "**indent**"

msgid "int, optional"
msgstr "int，可选"

msgid "Indentation of nested values, as in ``json.dumps``. By default the text is a single line."
msgstr "嵌套值的缩进，含义与 ``json.dumps`` 相同。默认文本只有一行。"

msgid "str"
msgstr "str"

msgid "JSON text that `from_json` reads back into an equal specification."
msgstr "JSON 文本， `from_json` 可将其读回为相等的分箱方案。"

msgid "Read the specification back."
msgstr "读回分箱方案。"

msgid "The same content as a dict."
msgstr "以 dict 表示的相同内容。"

msgid "Write the text to a file with ``Path(\"spec.json\").write_text(text, encoding=\"utf-8\")``."
msgstr "用 ``Path(\"spec.json\").write_text(text, encoding=\"utf-8\")`` 把文本写入文件。"

msgid "Read a specification from the JSON text of `to_json`."
msgstr "从 `to_json` 写出的 JSON 文本读取分箱方案。"

msgid ""
"The loaded specification groups and encodes every sample exactly as the one that was saved. A "
"file written by a newer version of the format is rejected rather than read in part."
msgstr "加载的分箱方案对每个样本的分组和编码，与保存时的分箱方案完全相同。由更新版本格式写出的文件会被拒绝，而不会只读取其中一部分。"

msgid "**text**"
msgstr "**text**"

msgid "str or bytes"
msgstr "str 或 bytes"

msgid "JSON text, for example from ``Path(...).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")``."
msgstr "JSON 文本，例如来自 ``Path(...).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")`` 。"

msgid "The specification, equal to the one that wrote `text`."
msgstr "分箱方案，与写出 `text` 的那个相等。"

msgid ""
"If `text` is neither a str nor bytes, is not valid JSON, contains ``NaN`` or ``Infinity``, or "
"does not describe a valid specification; see `from_dict`."
msgstr "如果 `text` 既不是 str 也不是 bytes、不是有效的 JSON、含有 ``NaN`` 或 ``Infinity`` ，或没有描述一个有效的分箱方案；参见 `from_dict` 。"

msgid "Write the specification."
msgstr "写出分箱方案。"

msgid "Rebuild the specification from a dict."
msgstr "由 dict 重建分箱方案。"

msgid "Population stability index"
msgstr "群体稳定性指标"

msgid ""
"Measure how far a distribution has shifted between two samples. :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table`"
" and :func:`~kivi.stability.psi` give the population stability index, and "
":func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` gives the change of a scorecard's average points that the shift"
" causes."
msgstr ""
"衡量分布在两个样本之间偏移了多少。 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 和 :func:`~kivi.stability.psi` 给出群体稳定性指标， "
":func:`~kivi.stability.csi_table` 给出这种偏移使评分卡平均分值发生的变化。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/psi` for examples and the usual thresholds."
msgstr "示例和常用阈值见 :doc:`/user_guide/psi` 。"

msgid ":py:obj:`psi_table <kivi.stability.psi_table>`\\ \\(reference\\, current\\, \\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`psi_table <kivi.stability.psi_table>`\\ \\(reference\\, current\\, \\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Compare two samples using their population stability index."
msgstr "通过群体稳定性指标（PSI）比较两个样本的分布。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`psi <kivi.stability.psi>`\\ \\(reference\\_counts\\, current\\_counts\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`psi <kivi.stability.psi>`\\ \\(reference\\_counts\\, current\\_counts\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the population stability index from counts per group."
msgstr "根据每组的计数计算群体稳定性指标（PSI）。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`csi_table <kivi.stability.csi_table>`\\ \\(reference\\, current\\, points\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`csi_table <kivi.stability.csi_table>`\\ \\(reference\\, current\\, points\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Measure how much a variable's shift moves the average score."
msgstr "衡量变量分布的变化使平均分数移动了多少。"

msgid ""
"Each group's share of the current sample is compared with its share of the reference sample. Sum "
"the ``psi`` column for the index."
msgstr "比较每组在当前样本中的占比与在基准样本中的占比。将 ``psi`` 列求和即得到该指数。"

msgid "**reference, current**"
msgstr "**reference, current**"

msgid ""
"Labels or values binned using the same edges. Missing values and categories observed in only one "
"sample are included."
msgstr "类别标签或按相同边界分箱的数值。保留缺失值以及仅出现在一侧的类别。"

msgid "Positive replacement for a zero count when calculating shares."
msgstr "计算占比时，用这个正数替代零计数。"

msgid "**reference_weights, current_weights**"
msgstr "**reference_weights, current_weights**"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation in the reference and the current sample, matched like the"
" samples. The counts are then sums of weights, and groups whose weights sum to zero in both "
"samples are left out. `smoothing` is then in units of weight."
msgstr "基准样本和当前样本中每个观测的非负权重，对应方式与样本相同。此时计数为权重之和，在两个样本中权重之和都为零的组会被排除，且 `smoothing` 以权重为单位。"

msgid ""
"Counts, normalized shares and the PSI contribution of each group. Sum the psi column for the "
"population stability index."
msgstr "各组的原始计数、归一化占比和 PSI 贡献。对 psi 列求和即得到总体 PSI。"

msgid ""
"If either sample is empty or not one-dimensional, or `smoothing` is not finite and positive. Also"
" if a weight array is not numeric, does not give each observation of its sample one finite, non-"
"negative weight with a positive total, or has an index other than that of its sample."
msgstr "如果任一样本为空或不是一维，或者 `smoothing` 不是有限正数。此外，如果某个权重数组不是数值、没有为对应样本的每个观测给出一个有限非负的权重、权重总和不为正，或其索引与对应样本不同。"

msgid ":obj:`psi`"
msgstr ":obj:`psi`"

msgid "The same index from counts per group."
msgstr "根据每组计数计算同一指标。"

msgid ":obj:`csi_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`csi_table`"

msgid "Weight the change of each group's share with its points."
msgstr "以分组分值为权重衡量每组占比的变化。"

msgid "Fit edges on the reference sample."
msgstr "在基准样本上拟合分箱边界。"

msgid "Relate the groups to a binary target."
msgstr "将分组与二分类目标关联起来。"

msgid ""
"For group :math:`i`, let :math:`q_i` be its share of the reference sample and :math:`p_i` its "
"share of the current sample. Then"
msgstr "对第 :math:`i` 组，令 :math:`q_i` 为其在基准样本中的占比，:math:`p_i` 为其在当前样本中的占比，则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{PSI}_i = (p_i - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{PSI} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{PSI}_i."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{PSI}_i = (p_i - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{PSI} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{PSI}_i."

msgid ""
"Each zero count is replaced with `smoothing` before the shares are normalized, so a group "
"observed in only one sample has a finite contribution. The ``reference`` and ``current`` columns "
"always report the observed counts."
msgstr "在归一化占比之前，每个零计数都会被替换为 `smoothing`，因此只在一个样本中出现的组也有有限的贡献值。 ``reference`` 和 ``current`` 列始终报告实际观测到的计数。"

msgid ""
"If both samples are categorical with the same categories, rows follow the order of the categories"
" with missing values last. Otherwise they follow the order in which the groups first appear, in "
"the reference sample and then in the current sample."
msgstr "如果两个样本都是分类型且类别相同，各行按类别顺序排列，缺失值排在最后。否则按分组首次出现的次序排列，先看基准样本，再看当前样本。"

msgid "[Rb11431c5e9a8-1]_"
msgstr "[Rb11431c5e9a8-1]_"

msgid ""
"Use this when the samples are already aggregated, for example monthly counts per score band from "
"a monitoring report."
msgstr "适用于样本已经汇总的情况，例如监控报表中按分数段统计的月度计数。"

msgid "**reference_counts, current_counts**"
msgstr "**reference_counts, current_counts**"

msgid ""
"One-dimensional, non-negative counts of each group in the reference and the current sample, in "
"the same group order. Weighted counts need not be integers."
msgstr "基准样本和当前样本中每组的一维非负计数，两者的分组顺序须一致。加权计数不必是整数。"

msgid "The population stability index."
msgstr "群体稳定性指标。"

msgid ""
"If the counts are not one-dimensional, numeric, finite and non-negative, have different lengths "
"or a zero total, or `smoothing` is not finite and positive."
msgstr "如果计数不是一维、不是数值、不是有限非负数，两组计数长度不同或总和为零，或者 `smoothing` 不是有限正数。"

msgid ":obj:`psi_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`psi_table`"

msgid "The index and its contributions from group labels."
msgstr "根据分组标签计算该指标及各组贡献。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.woe.iv`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.woe.iv`"

msgid "The same divergence between events and non-events."
msgstr "事件与非事件之间的同一种散度。"

msgid ""
"With :math:`q_i` and :math:`p_i` the smoothed shares of group :math:`i` in the reference and the "
"current sample,"
msgstr "记 :math:`q_i` 和 :math:`p_i` 为第 :math:`i` 组在基准样本和当前样本中平滑后的占比，则"

msgid "which equals the sum of the ``psi`` column of `psi_table` for the same groups."
msgstr "它等于相同分组下 `psi_table` 中 ``psi`` 列之和。"

msgid ""
"The characteristic stability index (CSI) weights the change of each group's share, from the "
"reference to the current sample, with the scorecard points of the group. Sum the ``csi`` column "
"for the change of the variable's average points."
msgstr "特征稳定性指标（CSI）以每组的评分卡分值为权重，衡量各组占比从基准样本到当前样本的变化。将 ``csi`` 列求和，即得到该变量平均分值的变化。"

msgid ""
"Labels or values binned using the same edges, as for `psi_table`. Missing values and groups "
"observed in only one sample are included."
msgstr "类别标签或按相同边界分箱的数值，与 `psi_table` 相同。保留缺失值以及仅出现在一个样本中的分组。"

msgid "pandas.DataFrame, pandas.Series or mapping"
msgstr "pandas.DataFrame、pandas.Series 或 mapping"

msgid ""
"Points of each group. A DataFrame holds the groups of one variable in a ``bin`` column, or in its"
" index without one, and their points in a ``points`` column, such as ``table.loc[[variable]]`` of"
" a `kivi.scorecard.points_table` result. A Series or mapping gives the points by group. A missing"
" label gives the points of missing values."
msgstr ""
"每个分组的分值。DataFrame 把一个变量的分组放在 ``bin`` 列中（没有该列时放在索引中），把分值放在 ``points`` 列中，例如 "
"`kivi.scorecard.points_table` 结果的 ``table.loc[[variable]]`` 。Series 或映射按分组给出分值。缺失标签给出缺失值的分值。"

msgid "float, optional"
msgstr "float，可选"

msgid ""
"Points of observed groups that are missing from `points`, such as a new category that "
"`kivi.woe.woe_transform` encoded with ``unseen``. Its applicants receive the "
"`kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` result for that WOE, not the WOE itself; see the Notes. By default"
" such groups raise an error."
msgstr ""
"`points` 中缺少的已观测分组的分值，例如 `kivi.woe.woe_transform` 用 ``unseen`` 编码的新类别。这些申请人得到的是对该 WOE 调用 "
"`kivi.scorecard.woe_to_points` 的结果，而不是 WOE 本身；参见“说明”。默认情况下，这样的分组会引发错误。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation in the reference and the current sample, matched like the"
" samples. The counts and shares are then sums of weights, and groups whose weights sum to zero in"
" both samples are left out."
msgstr "基准样本和当前样本中每个观测的非负权重，对应方式与样本相同。此时计数和占比都基于权重之和，在两个样本中权重之和都为零的组会被排除。"

msgid ""
"One row per observed group, indexed by ``bin``, with the counts ``reference`` and ``current``, "
"their shares ``reference_share`` and ``current_share``, the group's ``points`` and its "
"contribution ``csi``. Sum the csi column for the index."
msgstr ""
"每个观测到的分组一行，以 ``bin`` 为索引，列出计数 ``reference`` 和 ``current`` 、占比 ``reference_share`` 和 "
"``current_share`` 、该组的 ``points`` 及其贡献 ``csi`` 。将 csi 列求和即得到该指标。"

msgid ""
"If either sample is empty or not one-dimensional, `points` is not a DataFrame, Series or mapping,"
" holds more than one variable, repeats a group or has values that are not finite numbers, "
"`unseen_points` is not a finite number, or an observed group has no points and `unseen_points` is"
" not given. Also if a weight array is invalid, as in `psi_table`."
msgstr ""
"如果任一样本为空或不是一维的， `points` 不是 DataFrame、Series 或映射，包含多个变量、重复某个分组或含有不是有限数的值， `unseen_points` "
"不是有限数，或者某个观测到的分组没有分值且未给出 `unseen_points` 。此外，权重数组无效时也会引发错误，与 `psi_table` 相同。"

msgid "The population stability index of the same groups."
msgstr "相同分组的群体稳定性指标。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.scorecard.points_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.scorecard.points_table`"

msgid "The points of every group of a scorecard."
msgstr "评分卡每个分组的分值。"

msgid ""
"For group :math:`i` with points :math:`s_i`, let :math:`q_i` be its share of the reference sample"
" and :math:`p_i` its share of the current sample. Then"
msgstr "对分值为 :math:`s_i` 的第 :math:`i` 组，令 :math:`q_i` 为其在基准样本中的占比， :math:`p_i` 为其在当前样本中的占比，则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{CSI}_i = (p_i - q_i)\\, s_i, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{CSI} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{CSI}_i\n"
"= \\sum_i p_i s_i - \\sum_i q_i s_i,"
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{CSI}_i = (p_i - q_i)\\, s_i, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{CSI} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{CSI}_i\n"
"= \\sum_i p_i s_i - \\sum_i q_i s_i,"

msgid ""
"the average points of the variable in the current sample minus those in the reference sample "
"[R05dcc8ea5547-1]_. The shares sum to 1 in both samples, so adding the same number to the points "
"of every group leaves the CSI unchanged: only the differences between the groups count, not the "
"share of the intercept and offset that `kivi.scorecard.points_table` gives each variable. Over "
"all variables of a scorecard, the CSI values add up to the change of the average score."
msgstr ""
"即该变量在当前样本中的平均分值减去在基准样本中的平均分值 [R05dcc8ea5547-1]_ 。两个样本的占比之和都为 1，因此给每组的分值加上同一个数不会改变 "
"CSI：起作用的只是各组之间的差别，而不是 `kivi.scorecard.points_table` 分摊给每个变量的截距和偏移量份额。对评分卡的所有变量，CSI 之和就是平均分数的变化。"

msgid ""
"Unlike in `psi_table`, the shares are not smoothed. A contribution has no logarithm, so an empty "
"group contributes a finite amount without smoothing, and a smoothed share would credit an empty "
"group with applicants it does not have, so the sum would no longer be the change of the average "
"points."
msgstr "与 `psi_table` 不同，这里的占比不做平滑。贡献中没有对数，因此空组不经平滑也只有有限的贡献；而平滑后的占比会让空组拥有它并没有的申请人，求和结果也就不再是平均分值的变化。"

msgid ""
"`unseen_points` is in points, like `points`. For applicants that ``woe_transform(..., "
"unseen=woe)`` encoded, it is ``woe_to_points`` of a one-row frame that holds that WOE; a WOE of 0"
" gives the variable's share of the intercept and offset, the same for every variable. Passing the"
" WOE itself would give a wrong CSI without an error."
msgstr ""
"`unseen_points` 与 `points` 一样以分值为单位。对 ``woe_transform(..., unseen=woe)`` 编码的申请人，它是对包含该 WOE "
"的单行数据调用 ``woe_to_points`` 的结果；WOE 为 0 时得到该变量分摊的截距和偏移量份额，每个变量都相同。如果直接传入 WOE 本身，会在没有任何报错的情况下得到错误的 "
"CSI。"

msgid ""
"Some texts also call the PSI of a single variable its CSI; that is `psi_table` of the variable's "
"groups. Rows are ordered as in `psi_table`, and groups of `points` observed in neither sample are"
" left out, since they contribute nothing."
msgstr ""
"有些文献也把单个变量的 PSI 称为它的 CSI，那就是对该变量的分组调用 `psi_table` 的结果。各行顺序与 `psi_table` 相同； `points` "
"中在两个样本里都没有出现的分组不计入，因为它们没有贡献。"

msgid "[R05dcc8ea5547-1]_"
msgstr "[R05dcc8ea5547-1]_"

msgid "The average points fall from 32.5 to 28.75, by the sum of the ``csi`` column, -3.75."
msgstr "平均分值从 32.5 降到 28.75，降幅即 ``csi`` 列之和 -3.75。"

msgid "Credit strategy"
msgstr "信贷策略"

msgid ""
"Turn scores and PDs into credit decisions. :func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` shows what each "
"cut-off approves, :func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` compares the decisions of two scores, and "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss` and :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table` give the "
"expected loss of each exposure and of each grade."
msgstr ""
"把评分和 PD 转化为信贷决策。 :func:`~kivi.strategy.cutoff_table` 显示每个截断点通过哪些申请人， "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.swap_set` 比较两个评分的决策， :func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss` 和 "
":func:`~kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table` 给出每笔敞口和每个等级的预期损失。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/strategy` for examples on the bundled data."
msgstr "基于内置数据的示例见 :doc:`/user_guide/strategy` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`cutoff_table <kivi.strategy.cutoff_table>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, cutoffs\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`cutoff_table <kivi.strategy.cutoff_table>`\\ \\(score\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, cutoffs\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Summarize the approved book and the rejected events at each cut-off."
msgstr "汇总每个截断点下通过客群的情况及被拒绝的事件。"

msgid ":py:obj:`swap_set <kivi.strategy.swap_set>`\\ \\(current\\, new\\[\\, target\\, weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`swap_set <kivi.strategy.swap_set>`\\ \\(current\\, new\\[\\, target\\, weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Compare the decisions of a current and a new score at their cut-offs."
msgstr "在各自的截断点上比较现行评分与新评分的审批决策。"

msgid ":py:obj:`expected_loss <kivi.strategy.expected_loss>`\\ \\(probability\\, lgd\\, ead\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`expected_loss <kivi.strategy.expected_loss>`\\ \\(probability\\, lgd\\, ead\\)"

msgid "Compute the expected loss of each exposure from its PD, LGD and EAD."
msgstr "根据 PD、LGD 和 EAD 计算每笔敞口的预期损失。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`expected_loss_table <kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, probability\\, "
"...\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`expected_loss_table <kivi.strategy.expected_loss_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, probability\\, "
"...\\)"

msgid "Summarize exposure and expected loss by grade or other group."
msgstr "按等级或其他分组汇总敞口和预期损失。"

msgid ""
"A cut-off approves every observation whose score is at or below it, so a higher cut-off approves "
"more applicants and lets more events through. Each row shows the size and the event rate of the "
"approved book and the shares of events and non-events that the cut-off rejects."
msgstr "截断点通过所有评分不高于它的观测，因此截断点越高，通过的申请人越多，放进来的事件也越多。每一行给出通过客群的规模和事件率，以及该截断点拒绝的事件和非事件所占的比例。"

msgid ""
"Finite numeric scores that are higher for a higher risk, such as a PD. Negate scorecard points, "
"which are higher for a lower risk."
msgstr "有限的数值评分，风险越高，评分越高，例如 PD。评分卡分数越高表示风险越低，因此须取负后再传入。"

msgid "**cutoffs**"
msgstr "**cutoffs**"

msgid ""
"Number of quantile cut-offs, or increasing cut-off values. An integer `n` uses the edges of "
"``kivi.binning.bin_edges(score, bins=n)`` above the lowest, so the rows approve about 1/n, 2/n "
"and so on up to all of the sample, and tied scores can leave fewer rows. Pass explicit values as "
"a sequence, also for a single cut-off, such as ``[0.1]``. With `weights`, an integer gives "
"weighted quantiles, as ``bin_edges(score, bins=n, weights=weights)`` does."
msgstr ""
"分位数截断点的数量，或递增的截断点取值。整数 `n` 使用 ``kivi.binning.bin_edges(score, bins=n)`` 中最低边界以上的各个边界，因此各行大约通过样本的 "
"1/n、2/n，依此类推直至全部样本；相同评分可能使行数减少。显式取值须以序列传入，单个截断点也是如此，例如 ``[0.1]`` 。使用 `weights` 时，整数会得到加权分位数，与 "
"``bin_edges(score, bins=n, weights=weights)`` 相同。"

msgid "**loss**"
msgstr "**loss**"

msgid ""
"Non-negative loss of each observation, matched like `target`, such as its expected loss from "
"`expected_loss` or the loss realized on a defaulted account. The table then has a column "
"``approved_loss``."
msgstr "每个观测的非负损失，对应方式与 `target` 相同，例如由 `expected_loss` 得到的预期损失，或违约账户的实际损失。此时表中会增加一列 ``approved_loss`` 。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, such as the inverse of its sampling rate, matched like "
"`target`. Counts and losses become sums of weights. On the same cut-offs, integer weights give "
"the same table as repeating rows; an integer `cutoffs` can give other cut-offs, because weighted "
"quantiles use the inverted CDF."
msgstr ""
"每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` 相同。计数和损失变为权重之和。在相同截断点上，整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同；而整数 `cutoffs` "
"可能得到不同的截断点，因为加权分位数采用逆累积分布（inverted CDF）。"

msgid ""
"One row per cut-off, from the lowest to the highest, indexed by the cut-off value. The columns "
"are described in the Notes."
msgstr "每个截断点一行，从低到高排列，以截断点取值为索引。各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` "
"has a label other than 0 and 1 or lacks one of them, `score` is not real and numeric or has a "
"missing or infinite value, or `cutoffs` is neither a positive integer nor a sequence of "
"increasing numbers. Also if `loss` is not numeric or does not give each observation one finite, "
"non-negative loss, or `weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one finite, non-"
"negative weight, has an index other than that of `score`, or leaves a class without weight."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，索引或长度不一致，`target` 含有 0 和 1 以外的标签或缺少其中之一，`score` 不是实数数值或含有缺失值、无穷值，或 `cutoffs` "
"既不是正整数也不是递增数值的序列。此外，如果 `loss` 不是数值或没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负的损失，或 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负的权重、索引与 "
"`score` 不同，或使某一类没有权重。"

msgid ""
"If `cutoffs` is an integer and tied scores leave fewer cut-offs than requested, as in "
"`kivi.binning.bin_edges`."
msgstr "如果 `cutoffs` 是整数，且相同评分使截断点少于请求的数量，与 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` 相同。"

msgid ":obj:`swap_set`"
msgstr ":obj:`swap_set`"

msgid "Compare the decisions of two scores at their cut-offs."
msgstr "在各自的截断点上比较两个评分的审批决策。"

msgid ":obj:`expected_loss`"
msgstr ":obj:`expected_loss`"

msgid "Expected loss of each exposure, to pass as `loss`."
msgstr "每笔敞口的预期损失，可作为 `loss` 传入。"

msgid "Event rates of the bands between cut-offs."
msgstr "相邻截断点之间各评分段的事件率。"

msgid ""
"A score equal to the cut-off is approved, so tied scores always get the same decision. With the "
"cut-offs of an integer `cutoffs`, the approved book of a row consists of the bands of "
"``kivi.metrics.gains_table`` with ``bins=cutoffs`` up to that cut-off."
msgstr ""
"等于截断点的评分予以通过，因此相同评分总是得到相同的决策。对于整数 `cutoffs` 给出的截断点，某一行的通过客群由 ``bins=cutoffs`` 时 "
"``kivi.metrics.gains_table`` 中直至该截断点的各评分段组成。"

msgid "``approved``: observations with a score at or below the cut-off, or the sum of their weights;"
msgstr "``approved``：评分不高于截断点的观测数，或它们的权重之和；"

msgid "``approval_rate``: ``approved`` divided by the whole sample;"
msgstr "``approval_rate``：``approved`` 除以整个样本；"

msgid "``approved_event``: events among the approved observations;"
msgstr "``approved_event``：通过的观测中的事件数；"

msgid ""
"``approved_event_rate``: ``approved_event`` divided by ``approved``, the bad rate of the approved"
" book, NaN when nothing is approved;"
msgstr "``approved_event_rate``：``approved_event`` 除以 ``approved``，即通过客群的坏账率；没有通过任何观测时为 NaN；"

msgid ""
"``rejected_event_share`` and ``rejected_non_event_share``: shares of all events and of all non-"
"events with a score above the cut-off;"
msgstr "``rejected_event_share`` 和 ``rejected_non_event_share``：评分高于截断点的事件和非事件分别占全部事件和全部非事件的比例；"

msgid ""
"``approved_loss``: with `loss`, the sum of the losses of the approved observations, weighted with"
" `weights`."
msgstr "``approved_loss``：传入 `loss` 时，通过的观测的损失之和，按 `weights` 加权。"

msgid ""
"A higher cut-off raises the approval rate and lowers both rejected shares. "
"``rejected_event_share`` is the share of bad outcomes the cut-off avoids, and "
"``rejected_non_event_share`` the share of good business it gives up."
msgstr ""
"截断点越高，通过率越高，两个拒绝比例都越低。``rejected_event_share`` 是该截断点避开的坏结果所占比例，``rejected_non_event_share`` "
"是它放弃的好业务所占比例。"

msgid ""
"Each score approves the observations at or below its cut-off. The four rows are the observations "
"both scores approve, the swap-outs that only the current score approves, the swap-ins that only "
"the new score approves, and those both decline."
msgstr "每个评分通过不高于其截断点的观测。四行依次为：两个评分都通过的观测、只有现行评分通过的换出（swap-out）、只有新评分通过的换入（swap-in），以及两个评分都拒绝的观测。"

msgid "**current**"
msgstr "**current**"

msgid ""
"Finite numeric scores of the current model, higher for a higher risk, such as a PD. Negate "
"scorecard points."
msgstr "现行模型的有限数值评分，风险越高，评分越高，例如 PD。评分卡分数须取负。"

msgid "**new**"
msgstr "**new**"

msgid ""
"Finite numeric scores of the new model, of the same length as `current` and higher for a higher "
"risk. The two scores need not be on the same scale."
msgstr "新模型的有限数值评分，长度与 `current` 相同，风险越高，评分越高。两个评分不必采用同一刻度。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event, and missing values for unknown outcomes, such as the "
"applicants the current score declined. Without `target`, the table only counts the observations."
msgstr "二元标签，1 表示事件，缺失值表示结果未知，例如被现行评分拒绝的申请人。不传入 `target` 时，表中只统计观测数。"

msgid "**current_cutoff**"
msgstr "**current_cutoff**"

msgid "Cut-off of the current score. Observations with a `current` score at or below it are approved."
msgstr "现行评分的截断点。`current` 评分不高于它的观测予以通过。"

msgid "**new_cutoff**"
msgstr "**new_cutoff**"

msgid "Cut-off of the new score, applied in the same way to `new`."
msgstr "新评分的截断点，以同样方式作用于 `new`。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, such as the inverse of its sampling rate. Counts become "
"sums of weights, so integer weights give the same table as repeating rows."
msgstr "每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数。计数变为权重之和，因此整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同。"

msgid ""
"Four rows indexed by the decisions of the two scores, ``current`` and ``new``, each "
"``\"approve\"`` or ``\"decline\"``. The columns are ``total`` and ``share``, and with `target` "
"also ``known``, ``event`` and ``event_rate``; see the Notes."
msgstr ""
"四行，以两个评分的决策 ``current`` 和 ``new`` 为索引，取值均为 ``\"approve\"`` 或 ``\"decline\"``。列为 ``total`` 和 "
"``share``，传入 `target` 时还有 ``known``、``event`` 和 ``event_rate``；见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty or not one-dimensional, their lengths differ, or they are Series with "
"different indices; `current` or `new` is not real and numeric or has a missing or infinite value;"
" `target` has a value other than 0, 1 and missing; a cut-off is not a number or is missing; or "
"`weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one finite, non-negative weight with a "
"positive total, or has an index other than that of `current`."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空或不是一维的，长度不同，或为索引不同的 Series；`current` 或 `new` 不是实数数值或含有缺失值、无穷值；`target` 含有 0、1 "
"和缺失值以外的值；截断点不是数值或为缺失值；或 `weights` 不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负且总和为正的权重，或索引与 `current` 不同。"

msgid ":obj:`cutoff_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`cutoff_table`"

msgid "Approval and event rates over a range of cut-offs."
msgstr "一系列截断点下的通过率和事件率。"

msgid "Infer the outcomes of declined applicants."
msgstr "推断被拒申请人的结果。"

msgid ""
"The rows ``(\"approve\", \"decline\")`` and ``(\"decline\", \"approve\")`` are the swap-outs and "
"the swap-ins. Every row is reported, also when it is empty. The columns are:"
msgstr "``(\"approve\", \"decline\")`` 和 ``(\"decline\", \"approve\")`` 两行分别是换出和换入。每一行都会列出，即使为空。各列为："

msgid "``total``: observations in the row, or the sum of their weights;"
msgstr "``total``：该行的观测数，或它们的权重之和；"

msgid "``share``: ``total`` divided by the whole sample;"
msgstr "``share``：``total`` 除以整个样本；"

msgid "``known``: observations in the row with a known outcome;"
msgstr "``known``：该行中结果已知的观测数；"

msgid "``event``: events in the row;"
msgstr "``event``：该行的事件数；"

msgid "``event_rate``: ``event`` divided by ``known``, NaN without known outcomes."
msgstr "``event_rate``：``event`` 除以 ``known``；没有已知结果时为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"The outcomes of the applicants the current score declined are usually unknown, because they never"
" received a loan. The rows of current declines, including the swap-ins, then have no "
"``event_rate``, and the swap set alone cannot show whether the new score accepts better "
"applicants than it rejects. Reject inference estimates the missing outcomes; pass the inferred "
"labels, with weights for an augmented sample, to complete the table."
msgstr ""
"被现行评分拒绝的申请人从未获得贷款，因此其结果通常未知。这时现行评分拒绝的各行（包括换入）没有 "
"``event_rate``，仅凭交换集无法判断新评分接受的申请人是否优于它拒绝的申请人。拒绝推断可以估计缺失的结果；传入推断得到的标签（对扩充样本还需传入权重），即可补全该表。"

msgid "The current declines usually have no known outcome:"
msgstr "现行评分拒绝的申请人通常没有已知结果："

msgid ""
"The expected loss is the product of the probability of default, the loss given default and the "
"exposure at default."
msgstr "预期损失是违约概率、违约损失率与违约风险敞口的乘积。"

msgid "Probabilities of default, from 0 to 1. Missing values give missing losses."
msgstr "违约概率，取值在 0 到 1 之间。缺失值对应的损失也为缺失。"

msgid "**lgd**"
msgstr "**lgd**"

msgid ""
"Loss given default as a share of the exposure, from 0 to 1, as one value for all exposures or one"
" per exposure."
msgstr "违约损失率，即损失占敞口的比例，取值在 0 到 1 之间；可以为所有敞口给出一个值，也可以每笔敞口一个值。"

msgid "**ead**"
msgstr "**ead**"

msgid ""
"Exposure at default, such as the outstanding balance, finite and non-negative, as one value or "
"one per exposure."
msgstr "违约风险敞口，例如未偿余额，须为有限非负值；可以给出一个值，也可以每笔敞口一个值。"

msgid ""
"Expected losses, in the units of `ead`, with the broadcast shape of the inputs. If an input is a "
"Series, the result is a Series with its index and name; scalar inputs give a float."
msgstr "预期损失，单位与 `ead` 相同，形状为各输入广播后的形状。如果某个输入是 Series，结果为具有其索引和名称的 Series；输入均为标量时返回 float。"

msgid ""
"If an input is not real and numeric, the inputs cannot be broadcast together, Series inputs have "
"different indices, `probability` or `lgd` has a value outside [0, 1], or `ead` has a negative or "
"infinite value."
msgstr "如果某个输入不是实数数值，各输入无法一起广播，作为 Series 的输入索引不同，`probability` 或 `lgd` 含有 [0, 1] 以外的值，或 `ead` 含有负值或无穷值。"

msgid ":obj:`expected_loss_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`expected_loss_table`"

msgid "Exposure and expected loss by grade."
msgstr "按等级汇总的敞口和预期损失。"

msgid "Pass the expected losses as `loss` to sum them by cut-off."
msgstr "将预期损失作为 `loss` 传入，按截断点求和。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.scorecard.score_to_pd`"

msgid "The PD implied by a scorecard score."
msgstr "评分卡分数所对应的 PD。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For an exposure with probability of default :math:`\\mathrm{PD}`, loss given default "
":math:`\\mathrm{LGD}` and exposure at default :math:`\\mathrm{EAD}`,"
msgstr "对于违约概率为 :math:`\\mathrm{PD}`、违约损失率为 :math:`\\mathrm{LGD}`、违约风险敞口为 :math:`\\mathrm{EAD}` 的敞口，"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{EL} = \\mathrm{PD} \\times \\mathrm{LGD} \\times \\mathrm{EAD}."
msgstr "\\mathrm{EL} = \\mathrm{PD} \\times \\mathrm{LGD} \\times \\mathrm{EAD}."

msgid ""
"The PD refers to a horizon, usually one year, and the expected loss refers to the same horizon. "
"Missing values are not checked and give a missing loss."
msgstr "PD 对应一个期限，通常为一年，预期损失也对应同一期限。缺失值不做检查，对应的损失为缺失。"

msgid ""
"Each row adds up the exposures and expected losses of a group, such as a grade of a master scale,"
" and gives their ratio, the expected loss rate."
msgstr "每一行汇总一个分组（例如主标尺的一个等级）的敞口和预期损失，并给出两者之比，即预期损失率。"

msgid "Probability of default of each exposure, from 0 to 1, without missing values."
msgstr "每笔敞口的违约概率，取值在 0 到 1 之间，不得含有缺失值。"

msgid "Loss given default, from 0 to 1, as one value for all exposures or one per exposure."
msgstr "违约损失率，取值在 0 到 1 之间；可以为所有敞口给出一个值，也可以每笔敞口一个值。"

msgid ""
"Exposure at default, finite and non-negative, as one value or one per exposure. Series inputs "
"must have identical indices; otherwise the inputs are matched by position."
msgstr "违约风险敞口，须为有限非负值；可以给出一个值，也可以每笔敞口一个值。作为 Series 传入的输入，索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each exposure, such as the inverse of its sampling rate, matched like "
"`probability`. Counts, exposures and losses become sums of weights, so integer weights give the "
"same groups and sums as repeating rows, and groups whose weights sum to zero are left out. Groups"
" that are not categorical keep the order in which they first appear, also in rows of zero weight,"
" so their order can differ from that of repeated rows."
msgstr ""
"每笔敞口的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `probability` "
"相同。计数、敞口和损失都变为加权和，因此整数权重与重复相应行得到的分组和各项和相同；权重之和为零的分组不列出。非分类型的分组按首次出现的顺序排列，权重为零的行也计入顺序，因此其顺序可能与重复行不同。"

msgid "One row per group with the columns described in the Notes."
msgstr "每个分组一行，各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If `groups` or `probability` is empty or not one-dimensional, an input does not have one value "
"per exposure or a Series index other than that of the others, `probability`, `lgd` or `ead` is "
"not real and numeric or has a missing value, `probability` or `lgd` has a value outside [0, 1], "
"or `ead` has a negative or infinite value. Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each "
"exposure one finite, non-negative weight with a positive total, or has an index other than that "
"of `groups`."
msgstr ""
"如果 `groups` 或 `probability` 为空或不是一维的，某个输入没有为每笔敞口给出一个值，或其 Series 索引与其他输入不同，`probability`、`lgd` 或 "
"`ead` 不是实数数值或含有缺失值，`probability` 或 `lgd` 含有 [0, 1] 以外的值，或 `ead` 含有负值或无穷值。此外，如果 `weights` "
"不是数值、没有为每笔敞口给出一个有限非负且总和为正的权重，或索引与 `groups` 不同。"

msgid "Expected loss of each exposure."
msgstr "每笔敞口的预期损失。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.calibration.calibration_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.calibration.calibration_table`"

msgid "Observed and predicted default rates by grade."
msgstr "按等级比较实际与预测的违约率。"

msgid "For the exposures :math:`i` of a group, with weights :math:`w_i`, the columns are:"
msgstr "对于一个分组中权重为 :math:`w_i` 的敞口 :math:`i`，各列为："

msgid "``total``: the number of exposures, :math:`\\sum_i w_i`;"
msgstr "``total``：敞口数， :math:`\\sum_i w_i`；"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "``exposure``: :math:`\\sum_i w_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i`;"
msgstr "``exposure``： :math:`\\sum_i w_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i`；"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``exposure_weighted_probability``: :math:`\\sum_i w_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i \\mathrm{PD}_i / \\sum_i "
"w_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i`;"
msgstr ""
"``exposure_weighted_probability``： :math:`\\sum_i w_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i \\mathrm{PD}_i / \\sum_i "
"w_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i`；"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "``expected_loss``: :math:`\\sum_i w_i \\mathrm{PD}_i \\mathrm{LGD}_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i`;"
msgstr "``expected_loss``： :math:`\\sum_i w_i \\mathrm{PD}_i \\mathrm{LGD}_i \\mathrm{EAD}_i`；"

msgid "``expected_loss_rate``: ``expected_loss`` divided by ``exposure``."
msgstr "``expected_loss_rate``：``expected_loss`` 除以 ``exposure``。"

msgid ""
"The two ratios are NaN for a group without exposure. With one LGD for all exposures, "
"``expected_loss_rate`` is the LGD times ``exposure_weighted_probability``. The portfolio's "
"expected loss is the sum of the ``expected_loss`` column, and its expected loss rate is that sum "
"divided by the sum of ``exposure``."
msgstr ""
"没有敞口的分组，两个比率均为 NaN。所有敞口使用同一 LGD 时，``expected_loss_rate`` 等于 LGD 乘以 "
"``exposure_weighted_probability``。组合的预期损失是 ``expected_loss`` 列之和，其预期损失率是该和除以 ``exposure`` 之和。"

msgid "Univariate profile"
msgstr "单变量概况"

msgid ""
"Profile every column of a data frame in one row: how complete it is, how its values are "
"distributed and, with a binary target, how strongly it separates events from non-events. "
":func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` is the first look at the candidates of a model."
msgstr ""
"用一行概括数据框的每一列：完整程度、取值分布，以及在给出二元目标变量时区分事件与非事件的能力。 :func:`~kivi.univariate.profile_table` "
"是对模型候选变量的第一次全面审视。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/univariate` for an example and how to read the profile."
msgstr "示例以及如何解读概况表，见 :doc:`/user_guide/univariate` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`profile_table <kivi.univariate.profile_table>`\\ \\(frame\\[\\, target\\, columns\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`profile_table <kivi.univariate.profile_table>`\\ \\(frame\\[\\, target\\, columns\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Summarize each column of a data frame in one row."
msgstr "用一行概括数据框的每一列。"

msgid ""
"Every column gets its kind, its number of missing values and its most frequent value; numeric "
"columns also get their range, quantiles, mean and standard deviation. With a binary target, each "
"column also gets the event rates of its missing and non-missing rows, the information value of a "
"quick binning and, for numeric columns, the Gini coefficient of its values."
msgstr ""
"每一列都会给出其类型、缺失值个数和最常见的取值；数值列还给出取值范围、分位数、均值和标准差。有二分类目标时，每一列还会给出缺失行与非缺失行的事件率和快速分箱的信息值，数值列还给出其取值的 "
"Gini 系数。"

msgid ""
"One column per variable. Columns with a numeric dtype other than bool are numeric; all others, "
"such as object, string, category or bool, are categorical, as in `kivi.spec.fit_spec`."
msgstr ""
"每个变量一列。数值 dtype（bool 除外）的列是数值列；其他所有列（例如 object、string、category 或 bool）是类别列，与 `kivi.spec.fit_spec`"
" 相同。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event, one per row of `frame`. Both classes must be present."
" A Series must have the same index as `frame`; other inputs are matched by position. Without "
"`target` the table describes the columns only."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件， `frame` 的每一行一个。两类都必须出现。Series 必须与 `frame` 的索引相同；其他输入按位置对应。没有 `target` 时，表格只描述各列。"

msgid "Columns to profile, in the order of the rows. By default every column of `frame`."
msgstr "要分析的列，其顺序即结果中行的顺序。默认为 `frame` 的所有列。"

msgid ""
"Number of quantile bins of the quick binning of numeric columns, from `kivi.binning.bin_edges`, "
"for the ``iv`` column."
msgstr "数值列快速分箱的等频箱数，用于 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` ，结果见 ``iv`` 列。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Special codes of numeric columns, such as ``{\"pdays\": [-1]}``, as in `kivi.spec.fit_spec`. They"
" count as values, not as missing, but are left out of the numeric summary and of the Gini "
"coefficient, and each code forms its own group in the quick binning."
msgstr ""
"数值列的特殊值编码，例如 ``{\"pdays\": [-1]}`` ，与 `kivi.spec.fit_spec` 相同。它们算作取值而不算缺失，但不参与数值汇总和 Gini "
"系数，并在快速分箱中各自成组。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative frequency weight of each row, matched like `target`, such as the inverse of its "
"sampling rate. Counts become sums of weights and every statistic is weighted, so integer weights "
"give the same result as repeating rows with unit weights. Rows with zero weight count for "
"nothing, so their values are not checked."
msgstr ""
"每一行的非负频数权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` "
"相同。计数变为权重之和，每项统计量都加权计算，因此整数权重与重复相应行并使用单位权重的结果相同。权重为零的行不计入，因此也不检查其取值。"

msgid ""
"One row per column, indexed by the column names in an index named ``variable``. The columns are "
"described in the Notes."
msgstr "每列一行，以列名为索引，索引名为 ``variable`` 。各列含义见“说明”。"

msgid ""
"If `frame` is not a DataFrame or has no rows or no columns, `columns` repeats a column or names "
"one that `frame` lacks, a column name is not a string, or `bins` is not a positive integer. If "
"`target` does not give each row a label 0 or 1, lacks one of the two classes or is a column being"
" profiled, or if `weights` is invalid or leaves a class without weight. Also if `special` is not "
"a dict by column, names a column that is not profiled or is categorical, or has a code that is "
"not a number, or if a numeric column has infinite values that are not special codes."
msgstr ""
"如果 `frame` 不是 DataFrame、没有行或没有列， `columns` 重复某一列或指定了 `frame` 中没有的列，列名不是字符串，或 `bins` 不是正整数。如果 "
"`target` 的标签不是每行一个 0 或 1、缺少两类中的一类或是被分析的列之一，或者 `weights` 无效或使某一类没有权重。此外，如果 `special` 不是按列的 "
"dict、指定了未分析的列或类别列、含有不是数值的编码，或某个数值列含有不属于特殊值的无穷值。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.spec.fit_spec`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.spec.fit_spec`"

msgid "Bin and encode the columns chosen after profiling."
msgstr "对分析后选出的列进行分箱和编码。"

msgid "The WOE and IV of one grouped column."
msgstr "单个已分组列的 WOE 和 IV。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.metrics.gini`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.metrics.gini`"

msgid "The Gini coefficient of a score."
msgstr "评分的 Gini 系数。"

msgid "The quantile edges of the quick binning."
msgstr "快速分箱的分位数边界。"

msgid "Every column gets"
msgstr "每一列都包含"

msgid "``kind``: ``\"numeric\"`` or ``\"categorical\"``;"
msgstr "``kind`` ： ``\"numeric\"`` 或 ``\"categorical\"`` ；"

msgid ""
"``count`` and ``missing``: the number of rows with and without a value, and ``missing_share``, "
"the share of rows without one;"
msgstr "``count`` 和 ``missing`` ：有取值和无取值的行数； ``missing_share`` ：无取值的行所占的比例；"

msgid "``distinct``: the number of different values;"
msgstr "``distinct`` ：不同取值的个数；"

msgid ""
"``top`` and ``top_share``: the most frequent value and its share of the rows with a value. Of "
"values that are equally frequent, the first in the order of the categories, or else of "
"appearance, is shown;"
msgstr "``top`` 和 ``top_share`` ：最常见的取值及其在有取值的行中所占的比例。若多个取值同样常见，显示类别顺序中的第一个，没有类别顺序时显示最先出现的一个；"

msgid ""
"``special`` and ``special_share``: the number and share of rows with a special code, 0 for "
"categorical columns;"
msgstr "``special`` 和 ``special_share`` ：取特殊值编码的行数及其比例，类别列为 0；"

msgid ""
"``mean``, ``std``, ``min``, ``q01``, ``q50``, ``q99`` and ``max``: the mean, the sample standard "
"deviation, the smallest value, the 1%, 50% and 99% quantiles and the largest value of a numeric "
"column, without missing values and special codes. Categorical columns get NaN."
msgstr ""
"``mean`` 、 ``std`` 、 ``min`` 、 ``q01`` 、 ``q50`` 、 ``q99`` 和 ``max`` "
"：数值列去除缺失值和特殊值编码后的均值、样本标准差、最小值、1%、50% 和 99% 分位数以及最大值。类别列为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"The quantiles interpolate linearly, as ``numpy.quantile`` does; with `weights` they are weighted "
"quantiles by the inverted CDF, as the edges of `kivi.binning.bin_edges`. Weights, even unit "
"weights, therefore change the quantiles and, through the edges, ``iv`` and ``tied_bins``; with "
"integer weights every other column equals that of the repeated rows without weights. The standard"
" deviation divides by the total weight minus 1, as it divides by the number of rows minus 1 "
"without weights, so it is NaN when the weights of a column's values sum to 1 or less."
msgstr ""
"分位数按线性插值计算，与 ``numpy.quantile`` 相同；使用 `weights` 时，取逆累积分布（inverted CDF）意义下的加权分位数，与 "
"`kivi.binning.bin_edges` 的边界相同。因此权重（即使全为 1）会改变分位数，并通过边界改变 ``iv`` 和 ``tied_bins`` "
"；使用整数权重时，其他各列都等于不加权的重复行的结果。标准差除以总权重减 1，正如不加权时除以行数减 1，因此当某列取值的权重之和不超过 1 时，标准差为 NaN。"

msgid "With `target`, every column also gets"
msgstr "有 `target` 时，每一列还包含"

msgid "``event_rate``: the event rate of all rows, the same in every row of the table;"
msgstr "``event_rate`` ：全部行的事件率，在表格的每一行中都相同；"

msgid ""
"``missing_event_rate`` and ``non_missing_event_rate``: the event rates of the rows without and "
"with a value, NaN when there are no such rows;"
msgstr "``missing_event_rate`` 和 ``non_missing_event_rate`` ：无取值和有取值的行的事件率，没有这样的行时为 NaN；"

msgid ""
"``missing_lift`` and ``non_missing_lift``: these rates divided by ``event_rate``, so a lift above"
" 1 marks riskier rows;"
msgstr "``missing_lift`` 和 ``non_missing_lift`` ：上述事件率除以 ``event_rate`` ，提升度大于 1 表示这些行风险更高；"

msgid ""
"``iv``: the information value of the column, summed over the groups of `kivi.woe.woe_table`. "
"Numeric columns are cut into `bins` quantile bins with `kivi.binning.bin_edges` and "
"`kivi.binning.cut`, with a group for each special code; categorical columns keep their labels. "
"Missing values form a group of their own;"
msgstr ""
"``iv`` ：该列的信息值，即 `kivi.woe.woe_table` 各分组之和。数值列用 `kivi.binning.bin_edges` 和 `kivi.binning.cut` "
"切分为 `bins` 个等频箱，每个特殊值编码单独成组；类别列保留其标签。缺失值单独成组；"

msgid ""
"``tied_bins``: True where the quick binning of a numeric column has fewer bins than requested, "
"because tied quantiles were merged or no values are left to bin apart from missing values and "
"special codes. The table records this instead of warning for every column, as "
"`kivi.binning.bin_edges` does; such an IV understates the column until it is binned with custom "
"edges or special codes;"
msgstr ""
"``tied_bins`` ：数值列的快速分箱箱数少于所请求的箱数时为 True，原因是分位数重合而被合并，或者除缺失值和特殊值编码外没有可分箱的取值。表格记录这一情况，而不像 "
"`kivi.binning.bin_edges` 那样对每一列发出警告；在用自定义边界或特殊值编码分箱之前，这样的 IV 会低估该列；"

msgid ""
"``gini``: the Gini coefficient of the values of a numeric column as a score, without missing "
"values and special codes. It is positive when events have higher values, negative when they have "
"lower ones, and NaN for categorical columns or when the values leave out a class."
msgstr "``gini`` ：把数值列的取值作为评分时的 Gini 系数，不含缺失值和特殊值编码。事件的取值较高时为正，较低时为负；对类别列，或这些取值缺少某一类时，为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"The quick binning gives a first ranking, not a final one: an IV from five quantile bins can miss "
"a pattern that other edges would show, and a categorical column with many rare labels gets an "
"inflated IV."
msgstr "快速分箱只给出初步排序而非最终排序：五个等频箱的 IV 可能遗漏其他边界才能显示的规律，而含有许多稀有标签的类别列，IV 会被高估。"

msgid "With a target, the event rates and the separation of each column:"
msgstr "有目标变量时，给出各列的事件率和区分能力："

msgid "Vintage and roll-rate analysis"
msgstr "Vintage 与滚动率分析"

msgid ""
"Analyse a loan panel as the loans age. :func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` gives the cumulative "
"bad rate of each cohort by month on book, and :func:`~kivi.vintage.transition_matrix` and "
":func:`~kivi.vintage.roll_rates` show how loans move between delinquency buckets or grades."
msgstr ""
"随着贷款账龄增长分析贷款面板。 :func:`~kivi.vintage.vintage_table` 按账龄给出每个放款批次的累计坏账率， "
":func:`~kivi.vintage.transition_matrix` 和 :func:`~kivi.vintage.roll_rates` 展示贷款在逾期档位或等级之间的迁移。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/vintage` for examples on a synthetic loan panel."
msgstr "基于合成贷款面板的示例见 :doc:`/user_guide/vintage` 。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`vintage_table <kivi.vintage.vintage_table>`\\ \\(loan\\, cohort\\, month\\_on\\_book\\, "
"...\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`vintage_table <kivi.vintage.vintage_table>`\\ \\(loan\\, cohort\\, month\\_on\\_book\\, "
"...\\)"

msgid "Tabulate the cumulative bad rate of each cohort by month on book."
msgstr "按账龄列出每个批次的累计坏账率。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`transition_matrix <kivi.vintage.transition_matrix>`\\ \\(before\\, after\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`transition_matrix <kivi.vintage.transition_matrix>`\\ \\(before\\, after\\, \\*\\[\\, "
"...\\]\\)"

msgid "Count the movements of entities between two states."
msgstr "统计对象在两个状态之间的迁移次数。"

msgid ""
":py:obj:`roll_rates <kivi.vintage.roll_rates>`\\ \\(before\\, after\\, \\*\\[\\, states\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"
msgstr ""
":py:obj:`roll_rates <kivi.vintage.roll_rates>`\\ \\(before\\, after\\, \\*\\[\\, states\\, "
"weights\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the share of each state's entities that rolled to the next state."
msgstr "计算每个状态中滚动到下一状态的对象所占的比例。"

msgid ""
"A vintage table follows each cohort of loans, usually the loans originated in the same month, as "
"it ages. Its entry for a cohort and a month on book is the share of the cohort's loans that were "
"bad at or before that month on book, so every row is non-decreasing."
msgstr "Vintage 表（账龄表）跟踪每个贷款批次（通常是同一个月发放的贷款）随账龄增长的表现。某个批次在某个账龄上的取值，是该批次贷款中在该账龄或更早时已变坏的比例，因此每一行都不会递减。"

msgid "**loan**"
msgstr "**loan**"

msgid ""
"Identifier of the loan of each row of the panel. A loan has at most one row per month on book, "
"and its rows need not be sorted."
msgstr "面板中每一行所属贷款的标识。每笔贷款在每个账龄最多有一行，各行无需排序。"

msgid "**cohort**"
msgstr "**cohort**"

msgid ""
"Cohort of each row, such as the month of origination. It must be the same on every row of a loan."
" Cohorts are sorted, and categorical cohorts follow the order of their categories."
msgstr "每一行的批次，例如放款月份。同一笔贷款的每一行批次必须相同。批次会被排序；分类型批次按其类别顺序排列。"

msgid "**month_on_book**"
msgstr "**month_on_book**"

msgid "Whole number of months since origination of each row."
msgstr "每一行距放款的整月数。"

msgid "**bad**"
msgstr "**bad**"

msgid ""
"Whether the loan is bad at that month on book, as booleans or 0 and 1. Pass the bad definition as"
" a condition on the status, such as ``status == \"90+\"``, or ``status >= \"60-89\"`` for an "
"ordered categorical."
msgstr ""
"该贷款在该账龄时是否为坏，取布尔值或 0 和 1。坏的定义以状态上的条件传入，例如 ``status == \"90+\"`` ；对于有序分类变量，也可以写成 ``status >= "
"\"60-89\"`` 。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each loan, such as the amount lent, repeated on every row of the loan. The"
" table then reports the share of the cohort's weight in loans that were bad, and cohorts whose "
"weights sum to zero are left out."
msgstr "每笔贷款的非负权重，例如放款金额，在该贷款的每一行重复给出。此时表中报告的是批次权重中属于坏贷款的比例，权重之和为零的批次会被排除。"

msgid ""
"Cumulative bad rates with one row per cohort and one column per distinct month on book of the "
"panel. An entry is NaN outside the months on book at which the cohort is observed, from the "
"smallest to the largest month on book of its rows."
msgstr "累计坏账率：每个批次一行，面板中每个不同的账龄一列。在批次被观测的账龄范围（从其各行中最小的账龄到最大的账龄）之外，取值为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty, not one-dimensional or of different lengths, or Series with different "
"indices. Also if `loan` or `cohort` has a missing value, a loan has more than one cohort or more "
"than one row for a month on book, `month_on_book` has a value that is not a whole number, `bad` "
"has a value other than 0 and 1, or `weights` is not valid or differs between the rows of a loan."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空、不是一维的或长度不同，或者是索引不同的 Series。此外，如果 `loan` 或 `cohort` 含有缺失值，某笔贷款属于多个批次或在同一账龄有多行， "
"`month_on_book` 含有非整数的值， `bad` 含有 0 和 1 以外的值，或 `weights` 无效或在同一贷款的各行之间不一致，也会抛出此异常。"

msgid ":obj:`transition_matrix`"
msgstr ":obj:`transition_matrix`"

msgid "Movements between states from one month to another."
msgstr "从一个月到另一个月在各状态之间的迁移。"

msgid ":obj:`roll_rates`"
msgstr ":obj:`roll_rates`"

msgid "Share of each delinquency bucket that rolls to the next."
msgstr "每个逾期档位滚动到下一档位的比例。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel`"

msgid "Synthetic loan panel to try this on."
msgstr "可用于试用此函数的合成贷款面板。"

msgid ""
"Let :math:`L_c` be the loans of cohort :math:`c`, :math:`\\tau_i` the first month on book at "
"which loan :math:`i` is bad (infinite if it never is) and :math:`w_i` its weight, 1 without "
"`weights`. The entry for month on book :math:`k` is"
msgstr ""
"设 :math:`L_c` 为批次 :math:`c` 的贷款， :math:`\\tau_i` 为贷款 :math:`i` 首次为坏的账龄（从未变坏时为无穷大）， :math:`w_i` "
"为其权重（不传 `weights` 时为 1）。账龄 :math:`k` 处的取值为"

msgid ""
"V_{c,k} = \\frac{\\sum_{i \\in L_c} w_i \\, [\\tau_i \\le k]}\n"
"               {\\sum_{i \\in L_c} w_i}."
msgstr ""
"V_{c,k} = \\frac{\\sum_{i \\in L_c} w_i \\, [\\tau_i \\le k]}\n"
"               {\\sum_{i \\in L_c} w_i}."

msgid ""
"The denominator includes every loan of the cohort, also loans that left the panel early, for "
"example because they were repaid; such a loan counts as bad only if it was bad before it left. A "
"loan that is bad once stays counted as bad, even if it later cures."
msgstr "分母包括批次中的每一笔贷款，也包括提前离开面板的贷款（例如已经还清）；这类贷款只有在离开前变坏过才算作坏。贷款一旦变坏，即使之后回到正常，也一直算作坏。"

msgid ""
"A cohort is observed from the smallest to the largest month on book of its rows, and its entries "
"outside that range are NaN, not 0. Later months on book are missing because the cohort is too "
"young to show whether its loans will go bad, and earlier ones because the panel starts after the "
"cohort was originated. Loans that were bad only before the panel starts are not counted, so start"
" the panel at origination where possible. Comparing the cohorts at the same month on book "
"compares them at the same age, which separates a change in the quality of new lending from the "
"seasoning of the portfolio."
msgstr ""
"批次的观测范围从其各行中最小的账龄到最大的账龄，范围之外的取值为 NaN 而不是 "
"0。之后的账龄缺失，是因为该批次的账龄还太短，看不出其贷款是否会变坏；之前的账龄缺失，是因为面板在该批次发放之后才开始。只在面板开始之前变坏过的贷款不会被计入，因此应尽量让面板从放款时开始。在相同账龄上比较各批次，就是在相同的“年龄”上比较它们，从而把新增放款质量的变化与资产组合的账龄成熟效应区分开。"

msgid ""
"Two cases need care. If every loan of a cohort leaves the panel before it ends, for example "
"because all of them were repaid, the cohort's last entry is final, yet its later months on book "
"are NaN; to fill them, keep a row for each month end after a loan left, with a status that is not"
" bad, such as ``\"closed\"``. And a cohort that spans several origination months, such as a "
"quarter, mixes loans of different ages: at its largest months on book, its youngest loans count "
"in the denominator although they have not been observed that long, which biases those entries "
"down. Monthly cohorts avoid this."
msgstr ""
"有两种情况需要注意。如果某个批次的所有贷款都在面板结束前离开（例如全部已经还清），该批次的最后一个取值已是最终结果，但其之后的账龄仍为 "
"NaN；要补齐这些取值，可以在贷款离开后的每个月末保留一行，状态设为不算坏的值，例如 ``\"closed\"`` "
"。另外，跨越多个放款月的批次（例如按季度划分的批次）混合了不同账龄的贷款：在其最大的几个账龄上，最年轻的贷款虽然还没有被观测到这么久，却计入了分母，使这些取值偏低。按月划分批次可以避免这一问题。"

msgid ""
"Loan 1 cured after month on book 2 but stays counted as bad, and the 2024-02 cohort has not "
"reached month on book 3."
msgstr "贷款 1 在账龄 2 之后回到正常，但仍算作坏；2024-02 批次尚未达到账龄 3。"

msgid ""
"Each entity, such as a loan or an obligor, is observed in one state before and one state after, "
"for example its delinquency bucket at two consecutive month ends or its rating grade at two "
"annual reviews. Row :math:`i`, column :math:`j` counts the entities that moved from state "
":math:`i` to state :math:`j`. With `normalize`, each row holds the shares of the states after, "
"the migration matrix of a rating system."
msgstr ""
"每个对象（例如一笔贷款或一位债务人）先后各在一个状态上被观测，例如相邻两个月末的逾期档位，或两次年度复评时的评级。第 :math:`i` 行、第 :math:`j` 列统计从状态 "
":math:`i` 迁移到状态 :math:`j` 的对象数。设置 `normalize` 后，每一行给出之后各状态所占的比例，即评级体系的迁移矩阵。"

msgid "**before, after**"
msgstr "**before, after**"

msgid ""
"State of each entity at the first and at the second observation. If both are Series, they must "
"have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by position. Neither may contain missing "
"values: drop the entities that were not observed twice, or give the entities that left a state "
"such as ``\"closed\"``."
msgstr ""
"每个对象在第一次和第二次观测时的状态。如果二者都是 Series，索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。二者都不能含有缺失值：请删除没有被观测两次的对象，或给已离开的对象一个单独的状态，例如 "
"``\"closed\"`` 。"

msgid "**states**"
msgstr "**states**"

msgid ""
"All states in order, for delinquency buckets and rating grades from the best to the worst. States"
" without entities still get a row and a column. By default, the categories of categorical inputs,"
" which must then be the same for both, or else the sorted distinct values. Sorting puts labels "
"such as ``\"current\"`` after ``\"90+\"``, so pass `states` or ordered categoricals for "
"delinquency buckets."
msgstr ""
"按顺序排列的全部状态；对于逾期档位和评级，从最好到最差排列。没有对象的状态仍会占一行一列。默认取分类型输入的类别（此时两个输入的类别必须相同），否则取排序后的不同取值。排序会把 "
"``\"current\"`` 这样的标签排在 ``\"90+\"`` 之后，因此对于逾期档位，请传入 `states` 或使用有序分类变量。"

msgid ""
"If True, divide each row by its total, so that it holds the shares of the state's entities that "
"moved to each state. A row without entities is then NaN."
msgstr "如果为 True，每一行除以该行合计，使其给出该状态的对象迁移到各状态的比例。此时没有对象的行为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each entity, such as its balance at the first observation, matched like "
"`after`. The counts are then sums of weights."
msgstr "每个对象的非负权重，例如第一次观测时的余额，对应方式与 `after` 相同。此时计数为权重之和。"

msgid ""
"One row per state before and one column per state after, in the order of `states`. Without "
"`weights` and `normalize`, the entries are integer counts."
msgstr "之前的每个状态一行，之后的每个状态一列，按 `states` 的顺序排列。不传 `weights` 且不设置 `normalize` 时，取值为整数计数。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are empty, not one-dimensional, of different lengths or Series with different "
"indices, have a missing value or a value that is not one of `states`, or `weights` is not valid. "
"Also if `states` is not one-dimensional or has duplicates, or is not given while `before` and "
"`after` are categoricals with different categories."
msgstr ""
"如果输入为空、不是一维的、长度不同或是索引不同的 Series，含有缺失值或不属于 `states` 的值，或 `weights` 无效。此外，如果 `states` "
"不是一维的或有重复值，或者未给出 `states` 而 `before` 和 `after` 是类别不同的分类变量，也会抛出此异常。"

msgid "Share of each state that moved to the next worse state."
msgstr "每个状态中迁移到下一个更差状态的比例。"

msgid ":obj:`vintage_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`vintage_table`"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "With :math:`n_{ij}` entities moving from state :math:`i` to state :math:`j`, the normalized entry"
msgstr "设有 :math:`n_{ij}` 个对象从状态 :math:`i` 迁移到状态 :math:`j` ，则归一化后的取值"

msgid "p_{ij} = \\frac{n_{ij}}{\\sum_k n_{ik}}"
msgstr "p_{ij} = \\frac{n_{ij}}{\\sum_k n_{ik}}"

msgid ""
"estimates the probability of moving to :math:`j` from :math:`i`. If the movements follow a time-"
"homogeneous Markov chain, the :math:`h`-th power of the normalized matrix gives the probabilities"
" over :math:`h` periods."
msgstr "估计了从 :math:`i` 迁移到 :math:`j` 的概率。如果迁移服从时齐马尔可夫链，归一化矩阵的 :math:`h` 次幂给出 :math:`h` 期内的迁移概率。"

msgid ""
"Roll rates summarize the movements of delinquency between two month ends: the roll rate of "
"``30-59`` days past due is the share of the loans at 30 to 59 days that are at 60 to 89 days a "
"month later. The states must be ordered from the best to the worst, so that the next state is the"
" next worse one."
msgstr ""
"滚动率概括了两个月末之间逾期状态的变化：逾期 ``30-59`` 天的滚动率，是逾期 30 到 59 天的贷款中一个月后逾期 60 到 89 "
"天的比例。状态必须从最好到最差排列，这样下一个状态就是更差的一档。"

msgid ""
"State of each entity at the first and at the second observation, as in `transition_matrix`. "
"Neither may contain missing values."
msgstr "每个对象在第一次和第二次观测时的状态，与 `transition_matrix` 相同。二者都不能含有缺失值。"

msgid ""
"All states from the best to the worst. Required unless `before` and `after` are ordered "
"categoricals with the same categories, whose order is then used. A sorted order would be wrong "
"for most labels, for example ``\"current\"`` would come after ``\"90+\"``."
msgstr ""
"从最好到最差排列的全部状态。除非 `before` 和 `after` 是类别相同的有序分类变量（此时使用其类别顺序），否则必须传入。对大多数标签来说，排序得到的顺序是错误的，例如 "
"``\"current\"`` 会排在 ``\"90+\"`` 之后。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each entity, such as its balance at the first observation, matched like "
"`after`. The rates are then shares of weight, the balance roll rates."
msgstr "每个对象的非负权重，例如第一次观测时的余额，对应方式与 `after` 相同。此时滚动率是权重的比例，即余额滚动率。"

msgid ""
"Roll rate of every state except the worst, which has no next state, indexed by the state. A state"
" without entities has a NaN rate."
msgstr "除最差状态（没有下一个状态）外每个状态的滚动率，以状态为索引。没有对象的状态，其滚动率为 NaN。"

msgid ""
"In the same cases as `transition_matrix`, and if `states` is not given while `before` and `after`"
" are not ordered categoricals."
msgstr "与 `transition_matrix` 在相同的情况下抛出；此外，如果未给出 `states` 而 `before` 和 `after` 不是有序分类变量，也会抛出。"

msgid "The movements between all pairs of states."
msgstr "所有状态两两之间的迁移。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"With :math:`n_{ij}` entities moving from state :math:`i` to state :math:`j`, the roll rate of "
"state :math:`i` is"
msgstr "设有 :math:`n_{ij}` 个对象从状态 :math:`i` 迁移到状态 :math:`j` ，则状态 :math:`i` 的滚动率为"

msgid "r_i = \\frac{n_{i,i+1}}{\\sum_k n_{ik}}."
msgstr "r_i = \\frac{n_{i,i+1}}{\\sum_k n_{ik}}."

msgid ""
"Entities that improved, stayed or moved more than one state worse count in the denominator only. "
"A loan can fall at most one delinquency bucket further behind from one month end to the next, so "
"the product of the roll rates estimates the share of current loans that reach the worst bucket "
"after one month per roll, if the movements follow a Markov chain."
msgstr "状态改善、保持不变或恶化超过一档的对象只计入分母。从一个月末到下一个月末，贷款最多再恶化一个逾期档位，因此如果迁移服从马尔可夫链，各滚动率的乘积估计了正常贷款在经过与滚动次数相同的月数后处于最差档位的比例。"

msgid "Weight of evidence and information value"
msgstr "证据权重与信息值"

msgid ""
"Measure how each group of a variable separates a binary target, and encode groups with the "
"result. :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` gives the WOE and IV of each group and "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` encodes new data with them; :func:`~kivi.woe.woe` and "
":func:`~kivi.woe.iv` compute the same measures from aggregated counts."
msgstr ""
"衡量变量的每个分组区分二元目标变量的能力，并用结果对分组编码。 :func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 给出每组的 WOE 和 IV， "
":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_transform` 用它们对新数据编码； :func:`~kivi.woe.woe` 和 :func:`~kivi.woe.iv` "
"根据汇总计数计算同样的指标。"

msgid "See :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` for the definitions, examples and how to read the result."
msgstr "定义、示例以及如何解读结果，见 :doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 。"

msgid ":py:obj:`woe_table <kivi.woe.woe_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, smoothing\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`woe_table <kivi.woe.woe_table>`\\ \\(groups\\, target\\, \\*\\[\\, smoothing\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute weight of evidence and information value for observed groups."
msgstr "按观察到的分组计算证据权重（WOE）和信息值（IV）。"

msgid ":py:obj:`woe_transform <kivi.woe.woe_transform>`\\ \\(groups\\, table\\, \\*\\[\\, unseen\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`woe_transform <kivi.woe.woe_transform>`\\ \\(groups\\, table\\, \\*\\[\\, unseen\\]\\)"

msgid "Replace each group with its weight of evidence."
msgstr "将每个分组替换为其证据权重（WOE）。"

msgid ":py:obj:`woe <kivi.woe.woe>`\\ \\(event\\_counts\\, non\\_event\\_counts\\, \\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`woe <kivi.woe.woe>`\\ \\(event\\_counts\\, non\\_event\\_counts\\, \\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the weight of evidence of each group from its counts."
msgstr "根据每组的计数计算其证据权重（WOE）。"

msgid ":py:obj:`iv <kivi.woe.iv>`\\ \\(event\\_counts\\, non\\_event\\_counts\\, \\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"
msgstr ":py:obj:`iv <kivi.woe.iv>`\\ \\(event\\_counts\\, non\\_event\\_counts\\, \\*\\[\\, ...\\]\\)"

msgid "Compute the information value from counts per group."
msgstr "根据每组的计数计算信息值（IV）。"

msgid ""
"Each group's share of events is compared with its share of non-events. Sum the ``iv`` column for "
"the information value of the variable."
msgstr "比较每组在全部事件中的占比与在全部非事件中的占比。将 ``iv`` 列求和即得到该变量的信息值。"

msgid "Pre-binned values or category labels. Missing values form a group."
msgstr "已分箱的数值或类别标签。缺失值独立成组。"

msgid ""
"Binary labels, with 1 indicating the event. If `groups` and `target` are both pandas Series, they"
" must have identical indices; otherwise they are matched by position."
msgstr "二分类标签，1 表示事件。如果 `groups` 和 `target` 都是 pandas Series，二者的索引必须完全相同；否则按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"Non-negative weight of each observation, for example the inverse of its sampling rate, matched "
"like `target`. The counts are then sums of weights, and groups whose weights sum to zero are left"
" out, so `woe_transform` treats them as unseen. `smoothing` is then in units of weight: scale the"
" weights to sum to the number of observations, or scale `smoothing` with them."
msgstr ""
"每个观测的非负权重，例如其抽样比例的倒数，对应方式与 `target` 相同。此时计数为权重之和，权重之和为零的组会被排除，因此 `woe_transform` 会把它们视为未见过的分组。此时 "
"`smoothing` 以权重为单位：请把权重缩放到总和等于观测数，或按相同比例缩放 `smoothing` 。"

msgid ""
"One row per group with the columns ``non_event``, ``event`` and ``total`` (counts), "
"``non_event_share`` and ``event_share`` (smoothed shares within each class), ``total_share`` "
"(share of all observations), ``event_rate``, ``woe`` and ``iv``. Sum the iv column for the "
"variable's information value."
msgstr ""
"每组一行，包含以下列： ``non_event`` 、 ``event`` 和 ``total`` （计数）， ``non_event_share`` 和 ``event_share`` "
"（各自类别内平滑后的占比）， ``total_share`` （占全部观测的比例）， ``event_rate`` 、 ``woe`` 和 ``iv`` 。将 iv 列求和即得到该变量的信息值。"

msgid ""
"If the inputs are not one-dimensional, their indices or lengths do not match, `target` does not "
"contain both 0 and 1 or has missing or other labels, or `smoothing` is not finite and positive. "
"Also if `weights` is not numeric, does not give each observation one finite, non-negative weight,"
" has an index other than that of `groups`, or leaves a class with a zero total."
msgstr ""
"如果输入不是一维、索引或长度不一致、 `target` 没有同时包含 0 和 1 或含有缺失值及其他标签，或者 `smoothing` 不是有限正数。此外，如果 `weights` "
"不是数值、没有为每个观测给出一个有限非负的权重、索引与 `groups` 不同，或使事件或非事件的权重总和为零。"

msgid "Replace each group with its WOE."
msgstr "将每个分组替换为其 WOE。"

msgid ":obj:`woe`, :obj:`iv`"
msgstr ":obj:`woe`, :obj:`iv`"

msgid "The same measures from counts per group."
msgstr "根据每组计数计算同样的指标。"

msgid "Fit edges for numeric variables."
msgstr "为数值变量拟合分箱边界。"

msgid "Compare the distribution of two samples."
msgstr "比较两个样本的分布。"

msgid ""
"For group :math:`i`, let :math:`p_i` and :math:`q_i` be its shares of all events and of all non-"
"events. Then"
msgstr "对第 :math:`i` 组，令 :math:`p_i` 和 :math:`q_i` 分别为其在全部事件和全部非事件中的占比。则"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{WOE}_i = \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IV}_i = (p_i - q_i)\\,\\mathrm{WOE}_i, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IV} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{IV}_i."
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{WOE}_i = \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IV}_i = (p_i - q_i)\\,\\mathrm{WOE}_i, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IV} = \\sum_i \\mathrm{IV}_i."

msgid ""
"Each zero count is replaced with `smoothing` before the shares are normalized, so every WOE is "
"finite. The count columns, ``total_share`` and ``event_rate`` always use the observed counts."
msgstr ""
"在归一化占比之前，每个零计数都会被替换为 `smoothing`，因此每个 WOE 都是有限值。计数列、 ``total_share`` 和 ``event_rate`` "
"始终使用实际观测到的计数。"

msgid ""
"Categorical groups, such as the result of `kivi.binning.cut` or ``pandas.cut``, follow the order "
"of their categories with missing values last. Other groups follow the order in which they first "
"appear. Categories that are never observed are omitted."
msgstr "分类型的分组（例如 `kivi.binning.cut` 或 ``pandas.cut`` 的结果）按类别顺序排列，缺失值排在最后。其他分组按首次出现的次序排列。从未出现的类别不会列出。"

msgid "[R86ef760ac44f-1]_"
msgstr "[R86ef760ac44f-1]_"

msgid ""
"The WOE values come from a table fitted on the development sample, so a scorecard model sees the "
"same encoding in development, validation and production."
msgstr "WOE 取自在开发样本上拟合的表，因此评分卡模型在开发、验证和生产环境中看到的是同一套编码。"

msgid ""
"One-dimensional group labels formed in the same way as those passed to `woe_table`, for example "
"with the same edges and ``pandas.cut``."
msgstr "一维分组标签，划分方式须与传给 `woe_table` 的分组相同，例如使用同一组边界和 ``pandas.cut`` 。"

msgid "pandas.DataFrame or pandas.Series"
msgstr "pandas.DataFrame 或 pandas.Series"

msgid ""
"The result of `woe_table`, or a Series of WOE values indexed by group. A missing label in the "
"index gives the WOE of missing values."
msgstr "`woe_table` 的结果，或以分组为索引的 WOE 序列。索引中的缺失标签对应缺失值的 WOE。"

msgid "float or \"raise\", default \"raise\""
msgstr "float 或 \"raise\"，默认 \"raise\""

msgid ""
"WOE for groups that are not in `table`, such as a new category, an interval without development "
"observations, or missing values when `table` has no missing group. By default such groups raise "
"an error."
msgstr "不在 `table` 中的分组所用的 WOE，例如新类别、开发样本中没有观测值的区间，或 `table` 没有缺失组时的缺失值。默认情况下，这类分组会引发错误。"

msgid ""
"Float WOE values in the order of `groups`. A Series input gives a Series with the same index and "
"name."
msgstr "按 `groups` 顺序排列的浮点 WOE 值。输入为 Series 时返回 Series，索引和名称保持不变。"

msgid ""
"If `groups` is not one-dimensional, `table` has no ``woe`` column or repeats a group, `unseen` is"
" neither ``\"raise\"`` nor a number, or `unseen` is ``\"raise\"`` and some groups are not in "
"`table`."
msgstr ""
"如果 `groups` 不是一维、 `table` 没有 ``woe`` 列或有重复的分组、 `unseen` 既不是 ``\"raise\"`` 也不是数值，或者 `unseen` 为 "
"``\"raise\"`` 而部分分组不在 `table` 中。"

msgid ":obj:`woe_table`"
msgstr ":obj:`woe_table`"

msgid "Fit the edges used to form numeric groups."
msgstr "拟合用于划分数值分组的边界。"

msgid ""
"Labels are matched by equality, so an interval from ``pandas.cut`` matches the interval with the "
"same edges in `table`. Use the edges fitted on the development sample for every sample that is "
"transformed."
msgstr "标签按相等关系匹配，因此 ``pandas.cut`` 得到的区间会与 `table` 中边界相同的区间对应。对每个要转换的样本，都请使用在开发样本上拟合的边界。"

msgid ""
"Use this when the counts are already aggregated, for example from a database query or a report, "
"instead of one label per observation."
msgstr "适用于计数已经汇总的情况，例如来自数据库查询或报表，而不是每个观测一个标签。"

msgid "**event_counts, non_event_counts**"
msgstr "**event_counts, non_event_counts**"

msgid ""
"One-dimensional, non-negative counts of events and non-events in each group, in the same group "
"order. Weighted counts need not be integers."
msgstr "每组事件和非事件的一维非负计数，两者的分组顺序须一致。加权计数不必是整数。"

msgid "The WOE of each group."
msgstr "每组的 WOE。"

msgid ":obj:`iv`"
msgstr ":obj:`iv`"

msgid "The information value of the same counts."
msgstr "同一组计数的信息值。"

msgid "Counts, shares, WOE and IV from group labels and a target."
msgstr "根据分组标签和目标计算计数、占比、WOE 和 IV。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"With :math:`p_i` and :math:`q_i` the smoothed shares of group :math:`i` among all events and all "
"non-events, :math:`\\mathrm{WOE}_i = \\ln(p_i / q_i)`, as in the ``woe`` column of `woe_table`."
msgstr ""
"记 :math:`p_i` 和 :math:`q_i` 为第 :math:`i` 组在全部事件和全部非事件中平滑后的占比，则 :math:`\\mathrm{WOE}_i = \\ln(p_i "
"/ q_i)` ，与 `woe_table` 的 ``woe`` 列一致。"

msgid ""
"The information value summarizes how well the groups separate events from non-events, from counts"
" that are already aggregated."
msgstr "信息值概括了各组区分事件与非事件的能力，这里直接根据已汇总的计数计算。"

msgid "The information value of the variable."
msgstr "该变量的信息值。"

msgid ":obj:`woe`"
msgstr ":obj:`woe`"

msgid "The weight of evidence of each group."
msgstr "每组的证据权重。"

msgid "The IV contribution of each group from labels and a target."
msgstr "根据标签和目标计算每组的 IV 贡献。"

msgid ":obj:`kivi.stability.psi`"
msgstr ":obj:`kivi.stability.psi`"

msgid "The same divergence between two samples."
msgstr "两个样本之间的同一种散度。"

#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\mathrm{IV} = \\sum_i (p_i - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i},"
msgstr "\\mathrm{IV} = \\sum_i (p_i - q_i) \\ln \\frac{p_i}{q_i},"

msgid "which equals the sum of the ``iv`` column of `woe_table` for the same groups."
msgstr "它等于相同分组下 `woe_table` 中 ``iv`` 列之和。"

msgid "Writing documentation"
msgstr "编写文档"

msgid ""
"The English and the simplified Chinese editions are built from the same pages and docstrings. "
"This page describes how they are organized and written. :doc:`index` covers the checks that every"
" pull request runs."
msgstr "英文版和简体中文版由同一套页面和 docstring 构建。本页说明文档的组织方式和写法；每个拉取请求都要运行的检查见 :doc:`index` 。"

msgid "Kinds of pages"
msgstr "页面类型"

msgid ""
"Apart from the home page and the index page of each section, every page is one of five kinds, and"
" its kind decides what it contains."
msgstr "除首页和各部分的目录页外，每个页面都属于下列五种类型之一，类型决定了页面的内容。"

msgid "Kind"
msgstr "类型"

msgid "Pages"
msgstr "页面"

msgid "Contents"
msgstr "内容"

msgid "Tutorial"
msgstr "教程"

msgid "The pages of the getting started section, and :doc:`/user_guide/risk_workflow`"
msgstr "快速开始部分的各个页面，以及 :doc:`/user_guide/risk_workflow`"

msgid ""
"The installation, and worked examples on the bundled data from start to finish. They link to the "
"topic guides for the details instead of repeating them."
msgstr "安装说明，以及用随包数据从头到尾完成的示例。细节链接到对应的主题指南，不在教程里重复。"

msgid "Topic guide"
msgstr "主题指南"

msgid "The other pages of the user guide"
msgstr "用户指南的其余页面"

msgid ""
"One step of a risk model: what it measures, an example and how to read the result. "
":doc:`/user_guide/datasets` describes the example data in the same way."
msgstr "风控模型中的一个步骤：它衡量什么、一个示例，以及如何解读结果。 :doc:`/user_guide/datasets` 以同样的方式介绍示例数据。"

msgid "Reference"
msgstr "参考"

msgid "The pages of the API reference"
msgstr "API 参考的各个页面"

msgid ""
":doc:`/api/conventions`, the rules that every function follows; :doc:`/api/glossary`, the terms "
"of the guides; and one page per public module, generated from its docstrings."
msgstr ""
":doc:`/api/conventions` ，即所有函数共同遵守的规则； :doc:`/api/glossary` ，即各篇指南所用的术语；以及每个公共模块一页，由模块的 docstring"
" 生成。"

msgid "Release notes"
msgstr "版本说明"

msgid ":doc:`/release/index` and :doc:`/release/migration`"
msgstr ":doc:`/release/index` 和 :doc:`/release/migration`"

msgid ""
"What changed in each version, and how to move code from the 0.2.x classes to their replacements. "
"The notes of a released version are not edited. The migration guide is revised whenever a release"
" changes what it describes."
msgstr "每个版本的变化，以及如何把使用 0.2.x 类的代码迁移到替代接口。已发布版本的说明不再修改；当某个版本改变了迁移指南所描述的内容时，迁移指南随之修订。"

msgid "Contributor guide"
msgstr "贡献者指南"

msgid "The pages of this section"
msgstr "本节的各个页面"

msgid ""
"How to work on kivi. :doc:`legacy_review` records the review of the 0.2.x code that preceded the "
"rewrite."
msgstr "如何参与 kivi 的开发。 :doc:`legacy_review` 记录重写之前对 0.2.x 代码的评审。"

msgid "Where pages live"
msgstr "页面位置"

msgid ""
"A public module ``kivi.<module>`` has an API page ``docs/api/<module>.rst`` and usually a topic "
"guide ``docs/user_guide/<topic>.rst``. The toctrees of the API reference and of the user guide "
"list their pages in the order of a project and end with a glob, so a new page appears at the end "
"without editing them. The integration moves it to its place, as Entry points below describes."
msgstr ""
"公共模块 ``kivi.<module>`` 有一个 API 页面 ``docs/api/<module>.rst`` ，通常还有一个主题指南 "
"``docs/user_guide/<topic>.rst`` 。API 参考和用户指南的 toctree "
"按项目顺序列出各页，并以通配符结尾，所以新页面无需修改它们就会出现在末尾。集成时再把它移到应有的位置，详见下文“入口页面”。"

msgid ""
"The conventions and the glossary are ``docs/api/conventions.rst`` and ``docs/api/glossary.rst``. "
"They come first in the API reference, and the index of the user guide links to both."
msgstr "约定和术语表分别是 ``docs/api/conventions.rst`` 和 ``docs/api/glossary.rst`` 。它们排在 API 参考的最前面，用户指南目录页链接到这两页。"

msgid ""
"Page names are part of the URLs, and the language switch links each page to the page of the same "
"name in the other edition. Change the title of a page rather than renaming or removing it."
msgstr "页面名是 URL 的一部分，语言切换也会把每个页面链接到另一种语言中同名的页面。需要调整时改页面标题，不要重命名或删除页面。"

msgid ""
"The API page of a module and its topic guide have the same title. Its cards and its rows in the "
"README use that title or a short form of it, such as WOE and IV."
msgstr "同一个模块的 API 页面和主题指南使用同一个标题。它的卡片和 README 中的行使用这个标题或其简称，例如 WOE 与 IV。"

msgid "Topic guides"
msgstr "主题指南"

msgid ""
"A topic guide follows the order of an analysis, so that readers can stop as soon as they have "
"what they need. Its sections come in the order of the table below, with the titles that the table"
" gives in inline code:"
msgstr "主题指南按分析的顺序组织，读者找到所需内容即可停下。各节按下表的顺序排列，表中以行内代码给出的是各节的固定标题："

msgid "Section"
msgstr "节"

msgid "Opening, without a heading"
msgstr "开篇，不加标题"

msgid ""
"The question that the step answers and where it sits in a risk model, with links to the guides of"
" the steps before and after it in the order of the user guide. The public functions that the page"
" covers, each linked to its API entry. The opening has no examples."
msgstr "这一步回答什么问题，在风控模型中处于什么位置，并按用户指南的顺序链接到前后步骤的指南。本页涉及的公共函数，每个都链接到其 API 条目。开篇不含示例。"

msgid "``Definition``"
msgstr "``Definition`` （定义）"

msgid ""
"The measure and its formula in a math block, before any example. Title it ``Definitions`` when it"
" defines several measures, and leave it out when each tool of the page is defined in its own "
"section."
msgstr "指标及其公式（放在 math 块中），位于所有示例之前。定义多个指标时标题用 ``Definitions`` ；如果页面上的每个工具都在各自的小节中定义，则省略本节。"

msgid "``A worked example``"
msgstr "``A worked example`` （计算示例）"

msgid "A few values that readers can check by hand, right after the definition."
msgstr "读者可以手工验算的几个数值，紧接在定义之后。"

msgid "Body sections"
msgstr "正文各节"

msgid ""
"One section for each task, tool or question of the step, in the order of a project, with an "
"example on the bundled data and how to read its result. Title a body section with a noun phrase, "
"such as ``Gains table``, or a gerund phrase, such as ``Choosing a cut-off``; imperative titles "
"are for the steps of a tutorial. A body section may have subsections."
msgstr ""
"这一步的每个任务、工具或问题各占一节，按项目的顺序排列，并给出基于内置数据的示例以及如何解读其结果。正文小节的标题用名词短语，例如 ``Gains table`` ，或动名词短语，例如 "
"``Choosing a cut-off`` ；祈使句式的标题留给教程的步骤。正文小节可以再分子节。"

msgid "``Reading the result``"
msgstr "``Reading the result`` （解读结果）"

msgid ""
"A table of the columns of the page's main result, the direction of the measure, its usual "
"thresholds and what to check next. It follows the body sections whose examples print that result "
"and comes before the body sections about other tools. On a page whose tools each return their own"
" table, each body section describes its table instead."
msgstr "页面主要结果各列的表格、指标的方向、常用阈值以及下一步要检查什么。它位于打印该结果的正文小节之后、介绍其他工具的正文小节之前。如果页面上的每个工具各自返回一张表，则由各正文小节分别说明自己的表。"

msgid "``Special values``"
msgstr "``Special values`` （特殊值）"

msgid ""
"How codes such as ``-1`` for \"not applicable\" are passed in ``special``, and which group they "
"end up in."
msgstr "如何把表示“不适用”的 ``-1`` 等编码传入 ``special`` ，以及它们最终落入哪个分组。"

msgid "``Missing values``"
msgstr "``Missing values`` （缺失值）"

msgid "How missing values are counted, grouped or rejected."
msgstr "缺失值如何计数、分组或被拒绝。"

msgid "``Sample weights``"
msgstr "``Sample weights`` （样本权重）"

msgid ""
"What ``weights`` changes and what it leaves unchanged, and where weighted results differ from "
"repeated rows."
msgstr "``weights`` 改变什么、不改变什么，以及加权结果在哪些地方与重复行的结果不同。"

msgid "``Limits``"
msgstr "``Limits`` （局限）"

msgid "What the method cannot tell, and what kivi leaves out."
msgstr "方法无法说明什么，以及 kivi 没有实现什么。"

msgid "``Errors and warnings``"
msgstr "``Errors and warnings`` （错误与警告）"

msgid "The errors and warnings that readers are likely to meet, and how to resolve them."
msgstr "读者可能遇到的错误和警告，以及解决方法。"

msgid ""
"Leave out the sections that do not apply, but keep the order and the titles of the others, so "
"that the guides read alike. A variant that one or two sentences explain can stay in the body "
"section that it belongs to, and an error that belongs to one task can be shown where that task "
"is; a section of its own is for a variant or error that needs an example."
msgstr "不适用的小节可以省略，但其余小节要保持顺序和标题不变，让各篇指南读起来一致。一两句话就能说明的变体可以留在它所属的正文小节中，只属于某个任务的错误也可以在该任务处展示；需要示例的变体或错误才单独成节。"

msgid ""
"Section anchors are part of the URLs as well, and the READMEs link to some of them. Keep the "
"title of a section that a README links to, and keep a label when its section moves."
msgstr "小节锚点也是 URL 的一部分，README 会链接其中一些锚点。README 链接到的小节不要改标题；小节移动时要保留它的标签。"

msgid ""
"Examples are doctests, and the ``build`` check runs them. Their output is real: when a change "
"alters a printed table, run the code again and paste the new output instead of editing the "
"numbers."
msgstr "示例都是 doctest，由 ``build`` 检查运行。输出必须真实：改动影响了打印出的表格时，重新运行代码并粘贴新的输出，不要手工修改数字。"

msgid ""
"Examples use the data described in :doc:`/user_guide/datasets`, or a few values that readers can "
"check by hand. Random data comes from a generator with a fixed seed."
msgstr "示例使用 :doc:`/user_guide/datasets` 中介绍的数据，或者少量读者能手工验算的数值。随机数据由固定种子的生成器产生。"

msgid "Import each function from its module, as in ``from kivi.woe import woe_table``."
msgstr "每个函数都从其所在模块导入，例如 ``from kivi.woe import woe_table`` 。"

msgid ""
"Examples must not warn: a warning raised by a doctest or by a chart recipe in docs/_plotting.py "
"fails the build. When an example is about a warning, catch it with "
"``warnings.catch_warnings(record=True)`` and print the message."
msgstr ""
"示例不能产生警告：doctest 或 docs/_plotting.py 中的图表函数一旦发出警告，构建就会失败。如果示例要演示某个警告，请用 "
"``warnings.catch_warnings(record=True)`` 捕获它并打印警告信息。"

msgid ""
"All the examples of a page share one namespace, so a section can use what an earlier section "
"defined. When sections move, check that every name is still defined before it is used."
msgstr "同一页面的所有示例共享一个命名空间，因此后面的小节可以使用前面小节定义的名称。移动小节时，请检查每个名称在使用之前仍有定义。"

msgid "Charts"
msgstr "图表"

msgid ""
"Charts are drawn when the documentation is built. A ``plot`` directive calls a ``figure_*`` "
"function in ``docs/_plotting.py``, which recomputes the example shown just above the chart, so "
"change the two together. Text inside a chart is limited to kivi's column and parameter names and "
"to data values, so that one image serves both editions. The caption and the alternative text are "
"translated."
msgstr ""
"图表在构建文档时绘制。 ``plot`` 指令调用 ``docs/_plotting.py`` 中的 ``figure_*`` "
"函数，该函数重新计算图表上方示例的结果，所以两者要一起修改。图中的文字只使用 kivi 的列名、参数名和数据值，这样一张图可以同时用于两种语言。图注和替代文本会被翻译。"

msgid ""
"A pull request that adds a module describes the charts for its page in its description. They are "
"added to ``docs/_plotting.py`` when the page is integrated, together with the entry points."
msgstr "新增模块的拉取请求在描述中说明其页面需要的图表。这些图表在集成该页面时，与入口页面一起加入 ``docs/_plotting.py`` 。"

msgid "Names and links"
msgstr "名称与链接"

msgid "Write argument and column names as inline code, such as ``special`` or ``event_rate``."
msgstr "参数名和列名写成行内代码，例如 ``special`` 或 ``event_rate`` 。"

msgid ""
"In the topic guides and the tutorials, link the first mention of a kivi function, class or module"
" in each section to its API entry. Use the ``:func:``, ``:class:``, ``:exc:``, ``:meth:`` and "
"``:mod:`` roles with the full name and a leading tilde, such as ``:func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table```, "
"so that only the name is shown. Keep the module in the text where it tells two functions apart, "
"as in ``:func:`kivi.binning.cut``` next to ``pandas.cut``. Later mentions in the same section "
"stay inline code."
msgstr ""
"在主题指南和教程中，kivi 的函数、类或模块在每一节第一次出现时链接到其 API 条目。使用 ``:func:`` 、 ``:class:`` 、 ``:exc:`` 、 ``:meth:``"
" 和 ``:mod:`` 角色及完整名称，并在前面加波浪号，例如 ``:func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table``` ，这样只显示名称。需要用模块区分两个函数时保留模块名，例如与 "
"``pandas.cut`` 并列时写 ``:func:`kivi.binning.cut``` 。同一节中后续出现的名称仍写成行内代码。"

msgid ""
"``woe``, ``iv``, ``psi``, ``ks`` and ``gini`` are the names of functions and of columns. Link "
"them only where they mean the function."
msgstr "``woe`` 、 ``iv`` 、 ``psi`` 、 ``ks`` 和 ``gini`` 既是函数名，也是列名。只有表示函数时才加链接。"

msgid "Names inside examples are code and are not linked."
msgstr "示例中的名称是代码，不加链接。"

msgid ""
"Link to another page with the ``:doc:`` role and to a section of another page with the ``:ref:`` "
"role. Give a section a label only when a link points to it."
msgstr "链接到其他页面用 ``:doc:`` 角色，链接到其他页面的某个小节用 ``:ref:`` 角色。只有当某个链接指向一个小节时，才给它加标签。"

msgid ""
":doc:`/api` lists the conventions, the glossary and then the module pages in the order of the "
"user guide, and ends with a glob for the pages that are not integrated yet. ``api/datasets`` "
"comes last through the glob, so that the glob always matches a page."
msgstr ":doc:`/api` 先列出约定和术语表，再按用户指南的顺序列出各模块页面，最后以通配符收录尚未集成的页面。 ``api/datasets`` 通过通配符排在最后，从而保证通配符总能匹配到页面。"

msgid ""
"A module page starts with its title, a ``module`` directive, which gives ``:mod:`` links their "
"target, and an introduction: one or two sentences on what the module is for, with links to its "
"main functions, and a sentence that links to its topic guide. The entries follow. For example:"
msgstr ""
"模块页面依次包括：标题、 ``module`` 指令（为 ``:mod:`` "
"链接提供目标）以及简介。简介用一两句话说明模块的用途并链接其主要函数，再用一句话链接到对应的主题指南。之后是各条目。例如："

msgid ""
"The API page of a module documents every name in the module's ``__all__``: first in an "
"``autosummary`` table, then each with its own ``autofunction``, ``autoclass``, ``autoexception`` "
"or ``automethod`` entry, in the same order. ``python docs/build.py`` stops when a name has no "
"such entry."
msgstr ""
"模块的 API 页面要记录模块 ``__all__`` 中的每个名称：先列在 ``autosummary`` 表中，再按同样的顺序各自给出 ``autofunction`` 、 "
"``autoclass`` 、 ``autoexception`` 或 ``automethod`` 条目。某个名称没有这样的条目时， ``python docs/build.py`` 会停止。"

msgid ""
"Docstrings follow the numpydoc conventions and are validated with every check enabled, so a "
"missing section, such as See Also or Examples, fails the build. Their paragraphs are translated "
"like those of the pages."
msgstr "docstring 遵循 numpydoc 约定，并启用全部校验项，因此缺少某个小节（例如 See Also 或 Examples）会导致构建失败。docstring 的段落和页面一样需要翻译。"

msgid ""
":doc:`/api/conventions` holds the rules that every module follows, such as the order of the "
"arguments and the meaning of ``weights``. A guide or a docstring states a rule of its own module "
"and links to the conventions for the shared ones. :doc:`/api/glossary` defines each term once and"
" links to the guide that uses it."
msgstr ""
":doc:`/api/conventions` 收录所有模块共同遵守的规则，例如参数顺序和 ``weights`` 的含义。指南或 docstring "
"只说明本模块自己的规则，共同规则则链接到约定页面。 :doc:`/api/glossary` 对每个术语只定义一次，并链接到使用它的指南。"

msgid "Translations"
msgstr "翻译"

msgid ""
"The Chinese edition is generated from ``docs/locale/zh_CN/LC_MESSAGES/kivi.po``. Every paragraph "
"of the English pages and of the public docstrings is one entry in that file. ``python "
"docs/build.py`` stops when an entry is missing, fuzzy or no longer used."
msgstr ""
"中文版由 ``docs/locale/zh_CN/LC_MESSAGES/kivi.po`` 生成。英文页面和公共 docstring "
"中的每个段落都对应该文件中的一个条目。如果有条目缺失、标记为 fuzzy 或已不再使用，``python docs/build.py`` 会停止构建。"

msgid "After changing English text:"
msgstr "修改英文内容后："

msgid ""
"Run ``python docs/build.py --update-po``. New strings are added with an empty translation, and "
"changed strings keep their old translation marked as fuzzy."
msgstr "运行 ``python docs/build.py --update-po``。新字符串以空译文加入，已修改的字符串保留旧译文并标记为 fuzzy。"

msgid "Translate the empty entries, review the fuzzy ones and delete their ``#, fuzzy`` line."
msgstr "翻译空条目，复核 fuzzy 条目并删除其 ``#, fuzzy`` 行。"

msgid "Run ``python docs/build.py`` again."
msgstr "再次运行 ``python docs/build.py``。"

msgid ""
"In a translation, put a space or Chinese punctuation on both sides of inline markup such as "
"inline code and links, or the markup is not recognized. Translate each term as the catalog "
"already translates it, so that the edition keeps one vocabulary."
msgstr "翻译时，行内代码、链接等行内标记的两侧要留空格或使用中文标点，否则标记无法识别。每个术语沿用翻译目录中已有的译法，让中文版保持统一的用词。"

msgid ""
"A change that only replaces markup, such as inline code by a link, leaves the translations valid."
" Apply it to the source strings and to their translations in ``kivi.po`` before step 1, so that "
"the entries do not turn fuzzy."
msgstr "只替换标记的修改（例如把行内代码换成链接）不会使译文失效。请在第 1 步之前，把同样的修改应用到 ``kivi.po`` 的源字符串及其译文上，这样条目就不会变为 fuzzy。"

msgid "Entry points"
msgstr "入口页面"

msgid ""
"Some pages describe the library as a whole: ``README.md`` and ``README.zh-CN.md``, the home page,"
" the index of the user guide and :doc:`/user_guide/risk_workflow`. A pull request that adds a "
"module leaves them alone. They are updated together after a group of such pull requests has "
"merged, and that update rewrites them for the library as it now is instead of only appending to "
"them:"
msgstr ""
"有些页面描述整个库： ``README.md`` 和 ``README.zh-CN.md`` 、首页、用户指南目录页以及 :doc:`/user_guide/risk_workflow` "
"。新增模块的拉取请求不修改它们。它们在一批这样的拉取请求合并之后统一更新，而且这次更新要按库的现状重写，而不只是追加内容："

msgid "the title, the introduction and the steps on the home page;"
msgstr "首页的标题、简介和步骤；"

msgid "the cards on the home page and on the index of the user guide, and the order of the user guide;"
msgstr "首页和用户指南目录页上的卡片，以及用户指南的页面顺序；"

msgid "the order of the API reference;"
msgstr "API 参考的页面顺序；"

msgid "the links to the previous and the next step in the openings of the guides next to a new one;"
msgstr "新页面前后相邻的指南开篇中指向上一步和下一步的链接；"

msgid "the terms of :doc:`/api/glossary` and the rules of :doc:`/api/conventions` that a new module adds;"
msgstr "新模块需要加入 :doc:`/api/glossary` 的术语和 :doc:`/api/conventions` 的规则；"

msgid "the tables and the roadmap of both READMEs;"
msgstr "两份 README 中的表格和路线图；"

msgid "any sentence in :doc:`/release/migration` about functionality that is not ported yet."
msgstr ":doc:`/release/migration` 中关于尚未迁移功能的所有表述。"

msgid ""
"A pull request that adds a module lists in its description the glossary terms and the conventions"
" that it needs, as it does for its charts."
msgstr "新增模块的拉取请求要在描述中列出它所需的术语和约定，就像列出它的图表一样。"

msgid ""
"``python docs/build.py`` lists every public function that the API tables of the READMEs leave "
"out, and every user guide page without a card on the index of the user guide or a link in the "
"READMEs. ``python docs/build.py --release`` refuses to run until the list is empty."
msgstr ""
"``python docs/build.py`` 会列出 README 的 API 表格中遗漏的每个公共函数，以及每个在用户指南目录页上没有卡片、或在 README "
"中没有链接的用户指南页面。在这个列表清空之前， ``python docs/build.py --release`` 拒绝运行。"

msgid "Publishing the documentation"
msgstr "发布文档"

msgid ""
"The ``Documentation`` workflow on GitHub Actions runs the tests and builds both editions for "
"every pull request. On the master branch it also publishes docs/_build/html to the gh-pages "
"branch, which serves https://gchensy.github.io/kivi/."
msgstr ""
"GitHub Actions 上的 ``Documentation`` 工作流会对每个拉取请求运行测试并构建两种语言的文档。在 master 分支上，它还会把 docs/_build/html "
"发布到 gh-pages 分支，通过 https://gchensy.github.io/kivi/ 访问。"

msgid "Development"
msgstr "开发"

msgid ""
"This section is for contributors. This page sets up a checkout and describes the checks and the "
"rules for pull requests. :doc:`documentation` describes how the documentation is organized, "
"written and translated, and :doc:`releasing` how a version is published."
msgstr "本节面向贡献者。本页介绍如何准备本地仓库，以及检查项和拉取请求的规则。 :doc:`documentation` 介绍文档的组织、写法和翻译， :doc:`releasing` 介绍如何发布版本。"

msgid "Set up"
msgstr "环境准备"

msgid ""
"Clone the repository and install it in editable mode with the test, documentation and lint "
"dependencies, then install the pre-commit hook."
msgstr "克隆仓库，以可编辑模式安装，并同时安装测试、文档和代码检查依赖，然后安装 pre-commit 钩子。"

msgid "Build and verify"
msgstr "构建与验证"

msgid ""
"ruff checks the code against the rules in ``pyproject.toml`` and formats it. The pre-commit hook "
"runs it before every commit, and the ``build`` check runs it on every pull request. A second job "
"runs the tests with the oldest NumPy and pandas versions that kivi supports."
msgstr ""
"ruff 按 ``pyproject.toml`` 中的规则检查代码并统一格式。pre-commit 钩子会在每次提交前运行它， ``build`` 检查也会在每个 pull request "
"上运行它。另一个任务会用 kivi 支持的最低版本 NumPy 和 pandas 运行测试。"

msgid ""
"The doctest builder runs every example in these pages and in the docstrings. The HTML build "
"writes English and simplified Chinese editions under docs/_build/html. API signatures come from "
"the installed package."
msgstr "doctest 构建器会运行本文档页面和 docstring 中的全部示例。HTML 构建会在 docs/_build/html 下生成英文和简体中文两套文档。API 签名从已安装的包提取。"

msgid "Pull requests"
msgstr "拉取请求"

msgid ""
"Branch from the latest master and keep one topic per pull request. The master branch accepts "
"changes only through pull requests, and only after the ``build`` check of the ``Documentation`` "
"workflow has passed on a branch that is up to date with master. Every pull request is therefore "
"tested together with everything merged before it. To update a branch, merge master into it. "
"Merged branches are deleted automatically."
msgstr ""
"从最新的 master 创建分支，每个拉取请求只做一件事。master 分支只接受通过拉取请求合入的改动，而且分支必须已与 master 同步，并通过 ``Documentation`` "
"工作流的 ``build`` 检查。因此，每个拉取请求都会和此前已合并的全部改动一起测试。要更新分支，把 master 合并进来即可。合并后的分支会被自动删除。"

msgid ""
"Pull requests that edit the same files are merged one after the other rather than developed in "
"parallel. Two kinds of file change in almost every pull request and are set up so that they "
"rarely conflict:"
msgstr "修改相同文件的拉取请求应依次完成和合并，不要并行开发。有两类文件几乎每个拉取请求都会改动，它们的组织方式让冲突很少发生："

msgid ""
"Release notes. Describe each user-facing change as a bullet item in a new file "
"``docs/release/unreleased/<topic>.<category>.rst``, where the category is ``new``, ``changed``, "
"``fixed`` or ``removed``. Do not edit :doc:`/release/index` itself: the files appear there under "
"the Unreleased heading."
msgstr ""
"发布说明。在新文件 ``docs/release/unreleased/<topic>.<category>.rst`` 中，把每项面向用户的改动写成一个列表项，其中类别为 ``new`` 、 "
"``changed`` 、 ``fixed`` 或 ``removed`` 。不要直接编辑 :doc:`/release/index` ：这些文件会显示在其中的“未发布”标题下。"

msgid ""
"The translation catalog. When a merge or rebase stops on a conflict in ``kivi.po``, run ``python "
"docs/build.py --merge-po``. It keeps the translations of both sides and adds the strings that are"
" new after the merge. Translate those, then add the catalog to the commit."
msgstr ""
"翻译目录。合并或变基因 ``kivi.po`` 冲突而中止时，运行 ``python docs/build.py --merge-po`` "
"。它会保留双方的翻译，并加入合并后新出现的文本。翻译这些文本后，再把目录加入提交。"

msgid ""
"A pull request that adds a module therefore only adds files: the module, its tests, a user guide "
"page, an API page in ``docs/api/`` and a release note. The API reference and the user guide pick "
"up new pages automatically. The pages that describe the whole library are updated together after "
"a group of such pull requests has merged, as :doc:`documentation` describes."
msgstr ""
"因此，新增模块的拉取请求只需新增文件：模块本身、它的测试、一个用户指南页面、 ``docs/api/`` 中的一个 API 页面，以及一条发布说明。API "
"参考和用户指南会自动收录新页面。描述整个库的页面会在一批这样的拉取请求合并之后统一更新，见 :doc:`documentation` 。"

msgid "Legacy review"
msgstr "旧版评审"

msgid ""
"This review of the 0.2.x code guided the rewrite in 0.3.0. Its findings describe the legacy "
"implementation; :doc:`/release/migration` describes how each part was replaced."
msgstr "这份对 0.2.x 代码的评审指导了 0.3.0 的重写。其中的发现描述的是旧版实现；各部分的替代方式见 :doc:`/release/migration` 。"

msgid "Findings from the legacy implementation"
msgstr "旧版实现中的问题"

msgid ""
"Packaging. The 0.2.8 wheel placed NumPy and pandas behind the all extra. A default installation "
"could import kivi but failed on its dataset and WOE entry points."
msgstr "打包。0.2.8 的 wheel 将 NumPy 和 pandas 列在 all 可选依赖中。默认安装后可以导入 kivi，但加载数据和调用 WOE 都会失败。"

msgid ""
"Dependencies. evaluate/BucketsUtils.py imported PySpark at module load even for pandas PSI. Its "
"standalone CSI function also referenced an undefined self. The new metric functions depend on "
"pandas and NumPy."
msgstr ""
"依赖。evaluate/BucketsUtils.py 在模块加载时导入 PySpark，连 pandas 版 PSI 也依赖 Spark。该文件的独立 CSI 函数引用了未定义的 "
"self。新版指标函数只依赖 pandas 和 NumPy。"

msgid ""
"Numerical results. The old WOE zero-cell logic adjusted one class with an if/elif and used the "
"original totals. The old PSI helper modified the displayed counts. Tests now check raw counts, "
"normalized shares and hand-calculated metrics."
msgstr "数值结果。旧版 WOE 使用 if/elif 处理零频数，一次只调整一类，还沿用调整前的分母。旧版 PSI 会更改展示的计数。新版测试检查原始计数、归一化占比及手算指标。"

msgid ""
"State. Model/Tree.py removed the target column from the caller's frame. Dataset generation also "
"reset NumPy's global random state. Future estimators should preserve inputs and take a local "
"random seed."
msgstr "状态。Model/Tree.py 会从调用方传入的 DataFrame 中移除目标列。模拟数据生成器也会重置 NumPy 的全局随机状态。后续迁移估计器时，应保留输入并使用局部随机种子。"

msgid ""
"Coverage. Legacy scorecard and WOE tests printed tables without asserting the expected numbers. "
"Use frozen datasets to check fitted boundaries, score direction, special values and row counts "
"before porting these workflows."
msgstr "测试。旧版评分卡与 WOE 用例打印结果表，却没有断言具体数值。迁移前应用固定样本核对分箱边界、评分方向、特殊值和总行数。"

msgid ""
"Project scope. The former source tree mixed modeling, databases, distributed execution, notebooks"
" and deployment configuration. Keep infrastructure-specific imports inside optional integrations "
"and keep business SQL and local configuration outside the distribution."
msgstr "项目范围。旧目录混合了建模算法、数据库、分布式计算、笔记本与部署配置。新增集成时应在可选模块内导入相应依赖，将业务 SQL 和本地配置保留在分发包之外。"

msgid "Outcome"
msgstr "落实情况"

msgid ""
"The rewrite began with binning, WOE and PSI and then rebuilt the rest of the scorecard workflow, "
"checking each part against the legacy outputs or reference implementations on fixed samples. "
":doc:`/release/index` lists the parts release by release. Spark, SQL, AHP and the model wrappers "
"were not rebuilt. They are out of scope and remain in the repository history before the rewrite."
msgstr ""
"重写从分箱、WOE 和 PSI 开始，随后重建了评分卡流程的其余部分，每一部分都在固定样本上与旧版输出或参考实现核对过。 :doc:`/release/index` "
"按版本列出了这些部分。Spark、SQL、AHP 和模型封装没有重建：它们不在范围内，保留在重写之前的仓库历史中。"

msgid "Releasing to PyPI"
msgstr "发布到 PyPI"

msgid ""
"The ``Release`` workflow publishes kivi to PyPI when a version tag is pushed. It uses PyPI "
"trusted publishing, so no API token is stored in the repository."
msgstr "推送版本标签时，``Release`` 工作流会把 kivi 发布到 PyPI。它使用 PyPI 可信发布（trusted publishing），因此仓库中不保存任何 API 令牌。"

msgid ""
"Set ``version`` in ``pyproject.toml`` to the new version, for example ``0.3.1``. Run ``python "
"docs/build.py --release 0.3.1``, which moves the release-note files into a section of "
":doc:`/release/index` dated today, and translate the new heading."
msgstr ""
"把 ``pyproject.toml`` 中的 ``version`` 改为新版本号，例如 ``0.3.1`` 。运行 ``python docs/build.py --release "
"0.3.1`` ，它会把发布说明文件移入 :doc:`/release/index` 中以当天日期命名的新章节；然后翻译新章节的标题。"

msgid ""
"The command changes nothing while ``python docs/build.py`` still reports entry points to update, "
"as described in :doc:`documentation`."
msgstr "如果 ``python docs/build.py`` 仍报告有入口页面需要更新，这条命令不会做任何改动，详见 :doc:`documentation` 。"

msgid "Merge the change into the master branch."
msgstr "将改动合并到 master 分支。"

msgid "Tag the merged commit with ``v`` followed by the version and push the tag:"
msgstr "在合并后的提交上打 ``v`` 加版本号的标签，并推送该标签："

msgid ""
"Pushing the tag starts the upload without an approval step, so push it only when the release is "
"ready. The workflow stops before anything is uploaded if the tag does not match the version or "
"points at a commit that is not on master. Otherwise it runs the tests, builds the source "
"distribution and the wheel, checks them with twine and uploads them to PyPI. Only then does it "
"create the GitHub release, with the distributions attached and notes generated from the merged "
"pull requests. A version such as ``0.4.0rc1`` is marked as a pre-release."
msgstr ""
"推送标签后上传会直接开始，没有审批环节，因此只在准备好发布时才推送标签。如果标签与版本号不一致，或者标签指向的提交不在 master "
"上，工作流会在上传任何内容之前停止。否则它会运行测试，构建源码包和 wheel，用 twine 检查后上传到 PyPI。上传成功后，它才会创建 GitHub "
"release，附上安装包，并根据已合并的拉取请求生成说明。``0.4.0rc1`` 这类版本会被标记为预发布。"

msgid "The repository protects this path in three places:"
msgstr "仓库在三处保护这条发布路径："

msgid "Only repository administrators can create, move or delete ``v*`` tags."
msgstr "只有仓库管理员可以创建、移动或删除 ``v*`` 标签。"

msgid "The ``pypi`` environment accepts deployments from ``v*`` tags only."
msgstr "``pypi`` 环境只接受来自 ``v*`` 标签的部署。"

msgid ""
"PyPI trusts only the ``release.yml`` workflow of ``gchensy/kivi`` running in the ``pypi`` "
"environment."
msgstr "PyPI 只信任 ``gchensy/kivi`` 中在 ``pypi`` 环境下运行的 ``release.yml`` 工作流。"

msgid ""
"PyPI never accepts the same version twice. If a run fails before the upload, delete the tag with "
"``git push origin :refs/tags/v0.3.1``, fix the problem and tag again. If the upload succeeded, "
"release the fix under a new version."
msgstr ""
"PyPI 不接受重复上传同一个版本。如果运行在上传之前失败，可以用 ``git push origin :refs/tags/v0.3.1`` "
"删除标签，修复问题后重新打标签。如果已经上传成功，请用新的版本号发布修复。"

msgid "Getting started"
msgstr "快速开始"

msgid ""
"kivi needs Python 3.10 or newer with NumPy and pandas. Install it, then follow the quickstart to "
"bin a variable, compute its weight of evidence and check its stability between two samples."
msgstr "kivi 需要 Python 3.10 或更高版本，以及 NumPy 和 pandas。安装后，可按快速上手完成一个变量的分箱、计算其证据权重，并检查它在两个样本之间的稳定性。"

msgid "Installation"
msgstr "安装"

msgid "Install from PyPI, GitHub or a local checkout and check the version."
msgstr "从 PyPI、GitHub 或本地仓库安装，并检查版本。"

msgid "Quickstart"
msgstr "快速上手"

msgid "A complete analysis of the bundled bank marketing data, with the output of every step."
msgstr "用随包的银行营销数据完成一次完整分析，并展示每一步的输出。"

msgid ""
"kivi requires Python 3.10 or newer, NumPy 1.24 or newer and pandas 2.0 or newer. pip installs "
"NumPy and pandas automatically."
msgstr "kivi 需要 Python 3.10 或更高版本、NumPy 1.24 或更高版本，以及 pandas 2.0 或更高版本。pip 会自动安装 NumPy 和 pandas。"

msgid "PyPI"
msgstr "PyPI"

msgid "Install the latest release:"
msgstr "安装最新发布版本："

msgid "GitHub"
msgstr "GitHub"

msgid "Install the development version directly from the repository:"
msgstr "直接从仓库安装开发版："

msgid "Local checkout"
msgstr "本地仓库"

msgid "Clone the repository and install it from the checkout:"
msgstr "克隆仓库后从本地安装："

msgid "Check the installed version:"
msgstr "检查已安装的版本："

msgid ""
"To work on kivi itself, use an editable install with the test and documentation dependencies. See"
" :doc:`/development/index`."
msgstr "如需参与 kivi 开发，请使用可编辑安装并加装测试和文档依赖，详见 :doc:`/development/index`。"

msgid ""
"The 0.2.x releases have a different API. Read :doc:`/release/migration` before upgrading existing"
" code."
msgstr "0.2.x 版本的 API 与当前版本不同。升级已有代码前，请先阅读 :doc:`/release/migration`。"

msgid ""
"This walkthrough bins a numeric and a categorical variable from the bundled data, measures how "
"well each bin separates the target and checks whether the age distribution shifts between two "
"samples. Every output below is produced by the code above it."
msgstr "本教程对随包数据中的一个数值变量和一个类别变量进行分箱，衡量各箱对目标的区分能力，并检查年龄分布在两个样本之间是否发生偏移。下面的每个输出都由其上方的代码生成。"

msgid "Load the data"
msgstr "加载数据"

msgid ""
"The bundled bank marketing data records whether a customer subscribed to a term deposit. The "
"split below demonstrates two samples; the rows do not represent a chronological validation split."
msgstr "随包的营销数据记录了客户是否认购定期存款。下面按行切出两个样本演示用法，这一切分没有时间验证含义。"

msgid "Fit bins on the reference sample"
msgstr "在基准样本上拟合分箱"

msgid ""
"Fit the edges on the reference sample only, then reuse them for every other sample so that the "
"counts remain comparable."
msgstr "只在基准样本上拟合边界，再将同一组边界用于其他所有样本，使各组计数保持可比。"

msgid ""
"The outer edges are infinite, so an age outside the reference range still falls into the first or"
" last bin."
msgstr "最外侧的边界为无穷，因此超出基准范围的年龄仍会落入第一个或最后一个箱。"

msgid "Weight of evidence"
msgstr "证据权重"

msgid ":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` returns one row per bin, in the order of the intervals."
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.woe.woe_table` 每箱返回一行，按区间顺序排列。"

msgid ""
"A positive WOE means that the bin holds a larger share of the subscribers than of the non-"
"subscribers. Age on its own separates the two groups only weakly."
msgstr "WOE 为正表示该箱在认购客户中的占比高于在未认购客户中的占比。仅凭年龄区分这两类客户的能力较弱。"

msgid ""
"Read the per-bin contributions before interpreting a total. A group with few events can have a "
"large WOE despite representing few customers."
msgstr "解读总值前先检查每一箱的贡献。只有少量事件的箱也可能有很大的 WOE，但它代表的客户可能很少。"

msgid "Share of customers, subscription rate and WOE for each age bin"
msgstr "每个年龄箱的客户占比、认购率和 WOE"

msgid ""
"The same table as a chart: the share of customers and the subscription rate per age bin (top) and"
" the WOE (bottom). Younger and older customers subscribe more often."
msgstr "同一张表的图形版本：上图为每个年龄箱的客户占比和认购率，下图为 WOE。年轻和年长的客户认购比例更高。"

msgid "Categorical variables"
msgstr "类别变量"

msgid "Pass category labels directly; they need no edges."
msgstr "类别标签可以直接传入，无需边界。"

msgid "Population stability"
msgstr "群体稳定性"

msgid ":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` compares the two samples bin by bin. It does not use the target."
msgstr ":func:`~kivi.stability.psi_table` 逐箱比较两个样本，不使用目标标签。"

msgid "Next steps"
msgstr "后续阅读"

msgid ""
":doc:`/user_guide/binning` explains quantile, uniform and supervised edges, ties, special values "
"and missing values."
msgstr ":doc:`/user_guide/binning` 介绍等频、等距与有监督分箱边界、重复切点、特殊值和缺失值。"

msgid ":doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` and :doc:`/user_guide/psi` give the formulas and the smoothing rule."
msgstr ":doc:`/user_guide/woe_iv` 和 :doc:`/user_guide/psi` 给出计算公式与平滑规则。"

msgid ":doc:`/api` lists every parameter."
msgstr ":doc:`/api` 列出全部参数。"

msgid "Credit risk modeling with pandas"
msgstr "基于 pandas 的信用风险建模"

msgid ""
"kivi is a pandas toolkit for credit risk and financial modeling. It profiles and bins the "
"candidate variables, measures how well each bin separates a binary outcome such as default, "
"selects the variables and fits a logistic scorecard, infers the outcomes of rejected applicants, "
"scales the model to points, evaluates it and calibrates it on a master scale, prices the cut-offs"
" and the expected loss, tracks how the population shifts once the model is live, and follows how "
"the approved loans perform. Tables come back as pandas DataFrames with one row per bin, grade, "
"cut-off or variable."
msgstr ""
"kivi 是面向信用风险与金融建模的 pandas "
"工具包。它分析候选变量并分箱，衡量每一箱对违约等二分类结果的区分能力，筛选变量并拟合逻辑回归评分卡，推断被拒申请人的结果，把模型刻度为分值，评估模型并基于主标尺进行校准，衡量各截断点的代价与预期损失，在模型上线后跟踪客群分布的变化，并跟踪已批准贷款的表现。表格结果都是"
" pandas DataFrame，每箱、每个等级、每个截断点或每个变量一行。"

msgid "At a glance"
msgstr "速览"

msgid "WOE chart for age with the share of customers and the event rate per bin"
msgstr "age 的 WOE 图，含每箱的客户占比和事件率"

msgid "The WOE chart for ``age``, drawn from ``evidence``."
msgstr "根据 ``evidence`` 绘制的 ``age`` WOE 图。"

msgid "Built for risk teams"
msgstr "为风控团队打造"

msgid "Missing values, distributions, event rates and a first IV ranking of every candidate in one table."
msgstr "用一张表列出每个候选变量的缺失值、分布、事件率和初步的 IV 排序。"

msgid "Fine and coarse classing, special values and monotonic WOE for logistic regression scorecards."
msgstr "细分箱与粗分箱、特殊值处理，以及用于逻辑回归评分卡的单调 WOE。"

msgid "WOE and IV"
msgstr "WOE 与 IV"

msgid ""
"The WOE and IV of every bin, with smoothing that leaves the counts alone, and the WOE encoding of"
" new data."
msgstr "每箱的 WOE 和 IV，平滑时不改动计数，以及新数据的 WOE 编码。"

msgid ""
"Rank candidates by IV, drop correlated variables and select a logistic model whose coefficients "
"all point the right way."
msgstr "按 IV 给候选变量排序，剔除高度相关的变量，并选出系数方向全部正确的逻辑回归模型。"

msgid ""
"Infer the outcomes of declined applicants by fuzzy augmentation, parceling or reweighting, and "
"refit the model on all applicants."
msgstr "用模糊扩充、打包法或重新加权推断被拒申请人的结果，并在全部申请人上重新拟合模型。"

msgid ""
"Turn the model into points with PDO scaling, score new applications and explain each score with "
"reason codes."
msgstr "用 PDO 刻度把模型转换为分值，为新申请打分，并用原因码解释每个分数。"

msgid "AUC, Gini, KS, gains and lift on development and validation samples."
msgstr "在开发样本和验证样本上计算 AUC、Gini、KS、增益与提升。"

msgid ""
"Prior correction, master scales, binomial, Jeffreys and Hosmer-Lemeshow tests per grade, and "
"Platt and isotonic recalibration."
msgstr "先验校正、主标尺，按评级做二项检验、Jeffreys 检验和 Hosmer-Lemeshow 检验，以及 Platt 与保序回归重新校准。"

msgid ""
"Approval and bad rates of every cut-off, swap sets between a current and a new score, and "
"expected loss by grade."
msgstr "每个截断点的通过率与坏账率、现行评分与新评分之间的交换集，以及按等级的预期损失。"

msgid ""
"Save the binning and WOE of every variable as versioned JSON, so production groups new data "
"exactly as development did."
msgstr "把每个变量的分箱和 WOE 保存为带版本号的 JSON，生产环境对新数据的分组与开发时完全一致。"

msgid ""
"Compare live data with the development sample bin by bin, track PSI over time and measure each "
"variable's effect on the score with CSI."
msgstr "逐箱比较线上数据与开发样本，按期跟踪 PSI，并用 CSI 衡量每个变量对分数的影响。"

msgid ""
"Vintage curves by origination cohort, roll rates and transition matrices between delinquency "
"buckets."
msgstr "按放款批次的 vintage 曲线，以及逾期档位之间的滚动率和迁移矩阵。"

msgid "How it works"
msgstr "工作流程"

msgid "Profile and bin"
msgstr "概况与分箱"

msgid ""
"``profile_table`` gives a first look at every candidate. ``bin_edges``, or a supervised method "
"such as ``monotonic_edges``, fits edges on the development sample once, and every later sample is"
" cut with them. The outer edges are infinite, so later values always fall into a bin."
msgstr ""
"``profile_table`` 让你先概览每个候选变量。 ``bin_edges`` ，或 ``monotonic_edges`` "
"等有监督方法，在开发样本上拟合一次边界，之后的每个样本都用这些边界分箱。最外侧边界为无穷，因此后续数据总能落入某个箱。"

msgid "Encode and fit"
msgstr "编码与拟合"

msgid ""
"``woe_table`` measures each bin against the target and ``woe_transform`` encodes it. ``stepwise``"
" and ``logistic_regression`` select the variables and fit the model, with ``weights`` for "
"inferred rejects."
msgstr ""
"``woe_table`` 衡量每箱相对目标变量的表现， ``woe_transform`` 据此编码。 ``stepwise`` 和 ``logistic_regression`` "
"筛选变量并拟合模型，可通过 ``weights`` 纳入推断的拒绝样本。"

msgid "Scale and evaluate"
msgstr "刻度与评估"

msgid ""
"``points_table`` turns the model into points, and ``gains_table``, ``roc_auc`` and ``ks`` measure"
" how well the score ranks applicants on a holdout sample."
msgstr "``points_table`` 把模型转换为分值， ``gains_table`` 、 ``roc_auc`` 和 ``ks`` 在留出样本上衡量分数对申请人的排序能力。"

msgid "Calibrate"
msgstr "校准"

msgid ""
"``master_scale`` and ``assign_grades`` group the PDs into grades, and ``calibration_table`` with "
"the binomial and Jeffreys tests checks the PD of each grade."
msgstr ""
"``master_scale`` 和 ``assign_grades`` 把 PD 划分为等级， ``calibration_table`` 配合二项检验和 Jeffreys 检验核对每个等级的"
" PD。"

msgid "Decide"
msgstr "决策"

msgid ""
"``cutoff_table`` shows what each cut-off approves and lets through, ``swap_set`` compares two "
"scores, and ``expected_loss_table`` adds up the expected loss of each grade."
msgstr ""
"``cutoff_table`` 展示每个截断点批准了多少申请人、放进了多少事件， ``swap_set`` 比较两个评分， ``expected_loss_table`` "
"汇总每个等级的预期损失。"

msgid "Deploy and monitor"
msgstr "部署与监控"

msgid ""
"``BinningSpec`` saves the binning as JSON for production. ``psi_table`` and ``csi_table`` compare"
" live data with development, and ``vintage_table`` follows the approved loans."
msgstr ""
"``BinningSpec`` 把分箱保存为 JSON 供生产环境使用。 ``psi_table`` 和 ``csi_table`` 比较线上数据与开发样本， ``vintage_table``"
" 跟踪已批准贷款的表现。"

msgid "Documentation"
msgstr "文档"

msgid "Install kivi and walk through a complete analysis of the bundled bank marketing data."
msgstr "安装 kivi，并用随包的银行营销数据完成一次完整分析。"

msgid "User guide"
msgstr "用户指南"

msgid ""
"One page per step of a risk model, from the profile of the candidates to vintage analysis, with "
"definitions, worked examples and how to read each result."
msgstr "风控模型的每个步骤各占一页，从候选变量概况到账龄分析，包含定义、完整示例以及各项结果的解读方法。"

msgid "Parameters, return values and examples for every public function."
msgstr "每个公共函数的参数、返回值和示例。"

msgid "What changed in each release and how to migrate code written for 0.2.x."
msgstr "各版本的变化，以及如何迁移为 0.2.x 编写的代码。"

msgid "Unreleased"
msgstr "未发布"

msgid "Changes merged since the last release."
msgstr "上次发布以来合并的改动。"

msgid "New"
msgstr "新增"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.monitoring`` tracks a score over time. ``monitoring_table`` gives one row "
"per period, such as a month, with the number of observations, the known outcomes and events, the "
"AUC, Gini and KS of the known outcomes, and the PSI of the score against a reference period or a "
"reference sample, on bands fitted once on the reference. A missing target marks an outcome that "
"is not known yet; it counts in ``total`` but not in the event columns, and a period without both "
"classes has NaN discrimination instead of an error."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.monitoring`` 按期跟踪评分。 ``monitoring_table`` 每期一行（例如每月），给出观测数、已知结果数和事件数、已知结果上的 AUC、Gini 和"
" KS，以及评分相对基准期或基准样本的 PSI，评分段只在基准上拟合一次。缺失的目标值表示结果尚未得知：它计入 ``total`` ，但不计入事件相关的列；两类结果不全的期，其区分能力为 NaN"
" 而不是报错。"

msgid ""
"``stability_table`` gives the PSI of every grouped variable in every period against the same "
"reference, for the variable part of a stability report. Both functions take ``weights``, and "
"integer weights give the same table as repeating rows, for ``monitoring_table`` on the same band "
"edges."
msgstr ""
"``stability_table`` 给出每个已分组变量在每一期相对同一基准的 PSI，用于稳定性报告的变量部分。两个函数都接受 ``weights`` ，整数权重与重复相应行得到的表相同；对"
" ``monitoring_table`` 而言，这要求评分段边界相同。"

msgid "Changed"
msgstr "变更"

msgid ""
"The topic guides follow one outline with the same section titles, such as ``Special values``, "
"``Sample weights`` and ``Errors and warnings``, and their openings link to the steps before and "
"after them. The binning guide gathers its special values in one section, and the univariate "
"profile shows special codes after the screening by IV. The first mention of a kivi function in "
"each section links to its API entry."
msgstr ""
"各篇主题指南采用同一结构和相同的小节标题，例如 ``Special values`` （特殊值）、 ``Sample weights`` （样本权重）和 ``Errors and "
"warnings`` （错误与警告），开篇链接到前后两个步骤。分箱指南把特殊值的内容集中到一节，单变量概况在按 IV 筛选之后再介绍特殊值编码。kivi 函数在每一节第一次出现时都链接到其 "
"API 条目。"

msgid ""
"The API reference starts with two new pages: the conventions that every function follows, such as"
" the order of the arguments, keyword-only options, inputs and results, sample weights and error "
"messages, and a glossary of credit risk terms. Its module pages come in the order of the user "
"guide, each with an introduction and a link to its guide, and ``:mod:`` links now reach them."
msgstr ""
"API "
"参考新增两页并排在最前面：一页是所有函数共同遵守的约定，包括参数顺序、仅限关键字的选项、输入与结果、样本权重和错误信息；另一页是信用风险术语表。模块页面按用户指南的顺序排列，每页都有简介和指向对应指南的链接，"
" ``:mod:`` 链接现在也能跳转到这些页面。"

msgid ""
"The migration guide lists the ROC and precision-recall curves, precision, recall, F1 score and "
"confusion matrix of ``BinaryMetrics`` and the correlation heatmaps of ``evaluate/Heatmap.py`` as "
"not ported, with their replacements."
msgstr ""
"迁移指南把 ``BinaryMetrics`` 的 ROC 曲线和精确率-召回率曲线、精确率、召回率、F1 分数和混淆矩阵，以及 ``evaluate/Heatmap.py`` "
"的相关性热力图列为未移植，并给出替代做法。"

msgid "0.7.0 (2026-11-20)"
msgstr "0.7.0（2026-11-20）"

msgid ""
"``kivi.datasets.make_applications`` simulates seeded loan applications with numeric and "
"categorical features, the PD of an incumbent scorecard, policy declines, the approval decision "
"and a true default flag for every applicant, to try reject inference on."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.datasets.make_applications`` 按种子模拟贷款申请数据，每个申请人都有数值型和类别型特征、现行评分卡的 "
"PD、政策拒绝、审批决策和真实的违约标记，可用来试验拒绝推断。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.calibration.master_scale`` builds a master scale from the PD of each grade, such as a "
"geometric grid from ``numpy.geomspace``: one row per grade with its lower bound, PD and upper "
"bound, covering 0 to 1. The bounds are the geometric means of adjacent PDs by default, or their "
"arithmetic means with ``boundary=\"arithmetic\"``, as in the 0.2 versions."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.calibration.master_scale`` 根据每个等级的 PD 构建主标尺，例如由 ``numpy.geomspace`` "
"生成的几何网格：每个等级一行，包含其下界、PD 和上界，覆盖 0 到 1。界限默认取相邻 PD 的几何平均数，设置 ``boundary=\"arithmetic\"`` 时取其算术平均数，与 "
"0.2 版本相同。"

msgid ""
"``fit_grade_pd`` fits the PD of each grade to observed default rates, with the logarithm of the "
"rate a straight line in the grade number, by least squares weighted with the number of "
"observations. A grade without defaults enters the fit with ``smoothing`` defaults, and a grade "
"without observations gets a PD from the line."
msgstr ""
"``fit_grade_pd`` 按观测违约率拟合每个等级的 PD：把违约率的对数拟合为等级编号的直线，使用以观测数为权重的最小二乘法。没有违约的等级以 ``smoothing`` "
"次违约参与拟合，没有观测的等级从这条直线得到 PD。"

msgid ""
"``assign_grades`` gives each predicted PD the grade of a scale as an ordered categorical, which "
"``calibration_table`` counts directly, in the order of the scale. A PD on a bound goes to the "
"lower grade, as with ``pandas.cut``."
msgstr ""
"``assign_grades`` 以有序分类变量的形式为每个预测 PD 指定标尺上的等级， ``calibration_table`` 可以直接按标尺的顺序统计这些等级。恰好落在界限上的 PD"
" 归入较低的等级，与 ``pandas.cut`` 相同。"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.reject_inference`` infers outcomes for rejected applicants, so that a "
"scorecard developed on approved applicants can be refitted on all of them. ``fuzzy_augmentation``"
" splits each reject into a bad and a good row weighted by its PD, ``parceling`` labels the "
"rejects of each score band at the band's bad rate with a seeded generator, or returns the "
"expected weights, and ``reweighting`` weights the approved applicants of each band by the inverse"
" of its approval rate. A ``factor`` above 1 raises the inferred bad rate, and bands without "
"approved applicants raise an error."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.reject_inference`` 推断拒绝申请人的结果，使在获批申请人上开发的评分卡能在全部申请人上重新拟合。 ``fuzzy_augmentation`` "
"把每个拒绝申请人拆成按其 PD 加权的一行坏样本和一行好样本； ``parceling`` 用带种子的生成器按各评分段的坏账率标记其中的拒绝申请人，或者返回期望权重； "
"``reweighting`` 以各评分段通过率的倒数为该段获批申请人加权。大于 1 的 ``factor`` 会提高推断的坏账率，没有获批申请人的评分段会引发错误。"

msgid ""
"``logistic_regression`` and ``stepwise`` take ``weights``, frequency weights like those of "
"statsmodels' ``GLM(freq_weights=...)``. Integer weights give the same coefficients, standard "
"errors and selection as repeating rows; weights that do not count observations, such as those of "
"reject inference, make the standard errors and p-values too small."
msgstr ""
"``logistic_regression`` 和 ``stepwise`` 接受 ``weights`` ，即与 statsmodels 的 ``GLM(freq_weights=...)``"
" 相同的频数权重。整数权重与重复行得到相同的系数、标准误和变量选择；不表示观测个数的权重（例如拒绝推断的权重）会使标准误和 p 值偏小。"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.strategy`` supports the credit decisions that follow a scorecard. "
"``cutoff_table`` shows, for each candidate cut-off of a PD or of negated points, the approval "
"rate, the bad rate of the approved book, the shares of bads and goods it rejects and, with "
"``loss``, the expected loss it approves. Scores at or below the cut-off are approved, so tied "
"scores always get the same decision."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.strategy`` 支撑评分卡之后的信贷决策。``cutoff_table`` 针对 PD "
"或取负分数的每个候选截断点，给出通过率、通过客群的坏账率、被拒绝的坏客户和好客户所占比例，传入 ``loss`` "
"时还给出通过客群的预期损失。评分不高于截断点即予以通过，因此相同评分总是得到相同的决策。"

msgid ""
"``swap_set`` compares the decisions of a current and a new score at their cut-offs: the "
"applicants both approve, the swap-ins and swap-outs, and those both decline, with event rates "
"where outcomes are known. A missing target marks an unknown outcome, such as that of an applicant"
" the current score declined."
msgstr ""
"``swap_set`` "
"在各自的截断点上比较现行评分与新评分的决策：两者都通过的申请人、换入和换出，以及两者都拒绝的申请人，并在结果已知时给出事件率。缺失的目标值表示结果未知，例如被现行评分拒绝的申请人。"

msgid ""
"``expected_loss`` multiplies PD, LGD and EAD, and ``expected_loss_table`` adds up the exposure "
"and the expected loss of each grade, with the expected loss rate and the exposure-weighted PD."
msgstr "``expected_loss`` 将 PD、LGD 与 EAD 相乘，``expected_loss_table`` 汇总每个等级的敞口和预期损失，并给出预期损失率和按敞口加权的 PD。"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.univariate`` profiles the candidates of a model. ``profile_table`` "
"summarizes every column of a data frame in one row: its kind, missing values, distinct and most "
"frequent values and, for numeric columns, the range, quantiles, mean and standard deviation. With"
" a target it adds the event rates and lifts of missing and non-missing rows, the IV of a quick "
"binning and the Gini coefficient of numeric values. Tied quantiles are recorded in the "
"``tied_bins`` column instead of raising a warning for each column, and ``special`` codes and "
"``weights`` work as in ``fit_spec``."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.univariate`` 对模型的候选变量进行概况分析。 ``profile_table`` "
"用一行概括数据框的每一列：类型、缺失值、不同取值个数和最常见的取值；数值列还给出取值范围、分位数、均值和标准差。有目标变量时，还会加入缺失行与非缺失行的事件率和提升度、快速分箱的 IV "
"以及数值取值的 Gini 系数。分位数重合会记录在 ``tied_bins`` 列中，而不会对每一列发出警告； ``special`` 编码和 ``weights`` 的用法与 "
"``fit_spec`` 相同。"

msgid ""
"The risk modeling workflow screens the candidates with ``profile_table``, calibrates the PD on a "
"master scale with ``master_scale`` and ``assign_grades``, and sets a cut-off with "
"``cutoff_table`` and ``expected_loss_table``. The user guide has new charts for cut-off curves, "
"reject inference, grade PDs and missing values, and the README shows the cut-off and reject "
"inference charts."
msgstr ""
"风控建模流程示例改用 ``profile_table`` 筛选候选变量，用 ``master_scale`` 和 ``assign_grades`` 在主标尺上校准 PD，并用 "
"``cutoff_table`` 和 ``expected_loss_table`` 设定截断点。用户指南新增截断点曲线、拒绝推断、等级 PD 和缺失值图，README "
"也展示了截断点图和拒绝推断图。"

msgid "Fixed"
msgstr "修复"

msgid ""
"``gains_table`` warned about tied scores by suggesting the ``special`` argument of ``bin_edges``,"
" which ``gains_table`` does not take. It now suggests fewer bins or explicit edges, as "
"``cutoff_table`` does, and the warning points at the line that called it."
msgstr ""
"``gains_table`` 在评分并列时发出的警告曾建议使用 ``bin_edges`` 的 ``special`` 参数，而 ``gains_table`` 并没有这个参数。现在它与 "
"``cutoff_table`` 一样，建议减少箱数或给出明确的边界，并且警告指向调用它的那一行。"

msgid "0.6.0 (2026-11-20)"
msgstr "0.6.0（2026-11-20）"

msgid ""
"``kivi.calibration.platt_fit`` and ``platt_predict`` calibrate a score with a logistic curve, and"
" ``isotonic_fit`` and ``isotonic_predict`` with a step function that rises with the score. The "
"fits return plain numbers, a slope and an intercept or band edges and their probabilities, that "
"apply to the scores of any later sample."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.calibration.platt_fit`` 和 ``platt_predict`` 用逻辑曲线校准评分， ``isotonic_fit`` 和 "
"``isotonic_predict`` 则用随评分上升的阶梯函数进行校准。拟合结果是普通的数值（斜率和截距，或分段边界及其概率），可以应用到之后任何样本的评分上。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.stability.csi_table`` computes the characteristic stability index of a scorecard variable:"
" the change of each group's share from the reference to the current sample, multiplied by the "
"group's points. Its sum is the change of the variable's average points, and over all variables "
"the change of the average score. The shares are not smoothed, and a group without points raises "
"an error unless ``unseen_points`` gives its points."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.stability.csi_table`` "
"计算评分卡变量的特征稳定性指标：每组占比从基准样本到当前样本的变化乘以该组的分值。其总和是该变量平均分值的变化，对所有变量求和则是平均分数的变化。占比不做平滑；没有分值的分组会引发错误，除非用 "
"``unseen_points`` 给出其分值。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.datasets.load_bank`` loads the bank marketing data. ``Dataset.bank_data`` returns the same"
" data and keeps working without a warning."
msgstr "``kivi.datasets.load_bank`` 读取银行营销数据。 ``Dataset.bank_data`` 返回相同的数据，并且可以继续使用，不会发出警告。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel`` simulates a seeded monthly panel of instalment loans whose "
"delinquency rolls forward and cures, to try the vintage and roll-rate functions on."
msgstr "``kivi.datasets.make_loan_panel`` 按给定种子模拟分期贷款的月度面板数据，其中逾期会向前滚动，也会回到正常，可用来试用 Vintage 和滚动率相关函数。"

msgid ""
"``reason_codes`` takes ``unseen_points``, the points of applicants in groups that "
"``woe_transform`` encoded with ``unseen``, one value or values by variable. Points that match no "
"group but lie within ``atol`` of ``unseen_points`` cost nothing, so the variable is not one of "
"those applicants' reasons. Every other mismatch still raises an error, which now suggests "
"checking ``atol`` and the model and scaling first."
msgstr ""
"``reason_codes`` 新增 ``unseen_points`` 参数，即 ``woe_transform`` 用 ``unseen`` "
"编码的分组中申请人的分值，可以是一个值，也可以按变量给出。与任何分组都不匹配、但与 ``unseen_points`` 相差不超过 ``atol`` "
"的分值视为没有造成损失，因此该变量不会成为这些申请人的原因。其他任何不匹配仍会引发错误，错误信息现在会先提示检查 ``atol`` 以及模型和刻度。"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.spec`` bins all the columns of a data frame at once. ``fit_spec`` fits each"
" numeric column with ``bin_edges`` or a supervised method chosen by column, or with given edges, "
"and measures the WOE of every group; other columns keep their labels. The binning is never "
"changed automatically."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.spec`` 一次对数据框的所有列分箱。 ``fit_spec`` 用 ``bin_edges`` 、按列选定的有监督方法或给定的边界拟合每个数值列，并计算每个分组的 "
"WOE；其他列保留其标签。分箱从不自动更改。"

msgid ""
"The resulting ``BinningSpec`` groups a sample with ``cut``, encodes it with ``woe_transform`` "
"using an unseen-group policy by column, and keeps the ``woe_table`` of every column for review. "
"``to_json`` and ``from_json`` save and load it without changing the groups or the WOE encoding, "
"so production reproduces development exactly."
msgstr ""
"得到的 ``BinningSpec`` 用 ``cut`` 对样本分组，用 ``woe_transform`` 按列的未见分组策略编码，并保留每一列的 ``woe_table`` 供审阅。 "
"``to_json`` 和 ``from_json`` 保存并加载它，分组和 WOE 编码都不会改变，因此生产环境可以完全复现开发时的结果。"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.vintage`` analyses loan portfolios. ``vintage_table`` gives the cumulative "
"bad rate of each origination cohort by month on book, by count or by amount lent, and leaves the "
"months that a cohort has not reached as NaN. ``transition_matrix`` counts the movements of loans "
"between delinquency buckets or of obligors between rating grades, as counts, row shares or sums "
"of balances, and ``roll_rates`` gives the share of each bucket that rolls to the next worse one."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.vintage`` 用于分析贷款资产组合。 ``vintage_table`` 按账龄给出每个放款批次的累计坏账率，可以按笔数或按放款金额计算，并把批次尚未达到的账龄留为 "
"NaN。 ``transition_matrix`` 统计贷款在逾期档位之间、或债务人在评级之间的迁移，结果可以是计数、行内比例或余额之和； ``roll_rates`` "
"给出每个档位滚动到下一个更差档位的比例。"

msgid ""
"``roc_auc``, ``gini``, ``ks``, ``gains_table``, ``brier_score`` and ``calibration_table`` take "
"``weights``, like ``woe_table``. Counts become sums of weights, and integer weights give the same"
" result as repeating rows, for ``gains_table`` on fixed edges."
msgstr ""
"``roc_auc`` 、 ``gini`` 、 ``ks`` 、 ``gains_table`` 、 ``brier_score`` 和 ``calibration_table`` 与 "
"``woe_table`` 一样接受 ``weights`` 。计数变为权重之和，整数权重与重复相应行的结果相同（ ``gains_table`` 须使用固定边界）。"

msgid ""
"The risk modeling workflow saves the shortlist's binning with ``fit_spec`` and adds the "
"characteristic stability index of every scorecard variable to its stability report. The user "
"guide has new charts for gains, calibration and vintage curves, and the README shows the gains "
"and vintage charts."
msgstr ""
"风控建模流程示例用 ``fit_spec`` 保存入选变量的分箱，并在稳定性报告中加入每个评分卡变量的特征稳定性指数（CSI）。用户指南新增增益、校准和 vintage 曲线图，README "
"也展示了增益图和 vintage 曲线图。"

msgid "On pandas 2.0, ``calibration_table`` no longer fails when the target has a nullable integer dtype."
msgstr "在 pandas 2.0 上，目标为可空整数类型时， ``calibration_table`` 不再报错。"

msgid ""
"``cut``, ``bin_edges`` and the supervised binning functions match special codes after converting "
"numeric strings, so a column read as text, where ``pdays`` holds ``\"-1\"``, gives the code "
"``-1`` its own group instead of putting it into an interval. Boolean special codes, which ``True "
"== 1`` made match the value 1, raise an error."
msgstr ""
"``cut`` 、 ``bin_edges`` 和有监督分箱函数会在转换数字字符串之后再匹配特殊编码，因此按文本读入的列（例如 ``pdays`` 中的 ``\"-1\"`` ）会让编码 "
"``-1`` 单独成组，而不是落入某个区间。布尔型特殊编码会报错：由于 ``True == 1`` ，它们原先会匹配取值 1。"

msgid "Removed"
msgstr "移除"

msgid ""
"``kivi.evaluate`` is removed; import ``psi_table`` and the other stability functions from "
"``kivi.stability``."
msgstr "移除 ``kivi.evaluate`` ；请从 ``kivi.stability`` 导入 ``psi_table`` 等稳定性函数。"

msgid "``bin_edges`` no longer accepts ``method`` by position; pass ``method=\"uniform\"`` by keyword."
msgstr "``bin_edges`` 不再接受按位置传入的 ``method`` ；请用关键字传入，例如 ``method=\"uniform\"`` 。"

msgid "0.5.0 (2026-11-20)"
msgstr "0.5.0（2026-11-20）"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.calibration`` checks the calibration of PDs. ``prior_correction`` and "
"``corrected_intercept`` correct a model for a development sample with another event rate. "
"``calibration_table`` compares the observed and predicted default rates of master scale grades or"
" other groups, which ``binomial_test``, ``jeffreys_test`` and ``hosmer_lemeshow`` then test. "
"``herfindahl_index`` measures the concentration of the grades."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.calibration`` 用于检查 PD 的校准情况。 ``prior_correction`` 和 ``corrected_intercept`` "
"在开发样本的事件率与总体不同时校正模型。 ``calibration_table`` 比较主标尺等级或其他分组的观测违约率与预测违约率，再由 ``binomial_test`` 、 "
"``jeffreys_test`` 和 ``hosmer_lemeshow`` 进行检验。 ``herfindahl_index`` 衡量各等级的集中程度。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.woe.woe``, ``kivi.woe.iv`` and ``kivi.stability.psi`` compute WOE, IV and PSI from counts "
"that are already aggregated, including weighted counts."
msgstr "``kivi.woe.woe`` 、 ``kivi.woe.iv`` 和 ``kivi.stability.psi`` 可直接根据已汇总的计数（包括加权计数）计算 WOE、IV 和 PSI。"

msgid "``kivi.stability`` holds ``psi_table`` and ``psi``."
msgstr "``kivi.stability`` 模块包含 ``psi_table`` 和 ``psi`` 。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.metrics`` evaluates a score against a binary target. ``roc_auc``, ``gini`` and ``ks`` "
"measure how well it ranks events above non-events, ``gains_table`` reports event rates, captured "
"events, KS and lift by score band, and ``brier_score`` compares predicted probabilities with the "
"outcomes. Like ``woe_table``, each takes the score first and the target second, the reverse of "
"scikit-learn. A higher score must mean a higher event probability, so negate scorecard points "
"before passing them in."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.metrics`` 根据二分类目标评估评分。``roc_auc``、``gini`` 和 ``ks`` 衡量评分把事件排在非事件之前的能力，``gains_table`` "
"按评分段报告事件率、捕获的事件、KS 和提升度，``brier_score`` 将预测概率与实际结果进行比较。与 ``woe_table`` 一样，这些函数都是评分在前、目标在后，与 "
"scikit-learn 的顺序相反。评分越高必须表示事件概率越高，因此评分卡分数须取负后再传入。"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges``, ``chimerge_edges``, ``tree_edges``, ``monotonic_edges`` and ``woe_table`` take "
"``weights``, and ``psi_table`` takes ``reference_weights`` and ``current_weights``. Counts become"
" sums of weights, quantile edges become weighted quantiles by the inverted CDF, and observations "
"or groups with zero weight are left out."
msgstr ""
"``bin_edges`` 、 ``chimerge_edges`` 、 ``tree_edges`` 、 ``monotonic_edges`` 和 ``woe_table`` 新增 "
"``weights`` 参数， ``psi_table`` 新增 ``reference_weights`` 和 ``current_weights`` "
"参数。计数变为权重之和，等频边界变为逆累积分布意义下的加权分位数，权重为零的观测或分组会被排除。"

msgid ""
"The new module ``kivi.scorecard`` scales a logistic regression on WOE values into scorecard "
"points. ``score_scaling``, ``pd_to_score`` and ``score_to_pd`` convert between probabilities and "
"scores from the points to double the odds, a base score and base odds. ``points_table`` gives the"
" points of every group, ``woe_to_points`` those of each applicant, and ``reason_codes`` names the"
" variables that cost an applicant the most points."
msgstr ""
"新模块 ``kivi.scorecard`` 把基于 WOE 的逻辑回归转换为评分卡分值。 ``score_scaling`` 、 ``pd_to_score`` 和 "
"``score_to_pd`` 依据 PDO（几率翻倍所需分数）、基准分数和基准几率，在概率与分数之间相互转换。 ``points_table`` 给出每个分组的分值， "
"``woe_to_points`` 给出每个申请人的分值， ``reason_codes`` 列出让申请人失分最多的变量。"

msgid ""
"The new ``kivi.selection`` module selects the variables of a scorecard from WOE-encoded "
"candidates. ``correlation_filter`` drops one variable of each strongly correlated pair, keeping "
"the one with the higher priority, such as its IV. ``vif`` computes variance inflation factors."
msgstr ""
"新增 ``kivi.selection`` 模块，用于从 WOE 编码的候选变量中筛选评分卡变量。 ``correlation_filter`` "
"对每一对强相关的变量剔除其中一个，保留优先级（例如 IV）较高的那个。 ``vif`` 计算方差膨胀因子。"

msgid ""
"``logistic_regression`` fits a logistic regression in NumPy and reports each coefficient with its"
" standard error, Wald z statistic and p-value. It raises ``SeparationError`` when the variables "
"separate the classes, so that the estimates do not exist."
msgstr ""
"``logistic_regression`` 用 NumPy 拟合逻辑回归，并报告每个系数及其标准误、Wald z 统计量和 p 值。当变量把两类完全分开、以致估计值不存在时，它会抛出 "
"``SeparationError`` 。"

msgid ""
"``stepwise`` selects variables by their p-values in forward, backward or both directions. By "
"default, it keeps every coefficient positive, as expected for kivi's WOE."
msgstr "``stepwise`` 按 p 值进行向前、向后或双向的变量筛选。默认情况下，它使每个系数都为正，这正是 kivi 的 WOE 所预期的。"

msgid ""
"``woe_transform`` replaces each group with its WOE from a ``woe_table`` result, the encoding used"
" by a scorecard model. Groups that are not in the table raise an error unless ``unseen`` gives "
"their WOE."
msgstr ""
"``woe_transform`` 用 ``woe_table`` 结果中的 WOE 替换每个分组，这正是评分卡模型使用的编码。不在表中的分组会引发错误，除非用 ``unseen`` 指定其 "
"WOE。"

msgid ""
"The API reference has a page for each module. Links to a function on the former single page now "
"go to the page of its module."
msgstr "API 参考改为每个模块一页。原来指向单页中某个函数的链接，现在改为指向该函数所在模块的页面。"

msgid ""
"``method`` of ``bin_edges`` is keyword-only. Passing it by position raises a ``FutureWarning`` "
"and stops working in 0.6.0."
msgstr "``bin_edges`` 的 ``method`` 参数改为仅限关键字。按位置传入会发出 ``FutureWarning`` ，并将在 0.6.0 中失效。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.evaluate`` is deprecated in favour of ``kivi.stability``. Importing ``psi_table`` from it "
"raises a ``FutureWarning``, and the module is removed in 0.6.0."
msgstr ""
"``kivi.evaluate`` 已弃用，请改用 ``kivi.stability`` 。从中导入 ``psi_table`` 会发出 ``FutureWarning`` ，该模块将在 "
"0.6.0 中移除。"

msgid ""
"The risk modeling workflow runs end to end: variable selection, a fitted logistic model, "
"scorecard points, evaluation, calibration and score stability."
msgstr "风控建模流程现在完整串联：变量筛选、逻辑回归拟合、评分卡分值、模型评估、校准以及分数稳定性。"

msgid ""
"``woe_table`` also reports ``total``, ``total_share`` and ``event_rate`` for each group, the "
"columns of a classing report. They use the observed counts; only ``non_event_share`` and "
"``event_share`` are smoothed."
msgstr ""
"``woe_table`` 为每组新增 ``total`` 、 ``total_share`` 和 ``event_rate`` 三列，即分箱报表中常用的列。它们使用实际观测到的计数；只有 "
"``non_event_share`` 和 ``event_share`` 经过平滑。"

msgid ""
"``woe_table`` and ``psi_table`` no longer cause pandas to issue ``RuntimeWarning: invalid value "
"encountered in cast`` on NumPy older than 2.2 when the groups come from ``pandas.cut`` with "
"infinite edges."
msgstr ""
"分组来自带无穷端点的 ``pandas.cut`` 时， ``woe_table`` 和 ``psi_table`` 在 NumPy 2.2 以下的版本上不再引发 pandas 的 "
"``RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in cast`` 。"

msgid ""
"On pandas 2.0, ``cut`` and the supervised binning functions no longer fail when nullable integer "
"or float values are combined with ``special``."
msgstr "在 pandas 2.0 上，可空整数或浮点数与 ``special`` 一起使用时， ``cut`` 和监督分箱函数不再报错。"

msgid "0.4.0 (2026-11-19)"
msgstr "0.4.0（2026-11-19）"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges`` takes a ``special`` argument. Codes such as ``-1`` or ``-999`` are left out when "
"the edges are fitted."
msgstr "``bin_edges`` 新增 ``special`` 参数。 ``-1`` 、 ``-999`` 等编码在拟合边界时会被排除。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.binning.cut`` assigns values to the fitted bins and gives each special value its own "
"group. Without special values it returns the same result as ``pandas.cut``."
msgstr "``kivi.binning.cut`` 把取值分配到拟合好的各箱，并让每个特殊值单独成组。不传特殊值时，结果与 ``pandas.cut`` 相同。"

msgid ""
"``chimerge_edges``, ``tree_edges`` and ``monotonic_edges`` fit edges from a binary target: "
"ChiMerge merging of fine quantile bins, decision-tree splits by entropy or Gini with a minimum "
"bin share, and merging until the WOE is monotonic. They accept the same array-like inputs as "
"``woe_table``, return infinite-ended edges like ``bin_edges`` and need only NumPy and pandas."
msgstr ""
"``chimerge_edges``、``tree_edges`` 和 ``monotonic_edges`` 依据二分类目标拟合边界：分别是对等频细分箱做 ChiMerge "
"合并、按熵或基尼指数做决策树切分（可设定最小箱占比），以及合并到 WOE 单调为止。它们接受与 ``woe_table`` 相同的类数组输入，与 ``bin_edges`` "
"一样返回两端为无穷的边界，只依赖 NumPy 和 pandas。"

msgid "The binning guide compares the three methods on the bank data, with a chart for each."
msgstr "分箱指南在银行数据上对比了这三种方法，并为每种方法配有图表。"

msgid ""
"``chimerge_edges``, ``tree_edges`` and ``monotonic_edges`` take ``special`` like ``bin_edges``. "
"The codes are left out of the fit together with their labels, and ``kivi.binning.cut`` with the "
"same codes gives each one its own group."
msgstr ""
"``chimerge_edges``、``tree_edges`` 和 ``monotonic_edges`` 与 ``bin_edges`` 一样接受 ``special`` "
"参数。这些编码连同其标签不参与拟合；再把相同的编码传给 ``kivi.binning.cut`` ，即可让每个编码单独成组。"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges``, ``woe_table`` and ``psi_table`` accept any one-dimensional array-like input, such "
"as a list or a NumPy array. Group and target series passed to ``woe_table`` must still share an "
"index; arrays and lists are matched by position."
msgstr ""
"``bin_edges`` 、 ``woe_table`` 和 ``psi_table`` 接受任意一维类数组输入，例如列表或 NumPy 数组。传给 ``woe_table`` "
"的分组与标签序列仍须共享同一索引；数组和列表按位置对应。"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges`` issues a ``UserWarning`` when tied edges leave fewer bins than requested. The "
"message names the most frequent value so that it can be passed in ``special``."
msgstr "边界重合导致实际箱数少于期望箱数时， ``bin_edges`` 会发出 ``UserWarning`` 。提示信息会写出出现次数最多的取值，便于将其传给 ``special`` 。"

msgid "Error messages name the argument and report the value received."
msgstr "错误信息会写明参数名以及收到的值。"

msgid ""
"``kivi.__version__`` is ``\"0+unknown\"`` when kivi is imported from a source tree that is not "
"installed, instead of raising an error."
msgstr "从未安装的源码目录导入 kivi 时， ``kivi.__version__`` 为 ``\"0+unknown\"`` ，不再抛出错误。"

msgid "Group counts use ``numpy.bincount``, which is faster on large samples."
msgstr "分组计数改用 ``numpy.bincount`` ，在大样本上更快。"

msgid "The API reference documents errors, warnings, formulas and related functions."
msgstr "API 参考补充了异常、警告、公式和相关函数的说明。"

msgid ""
"``woe_table`` and ``psi_table`` list categorical groups, including the result of ``pandas.cut``, "
"in category order with missing values last. Other labels keep the order in which they first "
"appear. Previously all groups followed first appearance, and ``sort_index`` was needed to put "
"intervals in order."
msgstr ""
"``woe_table`` 和 ``psi_table`` 对分类型分组（包括 ``pandas.cut`` "
"的结果）按类别顺序排列，缺失值排在最后。其他标签仍按首次出现的次序排列。此前所有分组都按首次出现的次序排列，需要用 ``sort_index`` 才能让区间有序。"

msgid "0.3.0 (2026-11-19)"
msgstr "0.3.0（2026-11-19）"

msgid ""
"A rewrite around a small pandas core. Read :doc:`migration` before upgrading code written for "
"0.2.x."
msgstr "围绕精简的 pandas 核心重写。升级为 0.2.x 编写的代码前，请先阅读 :doc:`migration`。"

msgid ""
"``bin_edges`` fits quantile or uniform edges on a reference sample. The outer edges are infinite,"
" so the result can be passed to ``pandas.cut`` for any later sample."
msgstr "``bin_edges`` 在基准样本上拟合等频或等距边界。最外侧边界为无穷，因此结果可以传给 ``pandas.cut``，用于之后的任意样本。"

msgid ""
"``woe_table`` and ``psi_table`` return raw counts, smoothed shares and a contribution for each "
"group, including missing values."
msgstr "``woe_table`` 和 ``psi_table`` 返回每组的原始计数、平滑后的占比和单组贡献，缺失值也单独成组。"

msgid "Documentation in English and Simplified Chinese."
msgstr "提供英文和简体中文文档。"

msgid "NumPy and pandas are required dependencies. The 0.2.8 wheel placed them behind the ``all`` extra."
msgstr "NumPy 和 pandas 成为必需依赖。0.2.8 的 wheel 曾将它们放在 ``all`` 可选依赖中。"

msgid "The ``psi`` column holds the contribution of each bin. It previously repeated the overall total."
msgstr "``psi`` 列给出每箱的贡献，此前该列逐行重复总值。"

msgid ""
"Zero counts are replaced before each distribution is normalized, and reported counts are no "
"longer modified."
msgstr "先替换零计数，再分别对各分布归一化；结果中的计数不再被修改。"

msgid ""
"Spark, SQL, AHP, feature selection, model wrappers, weighted and supervised binning and "
"scorecards. They remain in the repository history."
msgstr "Spark、SQL、AHP、特征选择、模型封装、加权与监督分箱以及评分卡。这些代码仍保留在仓库历史中。"

